      "exp_en": "GB-35 and GB-38 are at different levels. ST-40 (feng long) and ST-39 are at different levels. BL-58 and GB-37 are at different levels. GB-35 is 7 cun superior to the prominence of the lateral malleolus while GB-38 is 4 cun superior to the prominence. The sets of points which are on the same general level are: ST-40 and ST-38 are on the same level. BL-58 and GB-36 are on the same level. BL-58 and GB-36 are on the same level. ST-40 is midway between the tibiofemoral joint and lateral malleolus, two finger widths lateral to the anterior crest of the tibia, and one finger width lateral to ST-38. ST-38 is midway between the tibiofemoral joint and lateral malleolus, one finger width lateral to the anterior crest of the tibia. GB-39 is above the ankle joint, 3 cun superior to the prominence of the lateral malleolus, between the posterior border of the fibula and the tendons peroneus longus and brevis. BL-59 is on the lower leg, 3 cun directly above BL-60. BL-58 is on the lower leg, 7 cun directly above BL-60. GB-36 is on the lateral aspect of the leg, 7 cun superior to the prominence of the lateral malleolus. ST-40 is a luo-connecting point. ST-40 transforms phlegm and dampness, benefits the chest, clears Lung phlegm, alleviates coughing and wheezing, clears Heart phlegm, calms the spirit, activates the channel and stops pain. ST-38 expels wind, stops pain, and benefits the shoulder. GB-39 is the meeting point for marrow. GB-39 benefits the sinews and bones, benefits the neck, dispels wind-damp, clears Gallbladder fire, and activates the channel and stops pain. BL-59 is the xi-cleft point of the Yang Motility vessel. BL-59 benefits the lumbar area and legs, activates the channel and stops pain. BL-58 is the luo-connecting point. BL-58 harmonises the upper and lower, expels wind from taiyang channel, treats hemorrhoids, activates the channel and stops pain. GB-36 is a xi-cleft point. GB-36 activates the channel. And stops pain, clears heat and detoxifies poison. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, pages 163, 165, 317, 453, 455, 457, 606, 607",
