      ],
      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Stomach Deficient and Cold. This pattern is often associated with Spleen Yang Xu pattern. The expected pulse in this pattern is a Deep-Slow-Weak pulse, particularly on the right middle position the Deep pulse indicates an internal condition. The Weak pulse indicates deficiency. The Slow pulse indicates Cold. From the point of view of the Eight Principles, the pulse indicates an Internal, Deficient, and Cold pattern. The expected tongue is pale and wet. The pale tongue results from the weak yang qi failing to bring blood to the tongue. The tongue wetness is due to Spleen Yang Xu failing to transform Body Fluids resulting in an accumulation. Epigastric discomfort which gets better after eating and cold limbs are sufficient to make the diagnosis of Stomach Deficient and Cold. The treatment principle is Tonify and Warm Stomach and Spleen Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 657; 2005 Edition, page 620; 1989 Edition, page 268",
      "exp_hant": "此為胃虛寒證的診斷，此證型常與脾陽虛並見。此證預期脈象為沉遲弱脈，尤以右關脈為明顯：沉脈主裡證；弱脈主虛證；遲脈主寒證。從八綱角度而言，此脈象提示裡、虛、寒證。預期舌象為舌淡而濕潤。舌淡是因陽氣虛弱，無法將血液帶至舌面所致；舌濕潤則因脾陽虛不能運化水液而致水濕停聚。胃脘不適於進食後緩解及四肢冰冷，已足以診斷為胃虛寒證。治療原則為溫補脾胃之氣。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 657; 2005 Edition, page 620; 1989 Edition, page 268"
