          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Measles can have fever up to 105 degrees F while chickenpox has a milder fever up to 102 degrees",
          "hant": "麻疹發燒可高達華氏105度，而水痘的發燒則較輕微，約至華氏102度",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Measles can generally have a much higher fever than chickenpox. Measles is contagious from 4 days before to 4 days after the rash while chickenpox is contagious 1-2 days before rash until the lesions crust over. Only chickenpox has red spots that are fluid filled. Both measles and chickenpox have vaccines. Measles can generally have a much higher fever than chickenpox. Both measles (paramyxo virus) and chickenpox (varicella zoster virus) are viral diseases. Both can be prevented by vaccines. Both are common in children. Both the measle and chickenpox virus are airborne and spread through respiration (coughing, sneezing) or contact with fluids from the infected person. Both have rashes and fever. The incubation period for varicella (chickenpox) is 14 to 16 days after exposure to a varicella or a herpes zoster rash, with a range of 10 to 21 days. A mild prodrome of fever and malaise may occur 1 to 2 days before rash onset, particularly in adults. In children, the rash is often the first sign of disease. In healthy children, chickenpox is generally mild, with an itchy rash, malaise, and temperature up to 102 degree F for 2 to 3 days. A person with varicella is contagious from 1-2 days before rash onset until the lesions have crusted. It takes from 10-21 days after exposure to the virus for someone to develop varicella. Measles is an acute viral respiratory illness. It is characterized by a prodrome of fever (as high as 105 degrees F) and malaise, cough, coryza, and conjunctivitis (the three \"Cs\"). Koplik spots are followed by a maculopapular rash. The rash usually appears about 14 days after a person is exposed. The rash spreads from the head to the trunk to the lower extremities. Patients are considered to be contagious from 4 days before to 4 days after the rash appears. Patients with weak immune systems often do not develop the rash. Measles can create complications in patients with a compromised immune system or can cause birth defects in pregnancy. The chickenpox virus can remain dormant in the body and can reactivate later, manifesting as shingles. The CDC recommends two doses of chickenpox vaccine for children, adolescents, and adults. Children should receive two doses of the vaccine, the first dose at 12 through 15 months old and a second dose at four through six years old. The MMR vaccine protects against measles, mumps, and rubella (German measles). The CDC recommends MMR starting with the first dose at 12 through 15 months of age, and the second dose at four through six years of age. There is also the MMRV vaccine where the V refers to the vacirella virus which cause chickenpox. www.cdc.gov",
      "exp_hant": "麻疹的發燒程度通常遠高於水痘。麻疹的傳染期為出疹前4天至出疹後4天，而水痘的傳染期則為出疹前1-2天至皮疹結痂為止。只有水痘的紅疹會有液體填充。麻疹與水痘皆有疫苗可預防。麻疹的發燒程度通常遠高於水痘。麻疹（副黏液病毒）與水痘（水痘帶狀疱疹病毒）皆為病毒性疾病，兩者皆可透過疫苗預防，且皆常見於兒童。麻疹病毒與水痘病毒皆經空氣傳播，透過呼吸道飛沫（咳嗽、打噴嚏）或接觸感染者體液傳染。兩者皆有皮疹與發燒。水痘的潛伏期為暴露於水痘或帶狀疱疹皮疹後14至16天，範圍為10至21天。發疹前1至2天可能出現輕微前驅症狀，如發燒及倦怠感，成人尤為明顯。兒童患者則常以皮疹為疾病的首發徵象。健康兒童罹患水痘通常病情輕微，伴搔癢性皮疹、倦怠感，體溫可達華氏102度，持續2至3天。水痘病患自出疹前1-2天至皮疹結痂為止具傳染性。暴露於病毒後10-21天內會發病。麻疹是一種急性病毒性呼吸道疾病，其特徵為前驅期發燒（可高達華氏105度）、倦怠感、咳嗽、鼻炎及結膜炎（即所謂「三C」）。柯氏斑出現後隨即出現斑丘疹。皮疹通常於暴露後約14天出現，並由頭部擴散至軀幹再至下肢。患者自出疹前4天至出疹後4天皆具傳染性。免疫力較弱的患者常不會出現典型皮疹。麻疹可能對免疫力低下的患者造成併發症，或於孕期造成胎兒缺陷。水痘病毒可潛伏於體內，日後重新活化即表現為帶狀疱疹。CDC建議兒童、青少年及成人皆應接種兩劑水痘疫苗，兒童應於12至15個月大接種第一劑，並於4至6歲接種第二劑。MMR疫苗可預防麻疹、腮腺炎及德國麻疹（風疹）。CDC建議MMR疫苗第一劑於12至15個月大接種，第二劑於4至6歲接種。另有MMRV疫苗，其中V即指造成水痘的水痘帶狀疱疹病毒。www.cdc.gov"
    },
