      "exp_en": "The pathology of Bell's Palsy is an acute invasion of wind-cold in the yang ming and shao yang channels that lead to malnutrition of the facial muscles. The foot and hand yang ming channels and the foot and hand shao yang channels supply the facial area. The yang ming and shao yang muscle meridians reach the forehead, cheek, and front of the ear. LI-4 is distal point that expels external pathogenic wind-cold in the face. GB-12 eliminates wind, benefits the head, and treats the headache. The local points GB-14, BL-2, TB-23, and extra point yu yao treat the inability to raise the forehead-eyebrow and close the eye. ST-3 and ST-4 are then added to the prescription to treat the inability to show the teeth. The other added points incompletely address that symptom. DU-26 is more for deviation of the philtrum, LI-20 for difficulty sniffling, and GB-2 is more tinnitus and deafness. CAM, 3rd Edition, page 457; CAM, 4th Edition, page 555",
      "exp_hant": "貝爾氏麻痺的病機為風寒邪氣急性侵犯陽明經與少陽經，導致顏面肌肉失於濡養。手足陽明經與手足少陽經皆循行至顏面部位，陽明與少陽經筋皆到達額部、頰部及耳前。合谷為遠端取穴，可袪除侵犯顏面的外感風寒。完骨能袪風、利頭部，治療頭痛。局部取穴陽白、攢竹、絲竹空及經外奇穴魚腰，治療無法上抬額眉及閉眼的症狀。之後於處方中加入巨髎與地倉，以治療無法露齒的症狀。其餘選項的加穴組合則無法完整對應此症狀：人中較適用於人中溝歪斜，迎香較適用於嗅覺失靈，聽會則較適用於耳鳴耳聾。CAM, 3rd Edition, page 457; CAM, 4th Edition, page 555"
