      "exp_en": "The Chief herbs are zhi fu zi and gan jiang. The Deputy herbs are fu ling and bai zhu. The Assistant herbs are mu gua, hou po, mu xiang, da fu pi, and cao guo. The Envoy herbs are zhi gan cao, sheng jiang, and da zao. This formula warms the yang, strengthens the Spleen, moves the qi, and promotes urination. This formula treats yin jaundice which arises from Spleen and Kidney yang xu. In yin jaundice the yang needs to be warmed and the Spleen needs to be tonified to promote water metabolism so pathogenic water can be eliminated. The chief herbs zhi fu zi and gan jiang warm. The chief herb gan jiang promotes Spleen yang movement to strengthen its water transportive function. gan jiang is hot but not toxic and focuses on the middle jiao to treat almost every type of xu cold patterns there. zhi fu zi is acrid and very hot and moves through the body to unblock and promote yang qi movement in all the twelve channels. zhi fu zi also tonifies the the gate of fire. It is effective in removing stasis due to accumulation of yin water. The deputy herbs fu ling and bai zhu tonify the Spleen and resolve dampness through encouraging urination. The assistant herb mu gua revives the Spleen, transforms dampness, and promotes urination. The other assistant herbs hou po, mu xiang, da fu pi, and cao guo direct qi down to guide out stagnation, transform dampness, and circulate body fluids. The envoy herbs zhi gan cao, sheng jiang, and da zao regulate-harmonize the other herbs and also benefit the Spleen and middle jiao. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 721",
      "exp_hant": "君藥為製附子與乾薑。臣藥為茯苓與白朮。佐藥為木瓜、厚朴、木香、大腹皮及草果。使藥為炙甘草、生薑及大棗。本方能溫陽、健脾、行氣、利水，主治因脾腎陽虛所致的陰黃。陰黃須溫陽並健脾，以促進水液代謝，使病理性水濕得以排除。君藥製附子與乾薑性溫，其中乾薑能促進脾陽運行以增強其運化水液之功能，乾薑性熱而不燥，專主中焦，幾乎可治療該處各種虛寒證。製附子辛烈大熱，能通行全身，疏通並促進十二經脈之陽氣運行，並能溫補命門之火，有效袪除因陰水積聚所致之瘀滯。臣藥茯苓與白朮能健脾，並藉利尿以化濕。佐藥木瓜能醒脾、化濕、利尿。其餘佐藥厚朴、木香、大腹皮及草果能引氣下行、導滯外出、化濕並運行津液。使藥炙甘草、生薑及大棗能調和諸藥，亦能補益脾臟與中焦。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 721"
