      "exp_en": "In an externally contracted disorder involving a pathogen, the distribution and location of the tongue coating reflects the movement of the pathogenic factor. The front part of the tongue connects with the upper jiao, the center to the middle jiao, and the root to the lower jiao. In the initial stage of an external disorder the coating will be more concentrated at either the front of the tongue or on the sides of the tongue. As the pathogen moves to the interior, the coating will most likely turn yellow and spread from the front to the center or from the sides to the center. The initial coating on the front of the tongue will remain and the coating at the center will become thicker. In an external disorder, the spreading of the tongue coating can occur over a few hours or within a day. In an internal disorder, the distribution of the tongue coating whether partial or complete is in relation to the organ tongue map. In an internal disorder, a coating on the left side, reflects a Liver disorder, on the center it reflects Stomach disorder, and on the root it can reflect a disorder with Bladder, Intestines, or Womb, etc. Tongue Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1995, page 99-100",
