        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Medical negligence does not involve intent. Medical negligence applies when a health care provider makes a \"mistake\" in treating patient and that mistake results in harm to the patient. While the act or omission is definitely negligence, it does not rise to the point of medical malpractice because the health care provider did not commit the action either with the intent to cause harm or the knowledge that the patient might suffer harm. For example, medical negligence is when a nurse accidentally leaves a sponge inside a surgical wound. She did not intend to cause harm. Medical malpractice is the breach of the duty of care by a medical provider. It has an element of \"intent\" that medical negligence does not have. The health care provider knew that a particular treatment or lab test should be done but failed to do so knowing that the failure to follow could harm the patient. It was not intentional in the sense of wanting to harm the patient but it was intentional because the doctor knew that not doing a treatment or lab test could harm the patient. For example, a doctor decides to forego an expensive diagnostic test because the patient's insurance will not pay for test and because the doctor could incur a financial burden.",
      "exp_hant": "醫療過失並不涉及故意的意圖。當醫療人員在治療病人時發生「失誤」並因此對病人造成傷害時，即屬醫療過失。雖然該作為或不作為確實構成過失，但由於醫療人員並非蓄意造成傷害，也不知道該行為可能使病人受害，因此尚未達到醫療不當行為的程度。舉例來說，護理師不慎將海綿遺留在手術傷口內即屬醫療過失，她並無意造成傷害。醫療不當行為則是醫療人員違反注意義務的行為，具有醫療過失所沒有的「故意」要素。醫療人員明知應進行某項治療或檢驗，卻在知道不這麼做可能傷害病人的情況下未予執行。這並非蓄意想要傷害病人，而是因為醫師明知不進行治療或檢驗可能造成傷害卻仍執意如此，因此帶有故意的性質。舉例來說，醫師因為病人的保險不給付某項昂貴的診斷檢驗，且擔心自己因此承受經濟負擔，而決定放棄該檢驗。"
