      "exp_en": "The original prescription focused mainly on Kidney deficiency (late period, frequent urination, back pain, dizziness, tinnitus, weak pulse, pale tongue) which guided the selection of KI-3 and BL-23 tonify the Kidneys, SP-6 tonify the Kidneys and regulate menstruation, and ST-36 tonifies qi and yang. Just seeing this case strictly from a deficient Kidney condition is incomplete. There are symptoms which also point to Liver Blood deficiency (late and scanty periods, dull-pale complexion, hair loss, blurred vision, splitting nails, pale tongue and choppy pulse). Additionally, there were symptoms pointing to mild Qi Stasis (abdominal distention, period starting hesitantly). BL-20 and BL-23 tonify the Kidneys and nourish Blood. KI-3 tonifies the Kidneys. ST-36 and SP-6 tonify Qi and Blood. REN-4 nourishes Blood, strengthen the Kidneys, and regulates the Uterus. BL-17 with moxa tonifies the Blood. LR-3 regulates menstruation and spreads Liver qi. The Rx with SP-8 focuses on moving Qi and Blood and fails to focus on tonifying the Blood. The Rx with DU-4 mostly focuses on tonifying the Kidneys. Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1998, page 180, 182, 191",
