    {
      "number": 99,
      "question_en": "Using the SOAP format of charting, what does the \"S\" refer to?",
      "question_hant": "使用SOAP病歷記錄格式時，「S」指的是什麼？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Patient description of complaint, its history, progression, response to previous treatments",
          "hant": "病人對主訴的描述，包括病史、病程進展及對先前治療的反應",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Findings from pulse, tongue, and palpation",
          "hant": "脈診、舌診及觸診所得之發現",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Problems listed by priority, potential diagnoses",
          "hant": "依優先順序列出的問題及可能診斷",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Therapeutic interventions",
          "hant": "治療介入措施",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A SOAP note is information about the patient. It is written or presented in a specific order, which includes certain components. SOAP notes are used for admission notes, medical histories, and used in a patient's chart. Many hospitals use electronic medical records which often use the SOAP note format as a template. \"S\" refers to subjective. This refers to subjective observations that are verbally expressed by the patient, such as information about symptoms. It is considered subjective because there is not a way to measure the information. \"O\" refers to objective. It involves objective observations, which means factors you can measure, see, hear, feel or smell. This is the section where you should include vital signs, such as pulse, respiration and temperature. \"A\" refers to assessment or potential diagnoses. An assessment is the diagnosis or condition the patient has. There may be one clear diagnosis. In other cases, a patient may have several things wrong. There may also be other times where a definitive diagnosis is not yet made, and more than one possible diagnosis is included in the assessment. \"P\" refers to plan. These are the steps taken to treat the patient such as acupuncture, herbs, massage, etc. It may also list long-term treatment plans and recommended changes to lifestyle as well as short and long term goals for the patient. The provider can also list treatment principle goals that need to be met such as increasing qi and blood. The SOAP note (an acronym for subjective, objective, assessment, and plan) is a method of documentation employed by health care providers to write out notes in the chart of a patient, along with other common formats, such as the admission note. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 79-80",
      "exp_hant": "SOAP病歷是關於病人的資訊，以特定順序及固定格式書寫或呈現，包含若干構成要素。SOAP病歷常用於入院記錄、病史記錄，以及病人病歷檔案中。許多醫院使用電子病歷系統，也常以SOAP格式作為範本。「S」代表主觀（Subjective），指病人以口頭方式表達的主觀觀察，例如症狀方面的資訊。之所以稱為主觀，是因為這類資訊無法客觀測量。「O」代表客觀（Objective），指可測量、看見、聽見、觸摸或聞到的客觀觀察結果，此部分應包含生命徵象，如脈搏、呼吸及體溫。「A」代表評估（Assessment）或可能診斷，即病人所患的診斷或病況。有時只有一項明確診斷；有時病人可能同時有多項問題；也有些情況尚未有確定診斷，評估中會列出一項以上的可能診斷。「P」代表計畫（Plan），即為治療病人所採取的步驟，例如針灸、中藥、按摩等，亦可能包括長期治療計畫、生活型態調整建議，以及病人的短期與長期目標。醫療人員亦可在此列出需達成的治療原則目標，例如補益氣血。SOAP病歷（Subjective、Objective、Assessment、Plan四字首字母縮寫）是醫療人員用於在病人病歷中撰寫記錄的一種文件方式，與其他常見格式（如入院記錄）並列使用。Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 79-80"
    },
