        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "In a first-degree burn there is no blister formation. A blister is the result of a second-degree burn. The main concern with second-degree burn is infection. If it is a first degree burn, the current practice is to run cool water over the burn (never ice), and then apply sterile gauze. If it is not possible to run water over the burn, then just use an over-the-counter burn cream followed by the application of sterile gauze. The same advice applies to blister caused by moxa treatment. Blister formation after cupping is an indication of excess treatment duration and excess suction strength. Blisters that contain blood (hemorrhagic bullae) are less common but are more likely in patients on anticoagulant drugs and supplements that can act as blood thinners. They can take two weeks to heal and can form crusting scabs. For blisters, patients should be instructed on using an antibiotic topical ointment, and keeping the area clean and covered, if necessary, until healed as infection is a concern. CNT Manual, 7th Edition, page 102",
      "exp_hant": "一度燒傷不會形成水泡，水泡是二度燒傷的結果。二度燒傷最主要的顧慮是感染。若為一度燒傷，目前的做法是以涼水沖洗燒傷處（絕不可用冰敷），接著覆蓋無菌紗布。若無法以水沖洗，則可先塗抹市售燒燙傷藥膏，再覆蓋無菌紗布。艾灸造成的水泡也適用相同的處理方式。拔罐後出現水泡，表示治療時間過長或吸力過強。含血水泡（出血性水泡）較為少見，但在服用抗凝血藥物或可能有抗凝血作用的補充品的病人身上較容易出現，這類水泡可能需要兩週才能癒合，並可能形成結痂。對於水泡，應指導病人使用外用抗生素藥膏，並保持該部位清潔及必要時加以覆蓋，直至癒合為止，因為感染是需要留意的問題。CNT Manual, 7th Edition, page 102"
