          "en": "clinical documents",
          "hant": "臨床文件",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Generally in the US, the information contained in the medical record belongs to the patient while the physical form the data takes belongs to the entity responsible for maintaining the record. HIPAA regulations gives patients the right to access and change their own medical records but it does not provide guidance as to who owns the records. Twenty-eight states have no laws that define medical record ownership. Twenty-one states have laws stating that the providers are the owners of the records. Only one state (New Hampshire), has a law ascribing ownership of medical records to the patient. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 77",
      "exp_hant": "一般而言，在美國，病歷中所含的資訊屬於病人所有，但記錄資料所依附的實體形式則屬於負責保管該記錄之機構所有。HIPAA法規賦予病人存取及變更自身病歷的權利，但並未就病歷所有權歸屬提供明確規範。有28個州並無明確界定病歷所有權歸屬的法律。有21個州的法律規定醫療提供者為病歷之所有人。僅有一個州（新罕布夏州）立法規定病歷所有權歸屬於病人。Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 77"
    },
