      "exp_en": "Legally, if a medical procedure is not documented it was not done. Lack of documentation may lead to procedures being done twice. Failure to document could place the patient at risk. It is important to document all patient information, evaluation findings, and interventions. This promotes continuity of care. It also helps substantiate care from a legal standpoint. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 77",
      "exp_hant": "從法律角度而言，若某項醫療處置未有記錄，即視同未曾執行。缺乏記錄可能導致處置被重複執行。未記錄可能使病人陷於風險之中。記錄所有病人資訊、評估結果及介入措施相當重要，此舉有助於照護的延續性，也有助於從法律角度佐證所提供的照護。Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 77"
