        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "deng xin cao (medulla junci), tong cao (medulla tetrapanacis), fu ling (sclerotium poria cocos)",
          "hant": "燈心草、通草、茯苓",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Deng xin cao, tong cao, and bai mao gen all clear heat indicated by dark urine. Xuan shen clears heat and cools Blood. It may be used to modify the formula for severe Yin deficiency with injured fluids and a dry throat. Fu ling is not added as its primary action is to treat Dampness. Its diuretic effect could concentrate the body’s fluids, potentially worsening symptoms like dark urine (a sign of heat and fluid deficiency) by further reducing available fluids to dilute the urine. Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Scheid, Bensky, Ellis, and Barolet, page 470; Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, 3rd Edition, Bensky, Clavey, and Stoger, pages 286, 288, and 579",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。燈心草、通草及白茅根皆能清熱，適用於小便色深之症狀。玄參能清熱涼血，可用於因陰虛嚴重、津液受損且咽喉乾燥之病例做加減。茯苓則不加入此方，因其主要功能為治療濕證。其利水作用可能使體液更為濃縮，反而可能加重小便色深（此為熱盛及津液不足之徵象）等症狀，因其會進一步減少可稀釋尿液的體液量。Formulas and Strategies, 2nd Edition, Scheid, Bensky, Ellis, and Barolet, page 470; Chinese Herbal Medicine Materia Medica, 3rd Edition, Bensky, Clavey, and Stoger, pages 286, 288, and 579"
    },
