      "exp_en": "Under HIPAA a patient has the right to access the medical information or on request provide a summary of the patient records or a copy of the records. If a copy of records is provided, a reasonable charge can be applied. The fees that can be charged to individuals exercising their right of access to their PHI apply only in cases where the individual is to receive a copy of the PHI, versus merely being provided the opportunity to view and inspect the PHI. A medical office may not charge an individual who, while inspecting their PHI, takes notes, uses a smart phone or other device to take pictures of the PHI, or uses other personal resources to capture the information. If the individual is making the copies of PHI using their own resources, the medical office may not charge a fee for those copies, as the copying is being done by the individual and not the entity. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "根據HIPAA規定，病人有權存取其醫療資訊，或依要求提供病歷摘要或病歷副本。若提供病歷副本，可收取合理費用。可對行使PHI存取權之個人收取費用之情形，僅限於個人將取得PHI副本之情況，若僅是提供查閱與檢視PHI之機會，則不適用收費。若個人在查閱其PHI時做筆記、使用智慧型手機或其他裝置拍攝PHI內容，或使用自身其他資源取得資訊，診所不得對此收費。若個人是以自身資源自行複製PHI，診所亦不得就此複製行為收費，因為複製工作是由個人自行完成，而非該機構所為。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
