      "exp_en": "In Japanese moxa treatment it is OK to treat a patient diagnosed with a \"hot\" condition. Moxa treatment has been used in various types of health conditions, whether those conditions are hot or cold. Though traditional TCM advises against the use of moxa on hot conditions, the use of moxa in non-emergency fevers has been confirmed by more current research in China such as applying moxa on DU-14 for fever. The text also lists: avoiding moxa on very hungry or very full patients, avoid moxa one hour before or after a very hot bath/sauna, avoid moxa on the face (risk of scarring). It is contraindicated to treat patients with very high fever, over an inflamed arthritic joint, and on the lower abdomen of a pregnant woman. Japanese Acupuncture, 1998, Birch and Ida, page 123, 136",
      "exp_hant": "在日式灸法中，可以對診斷為「熱」證的患者施灸。灸法已被運用於各種健康狀況，不論寒熱皆可施用。雖然傳統中醫主張熱證應避免使用灸法，但現代中國的研究已證實，在非急症發熱時施灸（例如於大椎穴施灸退熱）是可行的。文中亦列出：避免在患者過飢或過飽時施灸、避免在熱水浴或三溫暖前後一小時內施灸、避免在臉部施灸（有留疤風險）。禁忌症則包括高燒患者、發炎的關節炎關節，以及孕婦的下腹部。Japanese Acupuncture, 1998, Birch and Ida, page 123, 136"
