          "en": "marijuana dependence",
          "hant": "大麻成癮",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "barbiturate dependence",
          "hant": "巴比妥類藥物成癮",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Methadone is a narcotic drug used to treat chronic pain and opiate addiction. Unlike heroin and morphine, methadone is derived not from opium poppies but is synthesized in a lab. Methadone has similar analgesic properties like to opiates but lasts much longer, 24 hours for methadone vs 2-4 hours for opiates. Methadone binds to the same receptors as opiates and helps reduce many opiate withdrawal symptoms. The difference between the two is that methadone does not cause a euphoric high. Methadone can also block the euphoric effects of opiate drugs. This prevents the user from getting high in case of relapse. However, methadone does have drawbacks. Opiate addicts can barter their methadone for opiates. Addicts can also combine methadone with other drugs, such as alcohol. While methadone blocks the opiate high, the addict can still combine opiates and methadone which can result in death. tcmtests.com, February 2019",
      "exp_hant": "美沙冬是一種用於治療慢性疼痛與鴉片類藥物成癮的麻醉藥物。與海洛因及嗎啡不同，美沙冬並非萃取自罌粟，而是在實驗室中合成而成。美沙冬具有類似鴉片類藥物的鎮痛作用，但藥效持續時間更長，美沙冬可維持24小時，而鴉片類藥物僅維持2至4小時。美沙冬與鴉片類藥物結合相同的受體，有助於減輕許多鴉片戒斷症狀。兩者的差異在於美沙冬不會產生欣快感。美沙冬也能阻斷鴉片類藥物所帶來的欣快效果，防止使用者在復發時仍能感受到嗨的感覺。然而，美沙冬仍有其缺點。鴉片成癮者可能會以美沙冬交換鴉片類藥物。成癮者也可能將美沙冬與其他藥物（如酒精）合併使用。雖然美沙冬能阻斷鴉片類藥物的欣快作用，成癮者仍可能同時使用鴉片類藥物與美沙冬，進而導致死亡。tcmtests.com, February 2019"
    },
    {
      "number": 145,
      "question_en": "A 36 year-old female patient had an acute attack of viral pericarditis one year ago. With the attack, she had chest pain, was very weak, had an elevated temperature, and was sweating. Since then, she has been feeling very fatigued, sometimes dizzy, and forgetful. Her appetite was poor and had a frequent impulse of wanting to lie down. Sometimes, her mouth was very dry, she was often constipated with dry stools, and she had epigastric burning. Her pulse was rapid-slippery and the tongue was red with a sticky-yellow coating. The tongue had a midline crack. She was treated ten times from a group of points that included REN-12 (zhong wan), ST-36 (zu san li), SP-3 (tai bai), SP-6 (san yin jiao), REN-6 (qi hai), REN-4 (guan yuan), BL-17 (ge shu). On her follow up visit, she reports there has been little improvement in her symptoms and there was no change in the tongue or pulse. What treatment would you now select?",
      "question_hant": "一名36歲女性患者一年前曾急性發作病毒性心包炎。發作時，她出現胸痛、極度虛弱、體溫升高並伴有出汗。此後，她持續感到非常疲倦，偶爾頭暈、健忘。食慾不佳，並常有想躺下的衝動。有時口乾非常明顯，經常便秘且大便乾燥，並有胃脘灼熱感。脈象為滑數，舌紅苔黃膩，舌中線有裂紋。她曾接受十次治療，取穴包括中脘（REN-12）、足三里（ST-36）、太白（SP-3）、三陰交（SP-6）、氣海（REN-6）、關元（REN-4）、膈俞（BL-17）。複診時，她表示症狀改善甚微，舌脈亦無變化。此時您會選擇何種治療？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
