        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "ST-40 (feng long), BL-20 (pi shu), BL-21 (wei shu), REN-12 (zhong wan), ST-36 (zu san li)",
          "hant": "豐隆、脾俞、胃俞、中脘、足三里",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This case involves a mixture of deficiency and excess. There are deficient qi and blood symptoms (tiredness, wanting to lie down, poor appetite, poor memory) as well as excess phlegm (slippery pulse, sticky tongue coating) and excess heat (dry mouth, constipation, dry stool, rapid pulse, burning epigastrium). The original prescription focused on tonifying qi and blood but it did not help. This is a case where the excess pattern needs to be treated first. Though more true with herbal treatment, tonifying qi and blood when there is phlegm-heat will tend to worsen the phlegm and heat as tonifying herbs are sticky and warm in nature. The excess symptoms and signs (midline tongue crack) point to Stomach heat with phlegm. REN-12 and ST-40 transform phlegm, ST-44 and LI-4 clear stomach heat, and LI-11 clears heat in general. Once the phlegm is transformed (less tongue coating) and heat is cleared (less rapid pulse, less red tongue) it would then be appropriate to focus on tonification. The Rx with HT-8 focuses on heart phlegm-heat. The Rx with BL-21 focuses on transforming phlegm by strengthening the Spleen and Stomach and does not focus on clearing heat. The Rx with LR-2 focuses on Liver fire with phlegm. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 634; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 607, 662",
      "exp_hant": "此病例屬虛實夾雜。既有氣血虧虛的症狀（疲倦、想躺下、食慾不佳、健忘），又有痰濁偏盛（脈滑、舌苔黏膩）與熱邪偏盛（口乾、便秘、大便乾燥、脈數、胃脘灼熱）。原本的處方著重於補益氣血，但未見成效。此為應先治其標（實證）的病例。雖然此原則在中藥治療中更為明顯，但在有痰熱時若一味補益氣血，補益藥性黏膩溫燥，反易助長痰熱。實證症狀與體徵（舌中線裂紋）指向胃熱夾痰。中脘（REN-12）與豐隆（ST-40）化痰，內庭（ST-44）與合谷（LI-4）清胃熱，曲池（LI-11）則能清一般熱邪。待痰化（苔減）、熱清（脈數減緩、舌紅減退）之後，方適合轉為補益為主。選項B取少府（HT-8）著重於心經痰熱；選項D取胃俞（BL-21）著重於健脾胃以化痰，未著重清熱；選項A取行間（LR-2）著重於肝火夾痰。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 634; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 607, 662"
