      "exp_en": "The 8-Principles diagnosis is Internal with channel involvement, Hot, Excess. The etiology is emotional change. According to vital substances, the diagnosis is Stagnant Qi Transforming into Heat. According to channel theory, the diagnosis is Heat Constraint in Shao Yang Channels. The organ pattern is Gall Bladder Dysfunction in Facilitating Free-Flow of Qi. The treatment principle is to Regulate Gall Bladder Qi, Remove Heat, and Remove Channel Obstruction to Alleviate Pain. In the first set of points, tai yang is selected as a local point to regulate the area. GB-20 removes shao yang channel obstruction and regulates the head. ST-36 and SP-6 are selected to strengthen the middle burner which is showing the tendency of wood attacking earth. SP-6 is also selected to nourish and protect yin from the heat. The combination of LI-4 and KI-7 were selected to treat the abnormal sweating, nourishing yin, and clearing heat. These points did not adequately address removing the heat obstruction from the Gall Bladder as evidenced by the patient still feeling hot and the headache not being alleviated. GB-8 soothes Liver qi, removes obstructions from the Liver and Gall Bladder channels, and clears Heat from both the organ and channel. TB-7, the accumulation point, is selected to remove obstructions in the channel and is an important point for treating shao yang headaches. GB-34, the lower he-sea point, clears heat and removes stagnation, strengthens Liver function and can be selected when wood attacks earth. GB-8, TB-7, and GB-34 are all shao yang points located in the head, arm, and leg. They have the function of removing heat that results from stagnant qi and they also regulate the qi of the channel. The other prescriptions with LR-2 and LR-3 treat more the Liver organ and not the Gall Bladder channel obstruction. As there are no symptom of heat in the blood, there is no need to bleed TB-1. In terms of western medicine, the vital signs (BP, pulse rate, respirations) are normal. Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 57-61",
      "exp_hant": "八綱辨證為裡證兼經絡病變、熱證、實證。病因為情志所傷。就氣血津液辨證而言，診斷為氣鬱化熱。就經絡辨證而言，診斷為少陽經熱鬱。臟腑辨證為膽失疏泄。治療原則為疏調膽氣、清熱、通經止痛。第一組處方中，太陽穴為局部取穴以調理該部位。風池（GB-20）疏通少陽經氣、調理頭部。足三里（ST-36）與三陰交（SP-6）用以健運中焦，因病情有木乘土之勢。三陰交同時滋陰以防熱邪傷陰。合谷（LI-4）配復溜（KI-7）用以治療異常出汗、滋陰清熱。然而這些穴位未能充分清除膽經的熱鬱，故患者仍感發熱且頭痛未見改善。率谷（GB-8）疏肝理氣，通利肝膽經絡阻滯，並清瀉臟腑與經絡之熱。會宗（TB-7），為郄穴，能通經止痛，是治療少陽頭痛的重要穴位。陽陵泉（GB-34）為下合穴，能清熱化瘀、強肝，適用於木乘土之證。率谷、會宗、陽陵泉皆為少陽經穴，分別位於頭、臂、腿部，具有清除氣鬱化熱與調理經氣的作用。選項中取行間、太衝者，較著重於肝臟本身而非膽經之經絡阻滯。由於並無血分熱象，故無需點刺放血關衝。就西醫角度而言，生命徵象（血壓、脈搏、呼吸）皆屬正常。Acupuncture Patterns and Practice, Eastland Press, 1993, Xuemai and Jingyi, Pages 57-61"
