      "exp_en": "This is the most complete answer. Walk in clinics are not highly associated with hepatitis infections. Many patients in public health care settings (HIV clinics, TB clinics, drug addiction clinics) have a history of some type of hepatitis. These patients may not know which type they have and may not even know that they are hepatitis carriers. Chronic carriers of hepatitis can infect others through bodily fluids and excretions. There are two types of chronic carriers: 1) a chronic-persistent carrier does not have symptoms but can still infect others. 2) a chronic-active carrier has progressive symptoms and the disease continues to damage the liver. Chronic-active carriers can still transmit the virus to others. Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 142",
      "exp_hant": "這是最完整的答案。無預約門診與肝炎感染的關聯性並不高。許多在公共醫療機構（愛滋病診所、肺結核診所、戒毒診所）就診的病患曾有某種肝炎病史。這些病患可能不清楚自己感染的肝炎類型，甚至不知道自己是肝炎帶原者。慢性肝炎帶原者可透過體液與排泄物傳染他人。慢性帶原者分為兩類：1）慢性持續型帶原者無症狀，但仍可傳染他人；2）慢性活動型帶原者症狀持續進展，疾病持續損害肝臟，且仍可將病毒傳染給他人。Clean Needle Technique, 7th Edition, page 142"
