        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "all high-risk individuals are infectious",
          "hant": "所有高風險族群皆具有傳染性",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Universal precautions is an approach to infection control to treat all human blood and certain human body fluids as if they were known to be infectious for HIV, HBV and other bloodborne pathogens. The Bloodborne Pathogen Standard require employees to observe Universal Precautions to prevent contact with blood or other potentially infectious materials (OPIM). Under circumstances in which differentiation between body fluid types is difficult or impossible, all body fluids shall be considered potentially infectious materials. Universal precautions required that you treat all blood and other potentially infectious materials with appropriate precautions such as: use gloves, masks, and gowns if blood or OPIM exposure is anticipated and use work practice controls to limit exposure. Personal protective equipment (PPE), is equipment worn to minimize exposure to hazards that cause serious workplace injuries and illnesses. These injuries and illnesses may result from contact with chemical, radiological, physical, electrical, mechanical, or other workplace hazards. Personal protective equipment may include items such as gloves, safety glasses and shoes, earplugs or muffs, hard hats, respirators, or coveralls, vests and full body suits. Employers are also required to train each worker required to use personal protective equipment to know: 1) when it is necessary, 2) what kind is necessary, 3) how to properly put it on, adjust, wear and take it off, 4) the limitations of the equipment, 5) proper care, maintenance, useful life, and disposal of the equipment. Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 60",
      "exp_hant": "標準防護措施是一種感染控制方法，將所有人類血液及某些體液視為可能帶有HIV、HBV及其他血液傳播病原體而加以防護。血液傳播病原體標準要求員工遵守標準防護措施，以避免接觸血液或其他潛在感染性物質（OPIM）。在難以區分或無法區分體液種類的情況下，所有體液均應視為具有潛在感染性。標準防護措施要求對所有血液及其他潛在感染性物質採取適當防護措施，例如：在預期會接觸血液或OPIM時佩戴手套、口罩及隔離衣，並採取工作規範以降低暴露風險。個人防護裝備（PPE）是用以降低導致嚴重職業傷害與疾病之危害暴露的裝備，這些傷害與疾病可能源自化學性、放射性、物理性、電性、機械性或其他職場危害。個人防護裝備可包括手套、護目鏡、鞋具、耳塞或耳罩、安全帽、呼吸防護具，或連身防護服等。雇主亦須訓練每位需使用個人防護裝備的員工了解：1）何時需要使用、2）需使用何種裝備、3）如何正確穿戴、調整、配戴及脫除、4）裝備的限制、5）裝備的妥善保養、維護、使用年限與丟棄方式。Acupuncture Risk Management, CMS Press, Kailin, 1997 page 60"
