      "exp_en": "An adult is usually in charge of the use and disclosure of PHI for a minor. However, the rules also provide some flexibility that enables minors to protect their health status and personal confidentiality. For example, the minor controls PHI associated with HIV testing and mental health services without the need for adult consent. The parent or guardian does not control PHI when a court determines or other law authorizes someone other than the parent to make treatment decisions for a minor. The parent does not have rights to PHI when a parent/personal representative agrees to a confidential relationship between a health care provider and a minor. A medical practice must require that personal representatives (parents, guardians) of minors comply with the same privacy rules as individuals do. The personal representative (parent, guardian) can consent to an agreement of confidentiality between the minor and the medical practice. www.hhs.gov/hipaa/",
      "exp_hant": "通常由成人負責掌管未成年人受保護健康資訊（PHI）的使用與揭露。然而，相關規範也保留一定彈性，使未成年人得以保護自身的健康狀況與個人隱私。例如，未成年人可自行掌控與HIV檢測及心理健康服務相關的PHI，無需經成人同意。當法院裁定或其他法律授權由父母以外之人為未成年人做出治療決定時，父母則不擁有掌控PHI的權利。當父母／個人代理人同意醫療提供者與未成年人建立保密關係時，父母亦不具有相關權利。醫療機構必須要求未成年人的個人代理人（父母、監護人）遵守與成年個人相同的隱私規範。個人代理人（父母、監護人）可同意未成年人與醫療機構之間的保密協議。www.hhs.gov/hipaa/"
