      ],
      "exp_en": "In the book \"Discussion of Cold Damage\" the formula ling gui zhu gan tang (poria, cinnamom twig, atractylodes, and licorice decoction) is selected to treat injury due to cold that is caused by the improper use of purgatives. The wrong treatment results in chest fullness and hypochondriac fullness combined with vertigo. The book \"Essentials from the Gold Cabinet\" prescribes this formula for thin mucus in the epigastric area that is resolved via urination. In TCM the term \"thin mucus\" refers to both a set of symptoms and as a disease causing factor. This formula is indicated for the deficient type of thin mucus arising from Spleen and Kidney yang xu. The formula however does not focus on treating the deficiency in the Spleen and Kidneys zang organs but rather focuses on harmonizing the fluids and qi dynamic. Harmonizing implies regulating yin and yang, water and fire. This formula warms and transforms phlegm and thin mucus, strengthens the Spleen, and resolves dampness. The chief herb fu ling tonifies the Spleen and drains dampness. It transforms thin mucus by treating the root which is the transportation and transformation of fluids, the metabolism of fluids. The deputy herb gui zhi warms yang and strengthens the transforming power of qi. The combination of fu ling and gui zhi work together to increase the circulation of fluids while warming the qi flow. The assistant herb bai zhu tonfies the transforming and transporting functions of the Spleen to dry dampness. The herb bai zhu combined with gui zhi has a stronger effect on tonifying Spleen yang to transform excess dampness. The envoy herb is zhi gan cao augments the qi of the middle jiao. zhi gan cao can cause mild stagnation but fu ling counteracts that. CONTRAINDICATION: thin mucus arising from damp-heat patterns with yin xu and hyper yang. Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 735-737",
      "exp_hant": "在《傷寒論》中，苓桂朮甘湯（茯苓、桂枝、白朮、甘草湯）用以治療因誤用瀉下藥而導致的傷寒之證。誤治後導致胸滿與脅肋脹滿，並伴隨眩暈。《金匱要略》則以此方治療經由小便而解的心下痰飲。中醫所稱「痰飲」一詞，既指一組症狀，也指一種致病因素。此方適用於因脾腎陽虛所致的虛證痰飲。然而此方並非直接針對補益脾腎臟腑本身的虛損，而是著重於調和水液與氣機的運行。所謂調和，即調節陰陽、水火。此方能溫化痰飲、健脾、化濕。君藥茯苓補脾利濕，透過治療水液運化與輸布之本以化痰飲。臣藥桂枝溫陽，增強氣化之力。茯苓與桂枝相配，能在溫煦氣機的同時增強水液的運行。佐藥白朮增強脾之運化功能以燥濕，白朮配桂枝能更有效地溫補脾陽以化除過盛的濕邪。使藥炙甘草益中焦之氣，炙甘草雖可能引起輕微氣滯，但茯苓可制約此弊。禁忌：因濕熱夾陰虛陽亢所致的痰飲證不宜使用。Formulas and Strategies, Bensky, 2nd Edition, page 735-737"
