      "exp_en": "PATHOLOGY: When the qi of the Stomach muscle channel is disordered, there is pain or stiffness in the middle toe muscle, foot or ankle stiffness, twisted thigh muscles around ST-32, a swollen groin, abdominal muscle contractions up to the supraclavicular fossa (ST-12), hernia, deviation of the mouth, and an inability to close the eyes. PATHWAY: The Stomach muscle channel starts at the three middle toes, ascends to the tibia where it branches into two. One branch goes up the lateral part leg and knee and connects the front of the pelvis. From there it then goes to the lower ribs and curves back to connect to the spine. The other branch, the main branch, goes to ST-32 to converge in the genitals from where it ascends to the abdomen and chest to reach ST-12 from where it ascends to the neck, jaw, mouth, side of nose, cheek, and jaw. From the jaw there is one branch going to the front of the ear and the other branch going to the eye socket. The Stomach muscle channel connects with the muscle channels of the Gall Bladder, Large Intestine, and Bladder. Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 296, 316; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804; 2005 Edition, page 760",
