      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Kidney and Spleen Yang Deficiency. The expected pulse in this pattern is Deep-Weak. The weak nature of the pulse indicates a deficiency of a vital substance (qi, blood, yin, or yang), in this case a deficiency of yang. The pulse is Deep due to the weak yang failing to raise the pulse up. A Deep-Tight pulse can indicate either Excess-Internal-Cold if this pulse also has the quality of Fullness or a Deficient-Internal-Cold if it has the quality of Emptyness or Weakness. A Floating-Empty pulse tend to point to a Deficient Yin condition or an external-deficient disorder. The expected tongue is pale and wet. Deficient Kidney and Spleen Yang fail to transform fluids which results in an accumulation of dampness that is reflected as a wet tongue. The tongue is pale due to the failure of qi to bring blood to the tongue (qi moves blood) and due to Empty Cold. Low back pain, feeling cold, loose stools and a deep and weak pulse are sufficient to make the diagnosis of Kidney and Spleen Yang Deficiency. The treatment principle is Tonify and Warm Spleen and Kidney Yang. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 646; 2005 Edition, page 610; 1989 Edition, page 262",
      "exp_hant": "診斷為脾腎陽虛。此證預期脈象為沉弱。脈弱表示某種重要物質(氣、血、陰或陽)不足,此處為陽虛。脈沉是因陽虛無力升舉脈氣所致。沉緊脈可能表示裡實寒(若脈兼有力之特質)或裡虛寒(若脈兼虛弱之特質)。浮虛脈多提示陰虛或表虛證。預期舌象為舌淡而濕潤。脾腎陽虛無法運化水液,導致濕邪積聚,反映為舌苔濕潤。舌色淡則是因氣虛無法將血帶至舌面(氣行血),以及虛寒所致。下背痛、畏寒、大便溏薄及沉弱脈已足以診斷脾腎陽虛。治療原則為溫補脾腎陽氣。《中醫基礎學》,Maciocia,2015年,第646頁;2005年版,第610頁;1989年版,第262頁。"
    },
