      ],
      "exp_en": "REBELLIOUS QI: In the chong mai, rebellious qi can be associated with an internal urgency, vague anxiety and a restlessness at the emotional level or with physical symptoms such as chest tightness, fullness, distension, hernia, dizziness, nausea, constipation with an emotional background. A pattern of rebellious qi in the chong mai needs a combination of 3 or 4 symptoms at different levels or burners to arrive at this diagnosis. For example, in the legs (cold feet), lower abdomen (fullness, irregular/painful periods), epigastrium and hypogastrium (fullness, distension, pain, nausea), chest (breast distention, palpitations, chest tightness/oppression), throat-head (lump in throat, heat in face, dizziness). These symptoms follow the pathway of the chong mai. GYN BLOOD STASIS: The chong mai is the Sea of Blood which can root its pathology in GYN disorders. The three blood disorders affecting the chong mai are Blood xu (amenorrhea, scanty periods), Blood heat (heavy periods), and Blood stasis (painful period with clots). The chong mai is especially useful in treating GYN disorders due to Blood stasis as the ren mai is especially useful in treating GYN disorders due to qi stasis. FEMALE BREAST: The ren mai disperses in the chest and breast, making its qi having a deep influence on the breasts. The ren mai is responsible for producing breast milk after child birth, transforming menstrual blood into milk. The chong mai can help treat breast lumps, breast distension or pain, agalactia (breast milk does not come out) or insufficient lactation. THE HEART: The chong mai deeply influences the Heart as it has pathways that flow around the Heart. It can be used to treat heart rhythm problems and can treat arrhythmia. THE STOMACH: As the chong mai arises from ST-30 (upper point of Sea of Food) it is connected to the Stomach via this point. The chong mai can treat Stomach disorders especially those of the excess type (Stomach qi stasis, Rebellious Stomach qi, Stomach Blood stasis, Stomach Heat. QI CIRCULATION TO FEET: Because a branch of the chong mai descends to the top of the foot and the big toe, the vessel can treat circulatory disorders of the feet (coldness, numbness, tingling, purplish color changes). Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 915; 2005 Edition, page 862",
      "exp_hant": "氣逆:在衝脈中,氣逆可表現為內在急迫感、隱約的焦慮及情志上的躁動不安,或伴有胸悶、脹滿、疝氣、頭暈、噁心、便秘等軀體症狀,並帶有情志背景。診斷衝脈氣逆需結合不同層次或焦位的三到四個症狀組合。例如:下肢(足冷)、下腹(脹滿、月經不調或痛經)、上腹與少腹(脹滿、脹痛、疼痛、噁心)、胸部(乳脹、心悸、胸悶)、咽喉頭部(咽中如有異物感、面部發熱、頭暈)。這些症狀皆循衝脈之循行路徑而發。婦科血瘀:衝脈為血海,其病理根源常見於婦科疾患。影響衝脈的三種血病為血虛(閉經、月經量少)、血熱(月經量多)及血瘀(痛經夾血塊)。衝脈特別適用於治療婦科血瘀病症,如同任脈特別適用於治療婦科氣滯病症一般。女子乳房:任脈布散於胸與乳房,故其氣對乳房有深遠影響。任脈負責產後化生乳汁,將經血轉化為乳汁。衝脈則可協助治療乳房腫塊、乳房脹痛、缺乳(乳汁不下)或乳汁不足。心:衝脈對心有深遠影響,因其循行路徑環繞心臟。可用於治療心律問題及心律不整。胃:因衝脈起於氣衝穴(ST-30,水穀之海之上穴),故經由此穴與胃相連。衝脈可治療胃病,尤其是實證類型(胃氣鬱滯、胃氣上逆、胃血瘀、胃熱)。下肢氣血循行:因衝脈有一分支下行至足背及大趾,故此脈可治療足部循環障礙(發冷、麻木、刺痛、紫斑樣變化)。《中醫基礎學》,Maciocia,2015年,第915頁;2005年版,第862頁。"
    },
