      "exp_en": "This is yang ming channel pattern. At the Bright-Yang (yang ming) stage, the external pathogenic factor (Wind-Cold) has transformed into Heat and has moved interior. The Bright-Yang (yang ming) stage manifests in two ways: Heat without form (Bright-Yang channel pattern) and Heat with form (Bright-Yang organ pattern). In the Bright-Yang channel pattern there is interior Heat that is projected to the surface of the body. The Bright-Yang pattern has the key symptoms-signs of the \"Four Bigs\" which are Big Thirst, Big Sweating, Big Fever, and Big Pulse. Because there is Heat in the Stomach (yang ming) the thirst is strong. Because the Heat is strong there will be an actual fever in the yang ming stage as compared to the tai yang stage where the body feels hot without there being an actual fever. Because the heat is strong and in excess, there is no aversion to cold but more of an aversion to heat. There is profuse sweating because the excess Heat steams and pushes the Body Fluids out. The struggle between the strong anti-pathogenic qi (Upright qi or zheng qi) and the hyperactive pathogenic Heat leads to an accumulation of qi and Blood filling the Blood Vessels and resulting in a big pulse. The mental symptoms (irritability, delirium) are caused by Heat disturbing the Mind. The red tongue with yellow coating are indications of excess Heat. The treatment principle is to Clear Stomach Heat. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 757; 2005 Edition, page 715",
      "exp_hant": "此為陽明經證。在陽明階段,外邪(風寒)已化熱並傳入於裡。陽明階段表現有兩種方式:無形之熱(陽明經證)與有形之熱(陽明腑證)。陽明經證中,裡熱外透於體表。陽明證之關鍵症狀特徵為「四大」,即大渴、大汗、大熱、大脈。因胃(陽明)有熱,故口渴劇烈。因熱勢強盛,陽明階段會出現真正的發熱,相較於太陽階段身體發熱卻無實際發熱。因熱邪熾盛,不惡寒反惡熱。因熱邪蒸迫,津液外泄,故大汗淋漓。正氣(抗邪之氣)與亢盛之邪熱相搏,導致氣血充盈脈道,形成洪大之脈。神志症狀(煩躁、譫語)乃熱邪擾神所致。舌紅苔黃為熱盛之徵。治療原則為清胃熱。《中醫基礎學》,Maciocia,2015年,第757頁;2005年版,第715頁。"
