      "exp_en": "Dantian, dan tian, dan tien or tan t'ien can be translated as \"elixir field\", \"sea of qi\", or simply \"energy center\". There are three main dantians. The lower dantian is below the navel. The middle dantian is located on the middle of the chest. The upper dantian is located on the forehead between the eyebrows or third eye. The lower dantian is located about three finger widths below the navel and about two finger widths inside the body. In Tai Chi or Qigong it is the lower dantian which is focused on. The lower dantian is part of all martial art traditions. In Japanese it is called Hara. Some Buddhist practices emphasize focusing on the lower dantian as a way of controlling thoughts and emotions. tcmtests.com, January 2020",
      "exp_hant": "丹田（dantian）可譯為「煉丹之田」、「氣海」或簡稱「能量中心」。丹田主要有三個：下丹田位於肚臍下方；中丹田位於胸部正中；上丹田位於前額眉心（又稱天目）處。下丹田約位於肚臍下三指寬、體內約二指深處。在太極或氣功中，所著重的是下丹田。下丹田是所有武術傳統共通的概念，在日文中稱為「Hara」。部分佛教修行法門也強調專注於下丹田，以此作為控制思緒與情緒的方法。tcmtests.com, January 2020"
