      "exp_en": "One of the functions of the Extraordinary Vessels is to absorb and transfer qi. The overflow of qi that runs into Extraordinary Vessels irrigates and nourishes the space between the skin and muscles which is the space that circulates wei qi. The space between the skin and muscles is called cou li. The Extraordinary Vessels help circulate wei qi particularly in the thorax (ren mai, chong mai), abdomen (ren mai, chong mai) and back (du mai). The Extraordinary Vessels all derive directly or indirectly from the Kidneys. Thus, the Kidneys play a very important role in assisting the wei qi protect the body from external pathogenic factors. That is, there is a relationship between the Kidneys, via the Extraordinary Vessels, and the protective energy (wei qi) of the body. This explains why, for example, patients with a weak constitution can be subject to frequent wind-cold invasions. Wei qi is rooted in the lower jiao (Kidneys), nourished by the middle jiao (Spleen), and is spread out by the upper jiao (Lungs). The Extraordinary Vessels circulate the Kidney Essence and are a connection between Pre-Heaven Qi (Kidneys) and Post-Heaven Qi (Spleen, Lungs). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 870-871",
      "exp_hant": "奇經八脈的功能之一是蓄積並轉輸氣血。奇經蓄溢而出的氣灌注滋養皮膚與肌肉之間的空隙，此處正是衛氣循行之處，稱為「腠理」。奇經八脈特別有助於衛氣在胸部（任脈、衝脈）、腹部（任脈、衝脈）及背部（督脈）的循行。奇經八脈皆直接或間接源自於腎。因此，腎在協助衛氣抵禦外邪方面扮演極為重要的角色。也就是說，腎透過奇經八脈與人體的衛氣（防禦能量）之間存在著密切關係。這也說明了為何體質虛弱的患者容易反覆感受風寒。衛氣根源於下焦（腎），得中焦（脾）之滋養，並由上焦（肺）宣發布散。奇經八脈輸布腎精，並連結先天之氣（腎）與後天之氣（脾、肺）。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 870-871"
