    {
      "number": 304,
      "question_en": "Which of the following has correct symptoms associated with the level?",
      "question_hant": "下列何者所列的症狀與其所屬階段相符？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Nutritive Qi level Heat: incoherent speech, restlessness, night fever",
          "hant": "營分熱：譫語、心煩、夜間發熱",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Wei Qi level Heat: aversion to cold, profuse sweating, slight fever",
          "hant": "衛分熱：惡寒、大汗、微熱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Blood level Heat: low fever at night, bleeding, clear skin, twitching",
          "hant": "血分熱：夜間低熱、出血、皮膚清爽、抽搐",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Qi level Heat: aversion to cold, high fever, intense thirst",
          "hant": "氣分熱：惡寒、高熱、劇渴",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Blood level has tendency to have skin symptoms (macules, petechiae). Qi level does not have aversion to cold. Wei qi level can have slight sweating, not profuse. Blood level has high fever at night. At the Blood level, heat enters the blood, heating it, and makes the blood move recklessly which causes bleeding from various areas such as macules (bleeding under the skin which can also occur at the ying level), epistaxis, vomiting blood, and blood in stool. The heat in the blood can disturb the mind and cause manic behavior. Fever at night reflects heat penetrating at the Nutritive Qi level. The heat at this level affects the mind, causing mental changes (restlessness, delirium, insomnia). Macules can occur at the Nutritive Qi level but they are more typical with the Blood level. The pulse at the Blood level is wiry-rapid. The pulse at the Nutritive Qi level is fine-rapid. The tongue at the Blood level is dark-red and without coating. The tongue at the Nutritive Qi level is red and without coating. The treatment principle for the Blood level is Clear Blood Heat, Stop Bleeding. If the Blood Heat stirs the Liver Wind (high fever, twitching, convulsions, rigid neck, teeth clenching) the treatment principle is Clear Blood Heat, Extinguish Wind. If the heat at the Blood Level injures the yin leading to internal wind (low-grade fever, limb tremors, malar flush, listlessness), the treatment principle is Clear Blood Heat, Nourish Liver-Kidney yin, Extinguish Wind. The treatment principle for Heat at the Nutritive Qi level is Clear Nutritive Qi Heat, Promote Fluids. If the Nutritive Qi Heat has affected the Pericardium (night fever, mental confusion, incoherent speech, delirium, hot hands and cold feet, macules) the treatment principle is to Clear Nutritive Qi Heat, Clear Pericardium Heat, Restore Consciousness, Promote Fluids. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 771",
      "exp_hant": "血分階段易出現皮膚症狀（斑疹、瘀點）。氣分階段不會有惡寒。衛分階段可有輕微出汗，而非大汗。血分階段則有夜間高熱。在血分階段，熱邪入血，使血因熱而沸騰，導致血液妄行，於各處出血，如斑疹（皮下出血，營分階段亦可能出現）、鼻衄、吐血、便血。血中之熱可擾亂心神，引起狂躁行為。夜間發熱反映熱邪深入營分。此階段的熱邪影響心神，導致神志改變（心煩、譫語、失眠）。斑疹在營分階段可能出現，但以血分階段更為典型。血分階段脈象弦數，營分階段脈象細數。血分階段舌質深紅無苔，營分階段舌質紅而無苔。血分證的治療原則為清血分熱、涼血止血。若血熱動肝風（高熱、抽搐、驚厥、頸項強直、牙關緊閉），治療原則為清血分熱、涼血熄風。若血分之熱傷陰而致內風（低熱、肢體震顫、顴紅、精神萎靡），治療原則為清血分熱、滋養肝腎之陰、熄風。營分熱的治療原則為清營分熱、生津。若營分熱已影響心包（夜間發熱、神志不清、譫語、昏迷、手足心熱而四肢厥冷、斑疹），治療原則為清營分熱、清心包熱、開竅醒神、生津。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 771"
    },
    {
      "number": 305,
      "question_en": "A 60 year-old man complains of frequent night urination. There is no pain, no sense of urgency and no blood in the urine. After each urination there is the sensation that the bladder is not fully emptied. He needs to put forth effort in order for the urination to start. The urine stream is thin. The patient looks dejected. He has distention in the lower abdomen. He complains of feeling physically weak. He has shallow breathing. Other symptoms include a sore lower back, fear of cold and slight hearing loss. The tongue is pale with a white and wet coating. The pulse is deep and wiry. It is weak and thin in the rear positions. What is the diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一名60歲男性主訴夜尿頻繁，無疼痛、無急迫感，亦無血尿。每次排尿後皆有膀胱未排空之感，須用力才能排出小便，尿線細小。患者神情沮喪，小腹脹滿，自覺體力虛弱，呼吸短淺。其他症狀包括腰痠、畏寒及輕微聽力減退。舌淡，苔白而濕潤，脈沉弦，尺部脈弱而細。診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Deficient Qi with Accumulation of Cold",
          "hant": "氣虛兼寒積",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Kidney yang deficiency",
          "hant": "腎陽虛",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Kidney Qi Deficiency, Damp-Heat pouring Downward",
          "hant": "腎氣虛，濕熱下注",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Deficient Qi, Damp-Cold in the Bladder",
          "hant": "氣虛，膀胱寒濕",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Bladder function of storing-releasing urine is facilitated by Kidney qi. As the patient is 60 years old, by this age Kidney qi has declined and its control over the Bladder has diminished leading to frequent urination. As weakened Kidneys can lead to an imbalance in water distribution, this can result in incomplete urination, straining during urination, and reduced volume. Hearing loss, fear of cold, dejection, and sore low back point to Kidney weakness. The age of the patient and the fear of cold point to a deficiency of yang. Shallow breathing and pale tongue tongue point to a deficient qi condition. The deep-wiry pulse and wet tongue coating indicated stagnation of Fluids. The weak-thin pulse in the rear position reflect Kidney deficiency. Acupuncture Case Histories, Chen and Wang, 1988, page 87",
      "exp_hant": "膀胱貯尿排尿的功能須賴腎氣之推動。患者年已60歲，此年齡腎氣已漸衰退，對膀胱的約束控制力減弱，因而導致夜尿頻繁。腎氣虛弱可致水液輸布失衡，因而出現排尿不盡、排尿費力及尿量減少等表現。聽力減退、畏寒、神情沮喪及腰痠皆提示腎虛。患者的年齡與畏寒則提示陽虛。呼吸短淺與舌淡則提示氣虛之象。脈沉弦與舌苔濕潤提示水液停滯。尺部脈弱而細則反映腎虛。Acupuncture Case Histories, Chen and Wang, 1988, page 87"
    },
    {
      "number": 306,
      "question_en": "In index finger diagnosis, what helps to determine whether the child has an interior or exterior disease?",
      "question_hant": "在小兒食指診法中，判斷內外病證的依據為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "how many bars the veins stretch",
          "hant": "脈紋延伸至幾關",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "whether the veins are deep or not",
          "hant": "脈紋是否深沉",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "whether the veins are thin or dense",
          "hant": "脈紋是稀疏或濃密",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "the color of the veins",
          "hant": "脈紋的顏色",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Floating or deep veins help to differentiate between an internal or external disease. Veins that float and have a shallow color generally indicate an external disease. Veins that are deep with a deep color indicate an interior pattern. How many bars the vein stretch helps to determine the severity of the disease. Veins isolated in the Wind Bar indicate a mild disease, while those stretching into the Qi Bar indicate a relatively strong disease, and the veins stretching all the way to the Life Bar indicates a severe disease. If the network of veins stretches all the way to the edge of the nails this indicates a critical condition. The color of the veins provide information on whether the disease is hot or cold. Fresh red veins indicates wind-cold, purple-red indicates heat, green-blue indicates fright-wind, green blue with purple-black indicates a serious disease due to phlegm-food. Whether the veins are dense or thin can indicate repletion or vacuity. Veins that are thin with a shallow-pale color indicates vacuity. Veins that are dense, deep with stagnant color indicate repletion (usually due to stagnant accumulation in the GI tract). Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 26",
      "exp_hant": "脈紋浮現或深沉有助於區別內外病證。脈紋浮顯且色淺者，一般表示外感病證；脈紋深沉且色深者，則表示內在病證。脈紋延伸至幾關則有助判斷病情之輕重：脈紋僅見於風關者為病情較輕；延伸至氣關者病情較重；延伸至命關者則病情嚴重。若脈紋網絡延伸至指甲邊緣，則表示病情危重。脈紋的顏色可提供病證屬寒屬熱的訊息：鮮紅色主風寒，紫紅色主熱，青藍色主驚風，青藍夾紫黑色則表示因痰食所致之重症。脈紋濃密或稀疏則可顯示實證或虛證：脈紋稀疏、色淺淡者為虛證；脈紋濃密、深沉且色滯者為實證（通常因腸胃積滯所致）。Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 26"
    },
