      "exp_en": "It is a Kidney yang xu that overflows water to the Heart. The Heart belongs to the Fire element (yang), resides in the upper jiao, and represents movement. The Kidneys belong to the Water element (yin), resides in the lower jiao, and represents stillness. Yang Fire (Heart) and Yin Water (Kidneys) balance and nourish each other. The qi of the Heart descends to the Kidneys and the qi of the Kidneys ascends to the Heart. The yang of the Heart descends and nourishes Kidney yin which in turn ascends and nourishes-cools Heart yang. When Kidney yang is xu, body fluids do not transform, accumulate, and overflow to the Heart. When Kidney yin is xu, the yin does not ascend to nourish-cool the Heart and this results in an Empty Heat pattern of the Heart. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 179; 2005 Edition, page 174; 1989 Edition, page 106",
      "exp_hant": "水氣凌心是由腎陽虛所引起，而非腎陰虛。心屬火行（陽），位居上焦，主動；腎屬水行（陰），位居下焦，主靜。心之陽火與腎之陰水相互平衡、相互滋養。心氣下降於腎，腎氣則上升於心。心陽下降以滋養腎陰，腎陰則上升以滋養、涼潤心陽。當腎陽虛時，體內水液不能正常氣化，因而停聚並上凌於心。當腎陰虛時，陰液不能上升以滋養、涼潤心陽，因而形成心的虛熱證。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 179; 2005 Edition, page 174; 1989 Edition, page 106"
