      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. This patient does not have the pattern of blood stasis combined with phlegm accumulation. There are symptoms-signs for phlegm accumulation but not for blood stasis. During his outbreaks, this patient had typical psoriasis skin changes. The skin was thick, red, and itchy. The clinical picture points to blood-heat (skin redness, red tongue, rapid pulse) and blood dryness (dry, itchy skin) compounded with Spleen qi deficiency (overweight, abdominal bloating, weak pulse) and phlegm accumulation (yellow-greasy tongue coating). The weak pulse indicated deficiency while the rapid pulse indicated heat and the floating pulse indicated external wind-dry pathogens. The red tongue indicated heat and the yellow-greasy coating indicated phlegm accumulation. The full diagnosis is bai bi (psoriasis) due to blood heat with wind-dryness and Spleen qi deficiency causing phlegm accumulation. The treatment principle is to Clear heat, Dispel wind, Nourish blood, Resolve phlegm, and Fortify the Spleen. TCM Case Studies: Autoimmune Disease, Sheng-ping, Fratkin, and Jing, 2014, page 156-157",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。此患者並無血瘀夾痰積之證型。雖有痰積之症狀徵象，卻無血瘀之徵象。發作期間，此患者呈現典型的乾癬皮膚變化，皮膚增厚、發紅且搔癢。臨床表現提示血熱（皮膚發紅、舌紅、脈數）及血燥（皮膚乾燥搔癢），並兼夾脾氣虛（體重過重、腹脹、脈弱）及痰積（舌苔黃膩）。脈弱提示虛證，脈數提示熱證，脈浮則提示外感風燥之邪。舌紅提示熱證，苔黃膩則提示痰積。完整診斷為血熱風燥、脾氣虛致痰積所引起的白疕（乾癬）。治療原則為清熱、袪風、養血、化痰、健脾。TCM Case Studies: Autoimmune Disease, Sheng-ping, Fratkin, and Jing, 2014, page 156-157"
