          "en": "needle the Opening point and Associated point unilaterally",
          "hant": "於同一側針刺開穴與配穴",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "All of these are valid techniques for needling the Opening and Associated points of the Extraordinary Vessels. The Great Compendium of Acupuncture recommends first needling the Opening point and then needling the Associated point This is called the \"guest-host\" technique in which the Opening point (host) of the vessel is first needled and then followed by needling the Associated point (guest). Maciocia recommends first needling the Opening point on one side and the Associated point on the opposite side. Further, he assigns needling the Opening point on the left side and the Associated point on the right side for men. It is vice versa for women. Needling the Opening and Associated points unilaterally is selected to treat unilateral disorders such as one sided back pain, one sided headache, bi-syndrome, or the after effect of a Wind-Stroke. The needles are usually removed in the reverse order than they were inserted. The Opening and Associated points are selected when there is a need to influence the areas targeted by an Extraordinary Vessel or to absorb and regulate and absorb an excess such as stagnant qi or blood. For example, a patient has an acute itchy nose from an attack of wind-heat and also has an itchy anus due to damp-heat. Each disorder can be treated separately via pattern diagnosis (expel wind-heat, drain damp and clear heat). However, both disorders can be treated via the Governing Vessel's area of influence on the nose and anus without having to consider the cause (wind-heat, damp-heat) of each pattern. This is done by first needling SI-3 and then needling BL-62. These two points treat the whole area under the direct influence of the Governing Vessel (du mai). Individual points on the Extraordinary Vessels only influence the local area and DO NOT influence the totality of the areas of the vessel. Only the Opening and Closing points do that. However, individual points on the vessel can be combined with the Opening and Associated points to direct the energy of that Vessel to that area. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 880-881",
      "exp_hant": "以上皆為針刺奇經開穴與配穴的有效技法。《針灸大成》建議先針刺開穴，再針刺配穴，此稱為「主客」法，即先針刺該經脈之開穴（主），再針刺配穴（客）。馬萬里（Maciocia）則建議一側先針刺開穴，另一側針刺配穴；並進一步指出，男性應於左側針刺開穴、右側針刺配穴，女性則相反。於同一側針刺開穴與配穴，則適用於治療單側病證，如單側腰痛、單側頭痛、痹證，或中風後遺症。出針時通常依進針的相反順序拔出。當需要影響某條奇經所主治的區域，或需吸納並調節如氣滯血瘀等實邪時，即可選用開穴與配穴。舉例而言，患者因風熱侵襲而急性鼻癢，同時因濕熱而肛門搔癢。此兩種病證雖可依各自的辨證分別治療（袪風熱、瀉濕清熱），但亦可透過督脈對鼻與肛門所主治的區域一併治療，而無須分別考量各證型的病因（風熱、濕熱）。作法為先針刺後谿（SI-3），再針刺申脈（BL-62）。此兩穴可治療督脈直接主治的整個區域。奇經上的單一穴位僅能影響局部區域，並不能影響該經脈所主治的全部區域，唯有開穴與配穴方能達此效果。然而，該經脈上的單一穴位仍可與開穴、配穴合用，以引導該經脈之氣至該區域。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 880-881"
    },
