      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Small Intestine Qi Pain. This pattern (acute or chronic) is associated with Liver Qi Stasis attacking the Spleen with an emphasis on the Small Intestine. The white coating reflects that the pattern has yet to transform into Heat (Liver Qi Stasis transforming into Fire) in which case the coating could be yellow and the sides of the tongue turn red. If this pattern is acute it is a Full condition (Qi Stasis). If it is chronic it can be a mixed Full (Qi Stasis) and Empty (weak Spleen Qi) pattern. The pulse in this pattern is deep-wiry, particularly on the rear positions. Only having abdominal twisting pain is sufficient to make the diagnosis of Small Intestine Qi Pain. The treatment principle is Move Small Intestine Qi and Smooth Liver Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 680; 2005 Edition, page 639; 1989 Edition, page 274",
      "exp_hant": "此為小腸氣痛。此證(無論急性或慢性)與肝氣鬱結橫犯脾土,且偏重於小腸有關。白苔反映此證尚未化熱(肝氣鬱結化火),若化熱則苔可轉黃、舌邊轉紅。若屬急性則為實證(氣滯);若屬慢性,則可能為實(氣滯)虛(脾氣虛)夾雜之證。此證脈象沉弦,尤以尺部為甚。僅憑小腹絞痛即足以診斷為小腸氣痛。治療原則為理小腸氣、疏肝氣。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 680; 2005 Edition, page 639; 1989 Edition, page 274"
    },
    {
      "number": 352,
      "question_en": "A 37 year-old female patient has had scanty periods for the past six years. She also complained of dizziness, low back pain, and tinnitus. She sometimes feels cold. Her prescription drugs include Restasis (cyclosporine). The tongue did not have any coating and the pulse was thin. The treatment principle chosen was Tonify Kidney Qi. She was treated for three months through three menstrual cycles, after which she was evaluated. She reported that though she felt more energy she still did not see any improvement with her menstrual cycle. What would the treatment principle be now?",
