      "exp_en": "The original assessment and treatment was Kidney Qi Deficiency. That her menstrual period did not improve could mean that some important elements in the diagnosis were missed. The lack of tongue coating indicated a deficient yin condition. The drug Restasis is for chronic dry eyes, another yin deficiency symptom. The practitioner did not know or ask about the reason for the prescription. Eye dryness is a key symptom of Liver yin deficiency. The back pain and tinnitus point to the Kidneys. The dizziness can be caused by either the Liver or the Kidneys. There are not enough symptoms or strong enough symptoms to point to a Kidney yang deficiency (sometimes feels cold). What we are looking at is a Liver and Kidney yin deficiency as the root pattern for the early and scanty periods. The treatment principle was then changed to Nourishing the Liver and Kidney Yin. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 640",
      "exp_hant": "原先的辨證與治療為腎氣虛。月經未見改善,可能表示辨證中遺漏了重要的線索。舌無苔顯示為陰虛之證。Restasis是用於治療慢性乾眼症的藥物,乾眼亦為陰虛的另一項症狀。原醫者並未了解或詢問此藥物的用藥原因。眼睛乾澀是肝陰虛的關鍵症狀。腰痛與耳鳴則指向腎;頭暈則可能由肝或腎所致。目前症狀不足以支持腎陽虛(偶爾怕冷)的診斷。此案例應屬肝腎陰虛,為月經提前量少之根本證型,故治療原則其後改為滋養肝腎之陰。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 640"
