      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Small Intestine Qi Tied. This is always an acute pattern than can occur, from a Western point of view, with or without appendicitis. The expected pulse in this pattern is a Deep-Wiry pulse (especially in the rear positions which correspond to the Lower Burner). The Deep quality reflects that the condition is internal. The Wiry quality reflects both the Qi stagnation in this pattern and the intensity of the pain. The Deep-Wiry pulse reflects Qi obstruction in the interior. A thick-white tongue coating is expected in this pattern. There is a severe qi obstruction in the Small Intestine that blocks the descending of Stomach Qi resulting in a thickened tongue coating. The white color is that of normal coating indicating that there is no heat and, from the symptoms, no cold. Lower abdominal pain and deep-wiry pulse are sufficient to make the diagnosis of Small Intestine Qi Tied. The treatment principle is Remove Lower Jiao Obstruction and Move Small Intestine Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 681; 2005 Edition, page 641; 1989 Edition, page 275",
      "exp_hant": "此為小腸氣結之診斷。此證恆屬急性,從西醫角度來看,可能伴有或不伴有闌尾炎。此證預期脈象為沉弦(尤以尺部,對應下焦為甚)。沉主病在裡;弦則反映此證之氣滯及疼痛之劇烈。沉弦脈反映裡部氣機阻滯。此證預期舌苔厚白。小腸氣機嚴重阻滯,致使胃氣無法下降,因而舌苔增厚。白色為正常苔色,顯示無熱,且依症狀判斷亦無寒。下腹痛與沉弦脈即足以診斷為小腸氣結。治療原則為通下焦之阻、理小腸氣。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 681; 2005 Edition, page 641; 1989 Edition, page 275"
    },
    {
      "number": 362,
      "question_en": "A 70 year-old male patient with Parkinson's disease has been prescribed the drug L-dopa. He should be careful taking the medication with meals that have too much",
      "question_hant": "一名70歲男性帕金森氏症患者,已被處方左旋多巴(L-dopa)藥物。他在服藥時應避免與含過多下列何種成分的餐食一併食用?",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "carbohydrates",
          "hant": "碳水化合物",
