      "number": 382,
      "question_en": "Two days ago, a 44 year-old female patient started feeling cold with a slight fever and shivers, with severe body aches, an occipital headache, with no sweating, no thirst, and clear urine. The tongue was normal. She then started to feel more feverish with less shivers, decreased body aches, slight sweating, a stronger headache, slight thirst, and slightly dark urine. The front of the tongue was slightly red. Then she suddenly started to feel very hot, irritable, having a difficulty falling asleep, night sweats, and a dry mouth and throat. Her tongue was red and the coating was peeling. Based on the Six Stages and Four Levels differentiation what is the progression of the disease?",
      "question_hant": "兩天前,一名44歲女性患者開始出現怕冷、輕微發熱及發抖,伴嚴重周身痠痛、後頭部頭痛,無汗、不渴,小便清長。舌象正常。其後她開始發熱加重、發抖減輕、周身痠痛減緩、微汗出,頭痛加劇,口微渴,小便略顯深黃。舌尖略紅。接著她突然感到非常燥熱、煩躁、難以入睡、盜汗,並有口乾咽乾。舌紅,苔剝落。依六經與衛氣營血辨證,此病之傳變過程為何?",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "wind-heat → Lung Heat qi level → jue yin stage",
          "hant": "風熱 → 肺熱氣分證 → 厥陰病",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "wind-cold → Lung Heat qi level → shao yin stage",
          "hant": "風寒 → 肺熱氣分證 → 少陰病",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "tai yang stage → wei qi level → shao yin stage",
          "hant": "太陽病 → 衛分證 → 少陰病",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "tai yang stage → wei qi level → jue yin stage",
          "hant": "太陽病 → 衛分證 → 厥陰病",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "An external wind-cold pathogen has entered the body. The tai yang stage is associated with wind-cold (aversion to cold, slight fever, no sweating, headache, stiff neck, sneezing, runny nose with white discharge, breathlessness, normal tongue, floating-tight pulse). From there the wind-cold transformed into wind-heat. The wei qi level is associated with wind-heat (fever, aversion to cold, headache, sore throat, slight sweating, runny nose with yellow discharge, swollen tonsils, body aches, slight thirst, red tongue thin-white coating, floating-rapid pulse). From the wind-heat stage the disease progressed further into the body to the shao yin stage. The shao yin stage has two patterns: cold transformation (Kidney yang xu with empty cold) and heat transformation (Kidney yin xu with empty heat). Heat transformation of the shao yin stage has feelings of heat, irritability, insomnia, dry mouth and throat at night, dark urine, night sweating, red tongue without coating, and a fine-rapid pulse. The jue yin stage is characterized by Heat above (thirst, hot feelings, etc) and Cold below (no desire to eat, cold limbs, etc). Lung Heat is at the qi level (fever, SOB, cough, red tongue with yellow coating). Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 755, 761, 770",
      "exp_hant": "外感風寒之邪侵入人體。太陽病階段與風寒相關(惡寒、微熱、無汗、頭痛、項強、噴嚏、流清涕、氣短、舌象正常、脈浮緊)。其後風寒轉化為風熱。衛分證與風熱相關(發熱、惡寒、頭痛、咽痛、微汗、流黃涕、扁桃腺腫、周身痠痛、微渴、舌紅苔薄白、脈浮數)。由風熱階段,病邪進一步深入至少陰病階段。少陰病有兩種證型:寒化(腎陽虛兼虛寒)與熱化(腎陰虛兼虛熱)。少陰病熱化證表現為身熱感、煩躁、失眠、夜間口乾咽乾、小便深黃、盜汗、舌紅無苔、脈細數。厥陰病則以上熱(口渴、身熱感等)下寒(不欲食、肢冷等)為特徵。肺熱屬氣分證(發熱、氣短、咳嗽、舌紅苔黃)。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 755, 761, 770"
    },
