      "exp_en": "The tongue can be checked to exclude serious internal organ problems when assessing emotional issue. In this case, if the tongue were dark red, peeled, or cracked it would indicate that internal organs have been impacted by the emotional issues. It would mean that nutritive qi or blood level were affected. On the other hand, if the tongue was not red (just the tip red), had slightly thick coating, and the tongue body was normal then it would indicate that the emotional stress is at the qi level. If only the tip of the tongue is red, it indicates that the emotional problem is not deep. When the whole tongue is red and the tip is even redder, it reflects a more chronic and deeper emotional issue. If the whole tongue is red with a redder tip and with a midline crack going to just about the tip, it reflects a deep, chronic emotional problem with a constitutionally weak Heart that has a tendency to be affected by emotional stressors which is indicated by the tongue having a red tip. Tongue Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1995, page 124, 127",
      "exp_hant": "評估情志問題時,可藉舌象排除嚴重內臟病變之可能。此案例中,若舌暗紅、剝苔或有裂紋,即顯示情志問題已影響內臟,意味著營分或血分層次已受波及。反之,若舌不紅(僅舌尖紅)、苔略厚,舌體正常,則顯示情志壓力僅在氣分層次。若僅舌尖紅,顯示情志問題尚淺;若整體舌紅且舌尖更紅,則反映情志問題較深且屬慢性;若整個舌紅、舌尖更紅,並有一條幾乎抵達舌尖之正中裂紋,則反映情志問題深且屬慢性,並顯示心之體質性虛弱,易受情志壓力所擾,此即以舌尖紅為徵象。Tongue Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1995, page 124, 127"
    },
