      "exp_en": "The head is yang and the body is yin. All of the yang channels either end or begin on the head. Yang pathogenic factors (heat, fire) tend to rise to the head. The rest of the body (chest, abdomen) refers to yin and the chest/abdomen can be more affected by cold-damp (yin) pathogenic factors. Structure is yin and function is yang. Interior is yin and exterior is yang. Above the waist is yang and below is yin. Qi is yang and Blood/Fluids are yin. Wei qi is yang and ying qi (nutritive) is yin. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 9; 2005 Edition, page 9; 1989 Edition, page 7",
      "exp_hant": "頭為陽,身為陰。所有陽經皆起於或止於頭部。陽性病邪(熱、火)易上炎頭部。身體其餘部位(胸腹)屬陰,胸腹較易受寒濕(陰邪)所侵。結構屬陰,功能屬陽。裡屬陰,表屬陽。腰以上為陽,腰以下為陰。氣屬陽,血津液屬陰。衛氣屬陽,營氣屬陰。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 9; 2005 Edition, page 9; 1989 Edition, page 7"
    },
