        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Sea of Marrow, Sea of Blood , Sea of Qi, Sea of 12 Channels",
          "hant": "髓海、血海、氣海、十二經之海",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Sea of Marrow is associated with the Governing Vessel (du mai). Chong can be translated as \"infuse, rush, charge, street, activity, free passage, charge\". The word Penetrating combines the idea of rushing and streets that traverse and penetrate the body. The chong mai has been assigned various attributes. It is called \"Sea of Blood\" because it is related to the Uterus and controls the deep blood-luo connecting channels. It is called the \"Sea of the 12 Channels\" as it branches out in many small vessels that circulate wei qi in the abdomen-chest, circulates qi and Blood in all channels (except arms) and controls all of the luo channels. It is called the \"Sea of the Five Yin and Six Yang Organs\" as it connects Pre-Heaven and Post-Heaven qi through the chong mai connection to the Kidneys and Stomach, is directly related to the three yin leg channels (Spleen, Liver, Kidneys), and has a connection to the Heart (chong mai flows around the Heart). Maciocia does not say the Chong Mai itself is the Sea of Food. Instead, it is the Sea of Blood that has an important connection to the Sea of Food via ST-30 and the Stomach. The Chong Mai passes through or emerges at ST-30, creating a close connection that allows it to draw on Post-Heaven nourishment. Maciocia explains this as part of how the Chong Mai links Kidney Jing (Pre-Heaven) with Stomach-derived Qi and Blood (Post-Heaven). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 902, 908; Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 382",
      "exp_hant": "髓海乃與督脈相關。「衝」可譯為「注入、奔湧、衝擊、街道、活動、暢通無阻、衝擊」之意。「衝脈」一詞結合了奔湧與貫通全身之街道之意涵。衝脈被賦予多種特性。稱其為「血海」,乃因其與胞宮相關,並主司深層血絡。稱其為「十二經之海」,乃因其分支眾多細小脈絡,循行於胸腹間以布散衛氣,並(除手臂外)於諸經中運行氣血,且主司所有絡脈。稱其為「五臟六腑之海」,乃因其透過與腎、胃之聯繫,溝通先天與後天之氣,並直接與足三陰經(脾、肝、腎)相關,亦與心相繫連(衝脈環繞心而行)。Maciocia並未言明衝脈本身即為「水穀之海」。而是「血海」透過ST-30(氣衝)與胃,而與「水穀之海」有重要聯繫。衝脈經過或發於ST-30,形成緊密聯繫,使其得以汲取後天水穀之滋養。Maciocia將此解釋為衝脈聯繫腎精(先天)與胃所化生之氣血(後天)機制之一部分。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 902, 908; Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 382"
