      "exp_en": "This is a case of mixed excess and deficiency. There is Liver qi stasis (abdominal pain, distention, symptoms worse with emotions, wiry pulse) which turns into Fire (red tongue, redder side) and affects the Heart (red tongue tip, lusterless eyes). The abdominal pain improves with heat not because the underlying issue is cold but because the heat moves the qi and blood. The pulse is weak due to chronic deficiency of the Lungs (sadness, weepy voice, tiredness, weak pulse) and sinking Spleen qi (hypogastric pain worse with lifting, possible prolapse of bladder, tiredness, weak pulse) deficiency. The original prescription focuses on Liver and Kidney yin deficiency with Empty Fire. The second Rx focused on moving Liver qi and tonifying the Spleen and Lungs. There is no need to clear Liver Fire because it arises from Liver qi stasis which once eliminated will clear Liver Fire. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 768",
      "exp_hant": "此為虛實夾雜之案例。此案有肝氣鬱結(腹痛、腹脹、情緒波動時症狀加重、脈弦),日久化火(舌紅、舌邊更紅)並影響於心(舌尖紅、雙眼無神)。腹痛因熱敷而緩解,並非因病本屬寒,而是因熱能行氣活血。脈弱乃因肺之慢性虛損(悲傷、哭腔、疲乏、脈弱)及脾氣下陷(小腹痛因提重物加劇、可能伴膀胱脫垂、疲乏、脈弱)所致之虛證。原處方著重於肝腎陰虛兼虛火。第二次處方則著重於疏肝氣、補益脾肺。此案無須清肝火,因其源於肝氣鬱結,一旦肝氣鬱結消除,肝火自當隨之而清。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 768"
    },
