      "exp_en": "The clinical pictures has three patterns. The excess bleeding was due to Deficient Spleen Qi failing to hold the blood associated with a Kidney Yin Deficiency. There was also Empty Heat agitating the Blood. The Spleen Qi xu manifested as tiredness, bleeding in a sudden flood, and empty pulse. The Kidney Yin xu manifested as tinnitus, thirst, night sweating, back pain, and empty pulse. If the bleeding was due mainly to Kidney yin xu, the bleeding would be in trickles and at the end of the period. The Empty Heat manifested as a red-peeled tongue with cracks and an overflowing-empty pulse. It is the Empty Heat that is agitating the Blood. There is no Hot Blood in the clinical picture nor Liver yin Deficiency. The treatment principle was Tonify Spleen Qi, Nourish Kidney Yin, Clear Empty Heat, Stop bleeding. Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1st Edition, page 334",
      "exp_hant": "此臨床表現包含三種證型。經血過多乃因脾氣虛不能統血,並兼有腎陰虛。此外亦有虛熱擾動血分。脾氣虛表現為疲倦、經血突然崩流及脈虛。腎陰虛表現為耳鳴、口渴、盜汗、腰痛及脈虛。若經血過多主要因腎陰虛所致,則出血應呈點滴狀,並於經期末段出現。虛熱則表現為舌紅剝苔有裂紋,及洪而虛之脈象。正是此虛熱擾動血分。此臨床表現中並無血熱,亦無肝陰虛。治療原則為補脾氣、滋腎陰、清虛熱、止血。Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1st Edition, page 334"
