      "exp_en": "The symptoms are due to an excess in the channel. The fullness of connecting channels arise either from an external pathogenic factor or from inner qi or blood stasis, generally acute. The Large Intestine luo-connecting channel starts at LI-6, joins with its interior-exterior Lung channel three cun above the wrist, ascends the arm to LI-15 and then to the jaw and cheek where it splits with one branch connecting to the teeth and the other branch entering the ear. The Stomach, Small Intestine, Gall Bladder, and Triple Burner channels also gather and collect at the ear. LI-6 expels wind and clears heat, and opens and regulates the water passages. LI-6 as a luo point treats tooth decay, cold teeth, tinnitus, deafness, mouth deviation, swollen cheeks, dim vision, and pain in the wrist, elbow, and upper arm, Luo points treat disorders of their interior-exterior related channel or zang fu. LI-6 treats acute edema which occurs when external wind disrupts the Lung function of regulating the water passages. Luo points treat disorders in areas reached by the luo-connecting channel. The Large Intestine luo channel ascends to the ears and LI-6 can treat tinnitus and deafness and other ear disorders. Luo points can treat psychological and emotional disorders. LI-6 does not have any emotional symptoms. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804; 2005 Edition, page 760; A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 40, 96, 108; Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 250, 258",
      "exp_hant": "此症狀乃因絡脈實證所致。絡脈之實證,多因外感病邪或內在氣血瘀滯所引起,通常屬急性。大腸絡脈起於LI-6(偏歷),於腕上三寸處與其表裡相合之肺經相聯,沿手臂上行至LI-15(肩髃),再至下頷及頰部,一分支聯繫於齒,另一分支入耳。胃、小腸、膽及三焦諸經亦皆聚會於耳。LI-6袪風清熱,並通調水道。LI-6作為絡穴,可治齲齒、齒冷、耳鳴、耳聾、口喎、頰腫、視物昏花,以及腕、肘、上臂之疼痛。絡穴可治其表裡相合經絡或臟腑之病證。LI-6可治外感風邪擾亂肺主通調水道功能所致之急性水腫。絡穴可治絡脈所及部位之病證。大腸絡脈上行至耳,故LI-6可治耳鳴、耳聾及其他耳部病症。絡穴亦可治情志及精神方面病證。LI-6並無情志相關症狀。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804; 2005 Edition, page 760; A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 40, 96, 108; Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 250, 258"
