      "exp_en": "When the dai mai is too tight it is a Full condition. The symptoms include abdominal fullness, back feels like sitting in water (Damp-Cold Invades Spleen), back pain radiating to lower abdomen, heavy feeling in body, the feeling that the lower abdomen is carrying \"5,000 coins\", all of which are due to damp-cold exposure. The other answers are related to the dai mai being too loose, an Empty condition. The fetus depends on the Kidneys, Directing Vessel, and the Girdle Vessel. When the dai mai is too loose, the Spleen qi cannot rise and fails to nourish the fetus, resulting in miscarriages. The qi not rising due to a dai mai disorder can also result in organs sagging (prolapses) and hernias. A wei syndrome can also result when the dai mai vessel is slack. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 920",
      "exp_hant": "帶脈過緊屬實證，症狀包括腹部脹滿、背部如坐水中感（寒濕困脾）、腰痛牽引小腹、身體沉重感，以及小腹如負五千錢之感，這些皆因寒濕所致。其餘選項則與帶脈過鬆（虛證）有關。胎兒的發育有賴於腎、任脈與帶脈。當帶脈過鬆時，脾氣無法上升，無法濡養胎兒，因而導致流產。帶脈失調致氣不能升，亦可導致臟器下垂與疝氣。帶脈鬆弛亦可導致痿證。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第920頁"
