      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. The dai mai is the only channel that flows horizontally. It divides the body into two and is related to the Liver, Gall Bladder. It is the Kidney divergent channel which crosses the dai mai and connects to the dai mai at the level of BL-23. The Liver divergent channel ends at the genitals. The dai mai connects to BL-23. The dai mai itself flows through GB-26, GB-27, and GB-28. The dai mai is associated with the Liver's smooth flow of qi function through LR-13 (Spleen Mu point) and the Kidney's nourishing Essence through BL-23 (Kidneys). As such it connects Pre-Heaven Qi (Kidneys) with Post-Heaven Qi (Spleen), just like the chong mai does. The dai mai harmonizes the ascending of qi (Spleen) with the descending of qi (Kidneys). These functions associated with the Spleen, Kidney, and Liver depend on the dai mai (Belt Vessel) being relaxed and stretched. Moreover, the dai mai harmonizes the Liver and Gall Bladder and is useful in the treatment of full patterns such as temporal headaches with the Gall Bladder pulse as Full and Wiry. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 918",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。帶脈是唯一橫行的經脈，將人體分為上下兩部，與肝、膽相關。腎經別橫越帶脈，並於腎俞（BL-23）處與帶脈相連。肝經別止於陰部。帶脈聯繫腎俞（BL-23）。帶脈本身行經帶脈穴（GB-26）、五樞（GB-27）與維道（GB-28）。帶脈透過章門（LR-13，脾之募穴）與肝之疏泄功能相聯繫，並透過腎俞（BL-23）與腎之藏精功能相聯繫。如此一來，帶脈如同衝脈一般，連結先天之氣（腎）與後天之氣（脾）。帶脈協調脾氣之升與腎氣之降。這些與脾、腎、肝相關的功能，皆有賴帶脈保持鬆弛而富有伸展性。此外，帶脈能協調肝膽，對於治療實證（如伴隨膽脈弦實之偏頭痛）頗有助益。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第918頁"
