      "exp_en": "An excess eating of cold-raw foods or chronic exposure to cold on the abdomen can cause this pattern. This is an Internal, Deficient, and Cold pattern which is the same as a Spleen Yang Deficiency. The difference between the pattern of a Cold Large Intestine and Cold Invading the Large Intestine is that the former is a chronic Empty-Cold pattern and the latter is an acute Full-Cold pattern. The Empty-Cold manifests as loose stools, pale urine, cold limbs, and pale tongue. The deep weak pulse indicates an internal deficient condition. You only need loose stools, dull abdominal pain, and cold limbs to diagnose a Cold Large Intestine pattern. Just having loose stools, dull abdominal pain, cold extremities is enough to make the diagnosis. The treatment principle is to Tonify and Warm the Large Intestine and Spleen. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 698; 2005 Edition, page 657; 1989 Edition, page 281",
