          "key": "B",
          "en": "energetic level, the organs, the burners",
          "hant": "氣血層次、臟腑、三焦",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "the seasons, the burners",
          "hant": "季節、三焦",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "the seasons",
          "hant": "季節",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. The seasons are one of the factors influencing the depth or level of the pulse so that the pulse is deeper in the winter and more superficial in the summer. The three positions of the pulse (front, middle, rear) can be viewed from different perspectives. The three pulse positions can be assessed from the point of view of the type of energy (front: qi. Middle: Blood. Rear: yin), the energetic level (front: superficial level. Middle: middle level. Rear: deep level), the organs (front: heart and lungs. Middle: stomach and spleen. Rear: kidneys), and the three burners (front: upper burner. Middle: middle burner. Rear: lower burner). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 379",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且正確的答案。季節是影響脈象深淺的因素之一，冬季脈象較沉，夏季則較浮。脈診三部（寸、關、尺）可從不同角度來看待。三部脈位可依氣血種類（寸：氣。關：血。尺：陰）、氣血層次（寸：淺層。關：中層。尺：深層）、臟腑（寸：心肺。關：脾胃。尺：腎）以及三焦（寸：上焦。關：中焦。尺：下焦）加以評估。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第379頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 453,
      "question_en": "For the past two months 52 year-old female patient has had thickened and hardened skin on the hands and forearms. The thickened and hardened skin expanded from the hands to the skin above the wrist. She also reports her face feeling tight. One could observe puffed eyelids from edema. She reported having stiff hands and painful limb joints in the morning. Additional symptoms and signs include lack of strength with not even enough energy to have a conversation. She has lower back and leg pain after exertion and also after cloudy and rainy days. Upon further inquiry, she reported that during the summer she over relies on air-conditioning. The tongue was light red with a white-greasy coating. The pulse was deep-thready-weak. Immunological tests show the presence of antibodies related to scleroderma. Skin biopsy was positive for pathological changes found in scleroderma. What is the diagnosis for the acute symptoms?",
      "question_hant": "一名52歲女性患者近兩個月來雙手及前臂皮膚增厚變硬，硬化範圍由手部擴展至腕部上方皮膚。並訴顏面緊繃感，可觀察到眼瞼因水腫而浮腫。晨起時手部僵硬，四肢關節疼痛。此外，患者感覺乏力，甚至無足夠精力進行交談。運動後及陰雨天時腰腿疼痛加劇。經進一步詢問得知，患者夏季常過度依賴冷氣。舌質淡紅，苔白膩。脈沉細弱。免疫學檢查顯示存在與硬皮病相關之抗體。皮膚切片檢查亦顯示符合硬皮病之病理變化。此患者急性期症狀應診斷為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "deficiency of Spleen and Kidneys",
          "hant": "脾腎兩虛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "skin bi-syndrome due to cold",
          "hant": "寒邪所致皮痹",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "deficient qi with accumulation of dampness",
          "hant": "氣虛兼濕邪內蘊",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "skin bi-syndrome due to cold-damp",
          "hant": "寒濕所致皮痹",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "TCM does not have named disease for scleroderma. Based on the clinical picture, however, it can be viewed as a skin bi-syndrome (joint pain and thickened skin). It can also be viewed as vessel bi-syndrome (skin color changes, abnormal blood flow). Vessel bi corresponds to Raynaud's syndrome, which 90% of of scleroderma patients also have. In limited scleroderma the thickening of tissues mainly affects the skin while in diffused scleroderma not only is the skin affected but also internal organs, joints, bones or muscles. In TCM a deficiency in the upright qi of the Spleen (transforms food into qi), Kidneys transforms water, secretes clear fluid, directs turbidity down), and Lungs (spreads fluids and nourishes skin and hair) is the internal root cause for scleroderma. When these three zang organs are weakened, there will be an internal accumulation of phlegm-damp which will enter the ying and blood levels. This will result in blood stasis that obstructs the skin, internal organs, and the channels. In turn, blood stasis will further block the flow of body fluids which will increase the damp-phlegm lodging in the tissues which will manifest as a local and diffused swelling. When the underlying phlegm-dampness and blood stasis persist there will be a hardening of tissue. From a TCM point of view, the underlying pathology of scleroderma involves upright qi deficiency combined with the of damp-phlegm and blood stasis. These pathogenic factor are there even though there may not be obvious symptoms and signs other than they concentrate as a thickening of the skin and/or the internal organs. This patient has an acute case of skin bi-syndrome obstruction due to cold-damp due to prolonged cold exposure to air-conditioning combined with external summer dampness. These pathogenic factor disrupt the circulation of qi, body fluids, and blood which result in the thickening of the skin. It is the deficiency of upright qi (lack of energy, pain after exertion, deep-thready-weak pulse) that allows the pathogenic factors of dampness (pain worse with rain, white-greasy-coating) to enter the body to affect blood flow (blood stasis) and body fluids (phlegm formation) to thicken the skin. The diagnosis for the acute symptoms is skin bi-syndrome due to obstruction of cold and dampness. The treatment principle is to Disperse cold, Resolve dampness, Unblock the collaterals, Remove phlegm and blood stasis. After there is resolution of the acute symptoms. The root patterns in scleroderma cases are a yang deficiency of the Spleen and Kidneys. Once the acute symptoms resolve the treatment can also include boosting upright qi by strengthening the Spleen and warming the Kidney yang. Scleroderma is a condition that is difficult to treat. TCM Case Studies: Autoimmune Disease, Sheng-ping, Fratkin, and Jing, 2014, page 55-58",
      "exp_hant": "中醫並無與硬皮病完全對應之病名。然而依臨床表現，可將其視為皮痹（關節疼痛與皮膚增厚）。亦可視為脈痹（皮膚顏色改變、血行異常）。脈痹對應雷諾氏症候群，約有九成硬皮病患者兼有此症候群。局限性硬皮病主要影響皮膚組織增厚，而瀰漫性硬皮病則不僅影響皮膚，亦波及內臟、關節、骨骼或肌肉。中醫認為，脾（運化水穀為氣）、腎（主水，分清別濁，通調水道下降）與肺（宣布津液，濡養皮毛）之正氣不足，為硬皮病之內在根本病因。當此三臟正氣虛弱時，體內便會蘊積痰濕，進而侵入營血層次，導致血瘀阻滯皮膚、內臟與經絡。血瘀又進一步阻礙津液運行，使痰濕更易滯留於組織中，形成局部或瀰漫性腫脹。當潛在的痰濕與血瘀持續存在，組織便會逐漸硬化。從中醫觀點來看，硬皮病的根本病機為正氣虛弱兼夾痰濕與血瘀。即使沒有明顯的其他症狀與體徵，這些病邪仍可能存在，僅表現為皮膚及／或內臟的增厚。此患者屬急性皮痹，因長期使用冷氣受寒，加上夏季外感濕邪，寒濕相合阻滯所致。這些病邪擾亂氣、津液與血液之運行，導致皮膚增厚。正是因為正氣不足（乏力、活動後疼痛加劇、脈沉細弱），使得濕邪（陰雨天疼痛加劇、舌苔白膩）得以入侵，影響血行（血瘀）與津液（痰濕形成），進而導致皮膚增厚。此急性期症狀之診斷為寒濕阻滯所致之皮痹。治療原則為散寒、化濕、通絡、袪痰化瘀。待急性症狀緩解後，硬皮病之根本證型為脾腎陽虛。急性症狀緩解後，治療亦可加入健脾溫腎以扶助正氣。硬皮病是一種難以治療的疾病。《中醫案例研究：自體免疫疾病》，Sheng-ping、Fratkin與Jing合著，2014年，第55-58頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 454,
      "question_en": "Which Luo-Connecting channel treats the empty symptom of lower back ache?",
      "question_hant": "何條絡脈可治療虛證所致之腰痠？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Liver luo-connecting channel",
          "hant": "肝之絡脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Stomach luo-connecting channel",
          "hant": "胃之絡脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Spleen Luo-Connecting channel",
          "hant": "脾之絡脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Kidney luo-connecting channel",
          "hant": "腎之絡脈",
          "correct": true
        }
