      "exp_en": "The symptom is due to a deficiency in the channel. The Kidney luo-connecting channel begins at KI-4 on the posterior area of the medial malleolus, goes around the heel and internally enters to connect with the Bladder channel, ascends with the Kidney primary channel from KI-5 to an point below the Pericardium from where it goes posteriorly to and spread into the lumbar vertebrae. The point actions for KI-4 are to reinforce the Kidneys, anchor the qi and benefit the Lungs, and strengthen the will and dispels fear. Luo points treat disorders of their interior-exterior related channel or zang fu. KI-4 treats retention of urine, difficult urination, lumbar pain. Luo points treat disorders in areas reached by the luo-connecting channel. KI-4 treats palpitations, agitation, and restlessness through its connection to the Pericardium. Luo points can treat psychological and emotional disorders. KI-4 treats dementia, mental retardation, somnolence, propensity to anger, fright fear and unhappiness, desire to close the door and stay inside. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804; 2005 Edition, page 760; A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 40, 41, 332, 342; Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 250, 258",
