          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Spleen Qi Deficiency. ETIOLOGY: 1) excess intake of cold-raw foods or irregular eating habits or a non-nourishing diet can weaken the Spleen. 2) emotional stress (worry and pensiveness) can weaken the Spleen. 3) excess and chronic exposure to environmental Dampness can weaken the Spleen. 4) a chronic illness can weaken the Spleen. PRECURSORS TO PATTERN: as Spleen qi xu is a first-pattern there are not many precursors but a Lung qi xu can develop to include Spleen qi xu. PATTERN DEVELOPMENT: 1) Damp and/or Phlegm formation. 2) Blood xu. 3) Spleen yang xu. 4) Spleen qi sinking. 5) Spleen not holding Blood. 6) Heart qi and/or Blood xu. 7) Lung qi xu. 8) Kidney yang xu. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 599; 2005 Edition, page 568; 1989 Edition, page 242",
      "exp_hant": "脾氣虛。病因：一、過食生冷食物、飲食不規律或營養不足皆可耗弱脾氣。二、情志因素（憂思）可耗弱脾。三、長期過度接觸環境濕邪可耗弱脾。四、久病可耗弱脾。前驅證型：由於脾氣虛屬原發證型，故前驅證型不多，但肺氣虛可進一步發展而兼見脾氣虛。證型發展：一、濕聚及／或痰生。二、血虛。三、脾陽虛。四、脾氣下陷。五、脾不統血。六、心氣及／或心血虛。七、肺氣虛。八、腎陽虛。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第599頁；2005年版，第568頁；1989年版，第242頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 468,
      "question_en": "A 55 year-old patient complains of often feeling hot. She reports having a dry mouth and throat, dry stools and scanty dark urine. She reports mental restlessness, burning epigastric pain and a strong appetite. She reports feeling very feverish in the afternoon. She says that she has been taking her temperature. You ask if her temperature is over 100.4 degrees F. A \"yes\" answer to this question indicates that her symptoms are most likely due to",
      "question_hant": "一名55歲患者主訴常感發熱，口乾咽乾，大便乾結，小便短赤。自訴心神不寧、胃脘灼痛，食慾旺盛。並訴午後發熱明顯。患者表示自己有量體溫的習慣，你詢問其體溫是否超過華氏100.4度（攝氏38度）。若答案為「是」，則其症狀最可能是由下列何者所致？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Empty-Fire",
          "hant": "虛火",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Deficient Yin",
          "hant": "陰虛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Wind-Heat",
          "hant": "風熱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Stomach-Heat",
          "hant": "胃熱",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Asking about cold or hot feelings and fever is one of the 10 traditional diagnostic questions. One needs to differentiate hot and cold sensations arising from either interior conditions or exterior conditions. This question focuses on Cold and Hot interior conditions. The clinical picture can point to a Stomach-Heat pattern. The average body temperature is 98.6 F (37 C). A body temperature reading above 100.4 F is considered a true fever in adults. A hot flash due to a Deficient Yin with Empty-Fire should not cause the core body temperature to rise above normal. HOT INTERIOR conditions differentiate into Full Heat patterns and Empty Heat patterns. The clinical picture in FULL HEAT includes sudden onset, hot body sensations, thirst, red face, dry stools, scanty dark urine, a rapid full pulse, and a red tongue with a yellow coating. The clinical picture in EMPTY HEAT includes a gradual onset, feeling of heat in the afternoon, evening or middle of the night, dryness in the mouth with drinking small sips, a hot feeling in the chest, palms, and soles, dry stools, scanty dark urine, a floating-empty pulse and a red tongue without a coating. COLD INTERIOR conditions differentiate into Full Cold patterns and Empty Cold patterns. FULL COLD: A full external Cold pathogenic factor entering the body has a sudden onset, strong sensations of cold with shivering, pain, with the skin feeling cold to the touch and the pulse is of an excess type. In Stomach Full Cold the limbs and epigastrium often feel cold to the touch. In Intestines Full Cold, the legs and lower abdomen feel cold to the touch. If the Full Cold is located in the Uterus, the lower abdomen feels cold. In Qi Stasis, the feet and hands are cold but particularly the fingers. If the Full Cold persists for many months it can harm the Yang Qi and transform to Empty Cold. EMPTY COLD: Arising from Yang Deficiency, Empty Cold has a gradual onset, has mild cold feelings, the skin is mildly cold to the touch, and the pulse is of a deficient type. Deficient Yang of the Heart or Lung can manifest as cold and sweaty hands. Deficient Yang of the Stomach and Spleen can manifest as cold limbs and abdomen. Deficient Yang of the Kidneys can manifest as coldness in the feet, knees, legs and lower back. In Deficient Heart Blood, there is cold hands and cold chest. In Deficient Liver Blood, there is cold feet. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 456, 457, 662",
      "exp_hant": "詢問寒熱感覺及發熱與否，是傳統十問之一。臨床上需區分寒熱感覺究竟源於裡證或表證，此題聚焦於裡證之寒熱。此臨床表現可指向胃熱證。人體平均體溫約為華氏98.6度（攝氏37度）。成人體溫超過華氏100.4度（攝氏38度）方屬真正發熱。因陰虛虛火所致之潮熱，通常不會使核心體溫真正升高超過正常範圍。裡熱證可分為實熱與虛熱兩型。實熱之臨床表現為起病急驟、身熱、口渴、面赤、大便乾結、小便短赤、脈數而實、舌紅苔黃。虛熱之臨床表現則為起病緩慢、午後或夜間發熱感、口乾但只喜少量飲水、胸中及手足心發熱、大便乾結、小便短赤、脈浮虛、舌紅無苔。裡寒證則可分為實寒與虛寒兩型。實寒：外感寒邪之實證起病急驟，畏寒明顯並伴顫抖、疼痛，皮膚觸之發冷，脈屬實脈。胃實寒者，四肢與胃脘觸之常覺冷；腸實寒者，下肢與小腹觸之覺冷；若實寒位於胞宮，則小腹覺冷；氣滯者，手足發冷，尤以手指為甚。實寒若持續數月未癒，可損傷陽氣而轉化為虛寒。虛寒：因陽虛所致，起病緩慢，畏寒感較輕微，皮膚觸之略冷，脈屬虛脈。心陽或肺陽虛可見手冷汗出；脾胃陽虛可見四肢與腹部發冷；腎陽虛可見足、膝、腿及腰部發冷。心血虛則手冷、胸部發冷；肝血虛則足冷。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第456、457、662頁"
    },
