      "exp_en": "The Chinese character for Yi can also mean \"idea\". The Spleen houses the Yi (Intellect). The Yi has the functions of studying, memorizing, applied thinking, concentrating, and generating ideas. When the Spleen is healthy in Postnatal Qi and Blood, then thinking is clear, concentration is consistent, and there is the ability to study and memorize. When the Spleen function of transformation and transportation are in disorder leading to a lack in Qi and Blood generation, then the Yi will be dull with difficulty studying, memorizing, and focusing. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 272-273",
      "exp_hant": "「意」這個中文字亦可解作「想法」之意。脾藏意。意具有學習、記憶、運用思考、專注與產生想法等功能。當脾之後天氣血充盛健旺時，思緒清晰、專注力持續，並具備學習與記憶的能力。當脾之運化功能失調，導致氣血生成不足時，意便會遲鈍，出現學習、記憶與專注上的困難。《中醫臨床學》，Maciocia，2008年，第272-273頁"
