      "exp_en": "Kidney-jing, Kidney-yin, Kidney-yang, and Kidney-qi are intimately related. Kidney-jing transforms Kidney-yin into Kidney-qi through the fire of Kidney-yang. The image is that the Kidneys are like a big pot or cauldron full of water. The water is Kidney-jing and Kidney-yin as the jing is fluid-like. The fire under the pot is Kidney-yang and Ming Men. And the steam is Kidney-qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 48; 2005 Edition, page 46; 1989 Edition, page 40",
      "exp_hant": "腎精、腎陰、腎陽與腎氣四者關係密切。腎精藉由腎陽之火，將腎陰轉化為腎氣。可將腎比擬為一個裝滿水的大鍋：水即為腎精與腎陰，因精本身具有如水般的流動特性；鍋下之火即為腎陽與命門；而蒸氣則為腎氣。《中醫基礎學》，Maciocia，2015年，第48頁；2005年版，第46頁；1989年版，第40頁"
    },
    {
      "number": 491,
      "question_en": "Which of the following patterns is associated with an insufficient coming and going of the Hun?",
      "question_hant": "下列何種證型與魂的往來不足有關？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
