          "key": "A",
          "en": "Phlegm-Fire",
          "hant": "痰火",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Liver Yin Deficiency",
          "hant": "肝陰虛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Liver qi deficiency",
          "hant": "肝氣虛",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Heat or Fire patterns",
          "hant": "熱證或火證",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The patterns associated with an insufficient coming and going of the Hun are Liver Qi Stasis, Liver Blood Deficiency, Spleen and Kidney Yang Deficiency, and Liver Qi Deficiency. The common understanding is that the Liver Qi cannot be deficient. However, Liver Qi Deficiency is an emotional pattern associated with depression. The normal flow of Liver qi is to freely flow in all directions. The normal flow of Liver Qi also has an ascending direction. An important aspect of the ascending direction of the Liver qi is that it ascends to the Heart and Mind (Shen). This ascending Liver Qi is a way in which the Liver affects the coming and going of the Mind. A deficient Liver Qi indicates a failure of the Liver qi to ascend to the Mind resulting in depression. Heat and Fire patterns overstimulate the coming and going of the Mind. In Liver Blood and Liver Yin deficiencies the Hun fails to anchor itself in the Liver resulting in agitation of the Mind. Other patterns associated with the insufficient coming and going of the Mind include Liver Qi Stasis and Spleen and Kidney Yang Deficiency. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 263",
      "exp_hant": "與魂的往來不足相關的證型包括肝氣鬱結、肝血虛、脾腎陽虛，以及肝氣虛。一般的理解是肝氣不會虛，然而肝氣虛其實是一種與抑鬱相關的情志證型。肝氣的正常運行是能自由地向四方疏泄，其正常運行亦具有上升的方向性。肝氣上升的一個重要面向，是它會上升至心與神。這種肝氣的上升，正是肝影響神之往來的方式之一。肝氣虛則表示肝氣未能上升至神，因而導致抑鬱。熱證與火證則會過度刺激神的往來。在肝血虛與肝陰虛中，魂無法安藏於肝，因而導致神的躁動不安。其他與神之往來不足相關的證型還包括肝氣鬱結與脾腎陽虛。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 263"
