      "exp_en": "The Po (Corporal Soul) is the spiritual aspect of the Lungs. The Po comes into being three days after conception. The Hun of the mother nourishes the Essence and Hun of the fetus. The Po helps shape the body. The Po has a centripetal, separating, and aggregating force that materializes the fetus. As the skin is the boundary of the body, we can see the connection between the Po, the Lungs, and the skin. Further, the Po is the organizing and coordinating energy for all physiological processes. The Po also gives the body the ability to move, agility, balance, and movement coordination. After death, the Po remains with the body, especially in the bones, before returning to earth. Ancient Chinese culture had the ritual of looking after the bones of the dead. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 265",
      "exp_hant": "魄是肺的神志面向。魄於受孕後三天即已形成。母親的魂滋養胎兒的精與魂。魄協助形塑身體，具有向心、分離與凝聚的力量，使胎兒得以具體成形。由於皮膚是身體的邊界，我們可以看出魄、肺與皮膚三者之間的連結。此外，魄也是統籌協調一切生理活動的能量。魄同時賦予身體活動、靈敏、平衡與動作協調的能力。人死之後，魄仍會留在體內，尤其是骨骼之中，之後才逐漸歸於大地。古代中國文化中即有妥善安葬並照看亡者骸骨的習俗。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 265"
