      "exp_en": "When pulse diagnosis reveals that there is an imbalance within the yin and yang channels of the same element, the luo-connecting points are selected to transfer the excess energy from the strong channel to the weak channel. In this case, the yin Metal channel (Lungs, +2 deep inch position) is in excess while the yang Metal channel (Large Intestine, -1 superficial inch position) is deficient. Always choose the luo-connecting point in the deficient channel to transfer the excess energy. In this case it would the luo point in the yang Large Intestine Metal channel, LI-6. Clinical Manual Integrating Five Element Acupuncture with Traditional Chinese Medicine, Silverstein, 2015, page 120",
