      "exp_en": "The six Extraordinary Yang organs are the Uterus, Brain, Bones, Marrow, Gall Bladder, and Blood Vessels. They are extraordinary because they store substances (marrow, bile, blood, etc) similar to the yin organs and are hollow like the yang organs. There is no such thing as the Extraordinary Yin Organs. The Extraordinary Vessels do not have a direct connection or association with the zang fu. The Extraordinary Vessels indirectly connect to the zang fu through the Kidneys which are the source of yin and yang of all the zang fu. However, the Extraordinary Vessels all have a direct relationship to the Extraordinary Yang organs. The Brain is associated with the Governing and Yin-Yang Stepping Vessels. The Uterus is associated with the Penetrating and Directing Vessels. The Blood Vessels are associated with the Penetrating Vessel. The Gall Bladder is associated with the Girdle Vessel. The Bones are associated with the Penetrating, Governing, and Directing Vessels. Marrow is associated with the Governing and Penetrating Vessels. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 235, 871-872",
      "exp_hant": "六個奇恆之腑為子宮、腦、骨、髓、膽、脈。之所以稱為「奇恆」，是因為它們如陰臟一般儲藏精微物質（髓、膽汁、血等），但形態上卻如陽腑一般中空。並沒有所謂的「奇恆之陰臟」。奇經八脈與臟腑之間並無直接的連結或關聯，而是透過腎（一身陰陽之根本）間接與臟腑相連。然而，奇經八脈皆與奇恆之腑具有直接的關係：腦與督脈及陰陽蹻脈相關；子宮與衝脈及任脈相關；脈與衝脈相關；膽與帶脈相關；骨與衝脈、督脈及任脈相關；髓與督脈及衝脈相關。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 235, 871-872"
