      ],
      "exp_en": "The WIRY PULSE is a type of full pulse. It feels superficial and hard and can be clearly palpated at the deep and middle levels. The pulse hits the fingers with force and feels like a guitar string so that when you try to push it down it wants to spring up. The wiry pulse indicates full type of Liver disorders such as stuck Liver qi or Blood, Liver Yang Rising, Liver Fire, Liver Wind. It can also indicate Phlegm or chronic pain. It is often felt in elderly patients. The LEATHER PULSE is an empty type of pulse. This pulse is felt superficially and feels like a stretched skin of a drum but at the deep level it is empty. On the outside the pulse feels hard but empty on the inside. The leather pulse indicates severe deficiency of Blood, Essence, or yin. The SOGGY PULSE is palpated only on the superficial level. It is like a wet cotton wool that disappears when more pressure is applied. This pulse also goes by the name of weak-floating pulse. The soggy pulse indicates chronic qi xu with Dampness retention. The FIRM PULSE is an excess type of pulse. It is palpated only at the deep level, feels hard full, wiry, and long. It is a wiry pulse only at the middle and deep levels whereas a true wiry pulse is palpated at all three levels. The firm pulse indicates inner Cold that can be associated with old pain. It can also mean inner accumulation of stuck qi or Blood. Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 497",
      "exp_hant": "弦脈屬實脈的一種，觸感浮硬，於中、沉兩部皆可清楚觸及。此脈搏動有力，如按琴弦一般，按之欲彈起。弦脈提示肝的實證，如肝氣或肝血鬱滯、肝陽上亢、肝火、肝風等，亦可提示痰或久痛，年長患者常見此脈。革脈屬虛脈的一種，浮取時如按鼓皮般繃緊，但沉取則空虛無力，外硬而內空。革脈提示血、精或陰的嚴重虧虛。濡脈僅於浮取時可觸及，如濕棉絮一般，稍加重按即消失不見，此脈又稱弱浮脈。濡脈提示久病氣虛兼夾濕邪停滯。牢脈屬實脈的一種，僅於沉取時可觸及，觸感硬、實、弦而長。牢脈僅在中、沉兩部呈現弦象，而真正的弦脈則於浮、中、沉三部皆可觸及。牢脈提示內寒，並可能與久痛相關，亦可提示內有氣血鬱結積聚。Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 497"
    },
