      "exp_en": "Limb contractions occur when there is an involuntary clenching of the fists or fingers. A foot contraction is due to a rigidity of the leg with an inability to stretch the leg. Contractions can occur on the fingers, wrists, elbows, ankles, and knees. Dupuytren's contracture is an example occurring at the ring and little finger. Contractions due to Qi and Blood xu are mild with associated symptoms of tiredness, pale tongue, and a choppy or weak pulse. Contractions due to Liver Wind are pronounced and associated with vertigo and a wiry pulse. This can be seen after an attack of wind-stroke. Contractions due to Cold are pronounced and associated with pain, feeling cold, and improvement with heat. Cold particularly affects the knees or elbows. Contractions due to Dampness are associated with swelling and feeling heavy. Dampness particularly affects the wrist. Contractions due to Phlegm are associated with joint swelling and bone deformities. Phlegm can be seen combining with Cold or Dampness in later stages of bi-syndrome where bone deformities can occur. Contractions due to Blood stasis are associated with joint rigidity, severe pain, and a purplish tongue. This can be seen in later states of bi-syndrome. Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 63, 64",
      "exp_hant": "肢體攣縮是指手指或手掌不自主地緊握蜷曲。足部攣縮則是因小腿僵硬而無法伸展。攣縮可發生於手指、手腕、肘部、踝部及膝部。杜普伊特倫氏攣縮即為發生於無名指與小指的一例。因氣血兩虛所致的攣縮程度較輕，並伴隨疲倦、舌淡、脈澀或脈弱等症狀。因肝風所致的攣縮則較為明顯，並伴有眩暈及弦脈，此可見於中風發作之後。因寒邪所致的攣縮亦較明顯，並伴有疼痛、畏寒，得熱則減，寒邪尤其易侵犯膝部或肘部。因濕邪所致的攣縮則伴有腫脹及身體沈重感，濕邪尤其易侵犯腕部。因痰所致的攣縮則伴有關節腫脹及骨骼變形，痰在痺證後期可與寒或濕相合，導致骨骼變形。因血瘀所致的攣縮則伴有關節僵硬、劇痛及舌質紫暗，此可見於痺證的後期階段。Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 63, 64"
