      "exp_en": "A white coating in almost, but not all situations points to a cold pattern (deficiency/excess, exterior/interior). In an external pathogen invading the body, the white coating indicates that the pathogen is still located in the superficial energetic layers and has yet to penetrate to the interior. A white coating reflects the state of health of the Lungs and Large Intestine. In conjunction with other symptoms, a white coating on stiff tongue is a reflection of an excess pattern in the Lung and Large Intestine. A white-dry tongue coating reflects Large Intestine dryness. In contrast, the three main clinical interpretations for a yellow tongue coating are heat, interior, and Stomach-Spleen disorder. A yellow coating indicates heat (deficiency/excess, exterior/interior). In acute wind-cold, a yellow coating is usually interpreted to mean that the disease has moved to the interior (except for wind-heat, summer-heat, and external dryness). If during the course of a chronic and non-external disease, the tongue coating becomes yellow it indicates an interior disorder. A thick-yellow coating indicates an excess Stomach-Spleen disorder. Tongue Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1995, page 104, 108",
      "exp_hant": "白苔幾乎（但並非絕對）皆顯示寒證（可虛可實、可表可裡）。外邪侵襲人體時，白苔顯示邪氣仍停留於較表淺的能量層次，尚未深入於裡。白苔反映了肺與大腸的健康狀態。配合其他症狀，僵硬舌上的白苔反映肺與大腸的實證。白而乾的舌苔則反映大腸燥結。相對地，黃苔的三種主要臨床意義則是熱、裡證及脾胃病。黃苔顯示熱證（可虛可實、可表可裡）。在急性風寒證中，黃苔通常被解讀為病邪已傳裡（風熱、暑熱及外感燥邪則例外）。若在慢性、非外感病的病程中舌苔轉黃，則顯示為裡證。厚黃苔則顯示脾胃實證。Tongue Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1995, page 104, 108"
