          "en": "Does the headache mostly occur during the day?",
          "hant": "頭痛是否大多發生於白天？",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Asking about the head and body is one of the 10 traditional diagnostic questions. In enquiring about headaches you are assessing onset, time of day, location, type of pain, and aggravation. ONSET: a recent and short duration headache can be due to wind-cold or short-term Qi stasis. A gradual onset is most likely due to an internal disorder. TIME OF DAY: if there are other confirming symptoms, headaches during the day are more likely due to Deficient Qi or Yang, during the evening most likely due to Deficient Blood or Yin and night time pain can be due to Blood Stasis. LOCATION: nape of neck is associated with Tai Yang channels, forehead with Yang Ming channels, temples and sides with Shao Yang channels, vertex with Shao Yin channels, the whole head rather than the sides due to Liver Wind. TYPE OF PAIN: if there are other confirming symptom, a heavy sensation is most likely due to Phlegm or Dampness, a distending or throbbing sensation is most likely due to Hyperactive Liver Yang, a boring or sharp pain is most likely due to Blood Stasis. AGGRAVATION: headaches worsening with cold is most likely due to a Cold patter, worsening with heat due to a Heat pattern, worsening with fatigue and improve with rest is due to Deficient Qi, worsening with stress is most likely due to Hyperactive Liver Yang and worsening with sexual activity is most likely due to a Kidney Deficiency. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 349; The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, Second Edition page 34",
      "exp_hant": "詢問頭身情況是中醫十問之一。在詢問頭痛時，需評估發病時間、發作時段、部位、疼痛性質及加重因素。發病時間：近期且病程短的頭痛可能因風寒或短暫的氣滯所致；漸進發病則多因內傷所致。發作時段：若配合其他佐證症狀，白天發作的頭痛多因氣虛或陽虛所致，傍晚發作多因血虛或陰虛所致，夜間疼痛則可能因血瘀所致。部位：後頸部與太陽經相關，前額與陽明經相關，兩側及太陽穴與少陽經相關，頭頂與少陰經相關，若非侷限於兩側而是整個頭部，則多與肝風有關。疼痛性質：若配合其他佐證症狀，沉重感多因痰或濕所致，脹痛或搏動性疼痛多因肝陽上亢所致，鑽痛或刺痛則多因血瘀所致。加重因素：遇寒加重多屬寒證，遇熱加重多屬熱證，因疲勞加重、休息可緩解則屬氣虛，因壓力加重多因肝陽上亢，因房事加重則多因腎虛。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 349; The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, Second Edition page 34"
