      "exp_en": "The 10 traditional diagnostic questions include 1. feelings of cold/heat, 2. sweating, 3. head and body, 4. chest and abdomen, 5. food and taste, 6. stools and urine, 7. sleep, 8. hearing and tinnitus, 9. thirst and drink, and 10. pain. Eventually two other areas of enquiry were added to the 10 traditional questions: children and women. This makes it a total of 12 diagnostic questions. Asking diagnosis in regards to children is similar to that of adults except that it is mostly the parents who will provide the information. Four areas of children enquiry include: digestion, respiratory and ears, sleep and, more recently, immunizations. In this case, a barking cough with sticky-yellow sputum is enough to diagnose Lung Phlegm-Heat. RESPIRATORY: Children can easily be invaded by external Wind, Heat or Dampness resulting in an acute respiratory disorder. When a child has a recurring chronic cough and wheezing (often due to Lung Phlegm-Heat after an external pathogenic Wind invasion), chronic earaches (often due to Gall Bladder Channel Damp-Heat) or chronic runny noses or catarrh (often due to a combo of pathogenic Wind and Spleen Deficiency causing Phlegm). Recurrent coughs, wheezing, earaches and catarrh are often associated with acute external pathogenic Wind episodes treated with the frequent use of antibiotics. The use of the antibiotics can lead to the pathogenic factor entering deeper into the body and remaining in a latent and residual state that can be reactivated. DIGESTION: Abdominal pain is most often due to Cold Retention in the Stomach-Intestines or Qi Stasis in the Intestines. Babies can have abdominal pain due to food retention manifesting as vomiting of milk and colic. Colic is frequent, prolonged and intense crying or fussiness in an infant. SLEEP: Loud crying babies with disturbed sleep is most often due to Food Retention and Stomach-Heat. For older children the most common causes are Food Retention, Stomach-Heat or Liver-Fire. IMMUNIZATION: Immunizations affecting the health of a child, needs to be seen from the perspective of the Four Levels. Vaccines contain weakened bacteria or viruses. From a TCM perspective, vaccines bypass the Wei, Qi and Ying levels. They put the external pathogenic factor directly into the deepest Xue or Blood level. This can result in short-term Latent Heat effects at the Blood Level (skin rashes, sleep disturbance, and temporary personality changes) or can have long-term Latent Heat effects that can manifest later (chronic wheezing and cough, allergies, skin disorders, autism). In Western medicine, the long-term effects of vaccinations are considered controversial. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 370, 371, 589",
      "exp_hant": "中醫傳統十問包括：一、寒熱；二、汗；三、頭身；四、胸腹；五、飲食口味；六、二便；七、睡眠；八、耳聾耳鳴；九、口渴與飲水；十、疼痛。其後又加入兩個問診範疇：小兒與婦女，因此總共成為十二問。對小兒問診的方式與成人類似，只是多半由家長提供資訊。小兒問診的四大範疇包括：消化、呼吸系統與耳部、睡眠，以及近年新增的疫苗接種。本案例中，聲如犬吠的咳嗽並帶黏黃痰，即足以診斷肺痰熱。呼吸系統：兒童容易受到外感風、熱或濕邪的侵襲，導致急性呼吸道病症。當兒童反覆出現慢性咳嗽及喘鳴（多因外感風邪後轉為肺痰熱所致）、慢性耳痛（多因膽經濕熱所致），或慢性流涕及鼻涕倒流（多因風邪與脾虛生痰相合所致）時，這些反覆發作的咳嗽、喘鳴、耳痛及鼻涕，往往與急性外感風邪發作經常使用抗生素治療有關。抗生素的使用可能導致病邪深入體內，並以潛伏殘留的狀態滯留，日後可能再度被誘發。消化：腹痛最常見的原因是胃腸寒邪滯留或腸道氣滯。嬰兒也可能因食積而出現腹痛，表現為吐奶及腸絞痛。腸絞痛是指嬰兒頻繁、持續且劇烈的哭鬧或煩躁不安。睡眠：嬰兒大聲哭鬧並伴有睡眠不安，最常見的原因是食積及胃熱。年紀較大的兒童，最常見的原因則是食積、胃熱或肝火。疫苗接種：疫苗對兒童健康的影響，需從衛氣營血四層的角度來理解。疫苗含有減毒的細菌或病毒。從中醫的角度來看，疫苗會繞過衛、氣、營三層，直接將外邪置入最深的血分。這可能導致血分的短期伏熱效應（皮疹、睡眠不安、暫時性性情改變），也可能造成日後才顯現的長期伏熱效應（慢性喘鳴與咳嗽、過敏、皮膚病、自閉症）。在西醫觀點中，疫苗接種的長期影響仍存在爭議。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 370, 371, 589"
    },
