      "question_en": "Three days ago, a six-year old boy started having fever with a slight aversion to cold and a sore throat. His mother took his body temperature and it was 100 F. He also had dryness in the skin, nose, mouth, throat, and tongue. He occasionally had a cough but without any expectoration. His symptoms have changed. When his mother brought him for treatment his body temperature was 104 F. He was thirsty, was sweating, and he said he felt too hot and wanted to go without any shirt on. His cough worsened. He had a rash on his face and hands with red, solid, itchy spots. His tongue was red with yellow coating and the pulse was rapid. Based on the Four Levels differentiation what is the progression of the disease?",
      "question_hant": "三天前，一名六歲男孩開始發熱，微惡寒，並有咽喉痛。他的母親為他量體溫，為華氏100度。他也出現皮膚、鼻、口、咽喉及舌的乾燥。偶有咳嗽，但無痰咳出。其症狀其後發生變化：當母親帶他就診時，體溫已升至華氏104度，他感到口渴、汗出，自述感覺過熱並想脫去上衣。咳嗽加重，臉部及手部出現紅色、堅實、搔癢的皮疹。舌紅苔黃，脈數。依衛氣營血辨證，此病的傳變過程為何？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "wei qi level wind-heat → qi level Lung-Heat",
          "hant": "衛分風熱 → 氣分肺熱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "wei qi level wind-heat → qi level Stomach-Heat",
          "hant": "衛分風熱 → 氣分胃熱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "wei qi level dry-heat → qi level Stomach-Heat",
          "hant": "衛分燥熱 → 氣分胃熱",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "wei qi level dry-heat → qi level Lung-Heat",
          "hant": "衛分燥熱 → 氣分肺熱",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The first clinical presentation is dry-heat at the wei qi level. Because it is a the wei qi level there is some aversion to cold. The difference between the wei qi level dry-heat and wei qi level wind-heat is that the former is due to the presence of symptoms of dryness injuring the body fluids (dry skin, dry nose, dry mouth, dry throat, dry tongue). In both patterns the heat produces a sore throat and a floating-rapid pulse. For Lung-Heat at the qi level there is as in all qi level patterns fever, feeling, hot, sweating, and thirst. When the Heat injures the descending function of Lung qi there is coughing and there can also be shortness of breath. Four Levels warm diseases often produce rashes. Heat at the qi level (Lung-Heat or Stomach-Heat) can be associated with skin rashes called papules which are red and solid spots. This can occur with measles and chicken pox. When the Heat at the qi level is associated with dampness (Spleen-Stomach Damp-Heat) there can be vesicles which are blister-like spots filled with clear fluid. At the Nutritive-Qi and Blood level there can be macules which are red spots/splotches under the skin. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 770, 772, 773",
      "exp_hant": "最初的臨床表現為衛分燥熱。因屬衛分階段，故仍有輕微惡寒。衛分燥熱與衛分風熱的差別在於，前者出現燥邪傷津的症狀（皮膚乾燥、鼻乾、口乾、咽乾、舌乾）。兩證中，熱邪皆會導致咽喉痛及浮數脈。氣分肺熱與所有氣分證相同，皆會出現發熱、自覺發熱、汗出及口渴。當熱邪損傷肺氣的肅降功能時，便會出現咳嗽，亦可能伴有氣短。衛氣營血辨證中的溫病常會產生皮疹。氣分熱（肺熱或胃熱）可伴隨稱為「疹」的皮膚疹點，其特徵為紅色、堅實的斑點，可見於麻疹及水痘。當氣分熱兼夾濕邪（脾胃濕熱）時，可出現「疱」，即充滿清澈液體、如水泡般的疹點。至營血分階段，則可出現「斑」，即皮下的紅色斑點或斑塊。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 770, 772, 773"
    },
