      ],
      "exp_en": "Anatomically, the upper burner is from the diaphragm and up. The area between the navel and the diaphragm is the middle burner while the area below the navel is the lower burner.The upper burner has the Lungs, Heart, Pericardium, throat, and head. The middle burner has the Stomach, Spleen, and Gall Bladder. The lower burner has the Liver, Kidneys, Intestines, and Bladder. Anatomically the Liver is located in the middle burner where it manifests symptoms epigastric pain, belching, hypochondrial distention. The middle burner is mainly involved with the transformation and transportation of food essences. The Liver can influence this function but is not responsible for it. The Liver is placed in the lower burner because the Liver energetically influences the Uterus and the genital system. The Upper Burner is compared to a mist: it diffuses fine vapor fluids through the Lungs between the skin and muscles. The Middle Burner is compared to a maceration chamber or bubbling cauldron as a function of the Spleen and Stomach function of rotting-ripening foods and extracting food essences to be transported to the body. The Lower Burner is compared to a drainage ditch that separates food essences and water into clean and dirty parts and facilitates urine and stool excretion. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 224, 225",
      "exp_hant": "從解剖角度而言，上焦是指橫膈以上的部位。肚臍與橫膈之間的區域屬中焦，肚臍以下的區域則屬下焦。上焦包含肺、心、心包、咽喉及頭部；中焦包含胃、脾及膽；下焦包含肝、腎、腸及膀胱。從解剖位置而言，肝位於中焦，其病變可表現為胃脘痛、噯氣、脅肋脹滿等症狀。中焦主要負責水穀精微的運化與轉輸，肝雖可影響此功能，但並非負責此功能的臟腑。肝之所以被歸於下焦，是因為肝在能量上影響子宮及生殖系統。上焦的功能如霧一般，透過肺將精微的水氣佈散於皮膚與肌肉之間。中焦的功能如同漚漬之所或沸騰的鍋釜，即脾胃腐熟水穀、萃取水穀精微並轉輸至全身的功能。下焦的功能則如溝渠一般，將水穀精微與水液分為清濁兩部分，並促進大小便的排泄。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 224, 225"
    },
