        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. Anti-thyroid drugs are not associated with the pattern of Heart Blood Stasis. Anti-thyroid drugs are used to treat hyperthyroidism. In TCM hyperthyroidism is seen as due to yang repletion. As such these western drugs are posited to have the TCM classification of heat-clearing medicinals. The side effects of this class of western drugs includes fever, rash, lymphadenopathy, and susceptibility to infections. If the hyperthyroid medication clears too much heat it can cause qi vacuity where the central qi collapses downward causing depression or stagnation in the Lower Burner transforming into Heat which inflames the Life-Gate ministerial Fire which then floats upward causing qi vacuity fever and rashes. Frequent infections can be seen as a weakness in the wei or defensive qi. The lymphadenopathy (swollen lymph nodes) can be seen as phlegm nodules that result from a vacuity of Spleen qi unable to transform Fluids which then accumulates into Dampness. The vacuity heat from the qi vacuity fever can further congeal the accumulated Dampness into Phlegm nodules. Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 363",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且最正確的答案。抗甲狀腺藥物與心血瘀阻證並無關聯。抗甲狀腺藥物用於治療甲狀腺功能亢進。中醫認為甲亢乃因陽氣亢盛所致，故此類西藥被視為具有清熱藥的中醫屬性。此類西藥的副作用包括發熱、皮疹、淋巴結腫大，以及易感染。若抗甲亢藥物清熱過度，可導致氣虛，使中氣下陷，於下焦鬱結停滯，進而化熱，燻灼命門相火，相火上浮，遂見氣虛發熱與皮疹。反覆感染可視為衛氣虛弱之象。淋巴結腫大則可視為痰結，乃因脾氣虛弱不能運化水濕，水濕積聚所致；氣虛所生之虛熱又可進一步將積聚之濕濁凝結為痰核。Integrated Pharmacology, Sperber and Flaws, 2007, page 363"
    },
    {
      "number": 563,
      "question_en": "A patient has a sore and weak back, clear and frequent urination, weak urinary stream, dribbling after urination, feeling cold, incontinence, urination at night, nocturnal emission without dreams, and premature ejaculation, pale tongue, and deep-weak pulse in the rear position. What is the Kidney zang-fu pattern?",
      "question_hant": "患者腰部痠軟無力、小便清長頻數、尿線無力、尿後餘瀝、畏寒、遺尿、夜尿、無夢遺精、早洩，舌淡，尺脈沉弱。此為何種腎的臟腑證型？",
