      ],
      "exp_en": "Latent Heat happens when an external pathogenic factor penetrates the body without at first producing any of the apparent symptoms at the time of the invasion. The external pathogenic invasion (wind-cold or wind-heat) does not initially produce the characteristic external symptoms (aversion to cold, fever, body aches). What happens is that the external pathogen goes internal, incubates, and transforms into Heat which later manifests as acute symptoms of Heat that causes the patient to feel suddenly tired, have weary limbs, poor sleep, slightly thirsty, hot, and irritable. This is called Latent Heat and is one of the causes of Chronic Fatigue Syndrome (CFS). External pathogens can invade the body without producing any exterior symptoms. Often this is due to weak Kidneys. The Kidneys via the Essence and Original Qi play a role in protecting the body from external pathogens. Wei qi originates from the Kidneys (Essence and Original Q) and is transformed from Kidney Yang. Resistance to external pathogenic factors depends not only on the strength of the Lungs but also that of the Kidneys. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 55, 779; Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2nd Edition, page 1136",
      "exp_hant": "伏熱是指外邪侵入人體後，初期並未產生明顯症狀。外邪（風寒或風熱）侵襲之初，並未出現典型的表證（惡寒、發熱、身痛）。其後外邪內傳、潛伏、化熱，日後才表現出急性熱證症狀，令患者突然感到疲乏、四肢倦怠、睡眠不佳、口微渴、身熱、煩躁。此即所謂伏熱，為慢性疲勞症候群（CFS）病因之一。外邪可侵入人體而不產生任何表證，此常因腎虛所致。腎透過精與元氣，在防禦外邪方面發揮作用。衛氣源於腎（精與元氣），由腎陽所化生。抵禦外邪的能力不僅取決於肺氣的強弱，亦取決於腎氣的強弱。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 55, 779; Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2nd Edition, page 1136"
