      "exp_en": "Salivation is controlled by the Spleen. The mouth is the opening of the Spleen. Thus, the excess salivation, poor appetite, cloudy urine, unformed stools, pale tongue, and weak pulse all point to a deficient Spleen qi pattern. Because of the deficient Spleen, the Fluids were not properly transported and accumulated and traveled upward causing excess saliva. Because of congenital weakness, the patient had dull hair and preferred inactivity. Acupuncture Case Histories, Chen and Wang, 1988, page 287",
      "exp_hant": "涎液由脾所主。口為脾之竅。因此，流涎過多、食慾不佳、小便渾濁、大便不成形、舌淡、脈弱，皆指向脾氣虛之證。因脾氣虛弱，津液未能正常輸布，反而積聚並上溢，導致流涎過多。因先天稟賦不足，患者頭髮乾枯，且喜好靜而不喜動。Acupuncture Case Histories, Chen and Wang, 1988, page 287"
