      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. The suffix -afil refers to such drugs as Viagra (sildenafil). Hyperkalemia is an elevated level of potassium in the blood. Common symptoms of hyperkalemia include breathing difficulties, chest pain, irregular heartbeat, and muscle weakness. High blood pressure or heart disease prescription drugs interact with potassium-rich foods such as bananas. ACE INHIBITORS (-pril) such as lisinopril, Altace (ramipril), Vasotec (enalapril) and captopril and ARBs or Angiotensin II Receptor Blockers (-sartan) such as losartan (Cozaar), valsartan (Diovan), candesartan (Atacand) and telmisartan (Micardis) have the function of relaxing and dilating blood vessels, relaxing the heart, and improve circulation. ACE inhibitors and ARBs can increase potassium retention in the body that can elevate blood potassium that can lead to an irregular heart rhythm. Patients on these drugs should limit high-potassium foods (bananas, avocados, sweet/white potatoes, dried fruits). webmd.com",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且最正確的答案。字尾「-afil」是指如威而鋼（Viagra，sildenafil）之類的藥物。高血鉀症是指血液中鉀離子濃度升高。高血鉀症常見症狀包括呼吸困難、胸痛、心律不整，以及肌肉無力。治療高血壓或心臟病的處方藥物會與富含鉀的食物（如香蕉）產生交互作用。血管收縮素轉化酶抑制劑（ACE inhibitors，字尾-pril）如lisinopril、Altace（ramipril）、Vasotec（enalapril）及captopril，以及血管收縮素II受體阻斷劑（ARBs，字尾-sartan）如losartan（Cozaar）、valsartan（Diovan）、candesartan（Atacand）及telmisartan（Micardis），具有放鬆並擴張血管、放鬆心臟、改善血液循環之作用。ACE抑制劑與ARB類藥物可增加體內鉀滯留，進而升高血鉀濃度，導致心律不整。服用此類藥物的患者應限制高鉀食物（香蕉、酪梨、地瓜/馬鈴薯、乾果）。webmd.com"
