      "exp_en": "At the physiological level the Kidneys and the Heart communicate. At the psychological level the Zhi of the Kidneys is coordinated with the Shen of the Heart. The Zhi or Will-Power of the Kidneys provides the Shen or Mind of the Heart with drive, motivation, and determination in pursuing goals. The Shen (Mind) controls and directs the Zhi (Will-Power). When both the Zhi and Shen are strong, then the individual can pursue goals. On the other hand, if the Mind (Shen) is clear about its goals but the Zhi or Will-Power is weak, there will be a lack of determination to carry through on those goals. But if the Zhi is strong but the Shen is confused and unclear, then the Zhi will not be controlled and can become destructive. An example would be a 2-year old child with a strong determination (always saying no) having an immature Mind (Shen) or an adult with a strong determination (Zhi) with a weak or confused Shen resulting in reckless behavior and taking too many risks. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 274",
      "exp_hant": "於生理層面，心腎相交。於心理層面，腎之志須與心之神相協調。腎之志（意志力）為心之神（心神）提供追求目標的動力、動機與決心。神（心神）主宰並引導志（意志力）。當志與神皆強健時，個體便能追求目標。反之，若心神對目標明確，但志（意志力）薄弱，則會缺乏貫徹目標的決心。然而，若志堅強而神卻混亂不清，則志將失去掌控，甚或變得具破壞性。例如，一名意志堅定（總是說不）但心神尚未成熟的兩歲幼兒；或一名意志堅定（志）但心神混亂不清的成人，則會表現出魯莽行為並冒過多風險。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 274"
