      "exp_en": "The earliest observations of yin/yang must have come from the ancients observing the movement of the sun and moon, day and night. The day, brightness, and activity are yang while the night, darkness, and rest are yin. The ancients saw the cyclical movement of the day giving to night and night changing to day. As the sun rises in the East and sets in the West, the Eastern direction was categorized as yang and the western direction as yin. If one is in the northern hemisphere and face South, East will be on the left and West on the right. Thus, East = yang and West = yin. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 5; 2005 Edition, page 5; 1989 Edition, page 3",
      "exp_hant": "陰陽最早的觀察，應源於古人對日月運行、晝夜交替的觀察。白晝、光明與活動屬陽，夜晚、黑暗與靜息屬陰。古人觀察到晝轉為夜、夜轉為晝的循環規律。由於太陽從東方升起、西方落下，東方被歸類為陽，西方則歸類為陰。若人位於北半球面向南方，則東方在左、西方在右。因此，東方屬陽、西方屬陰。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 5; 2005 Edition, page 5; 1989 Edition, page 3"
    },
