      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. An ancient TCM text writes: \"if Liver Blood is deficient Fire agitates the Ethereal Soul resulting in nocturnal emissions with dreams.\". The Liver regulates the volume of Blood when the body is active or at rest. Liver Blood is released with activity and Blood returns to the Liver with rest. If this Blood volume regulating function of the Liver is impaired, the person can easily become tired with activities or unable to feel refreshed with rest. The Liver is affected by Wind and can result in migraines and neck stiffness. The Liver houses the hun (Ethereal Soul) which is responsible for the person to have life direction, goals, and vision. A weak Liver can manifest as an inability to plan. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 124; 2005 Edition, page 123-124; 1989 Edition, page 82",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確的答案。古代醫籍記載：「肝血虛則火擾魂，以致夢遺」。肝主調節人體動靜時的血量，活動時肝血釋出，靜息時血則歸於肝。若肝此種調節血量的功能受損，患者容易在活動後感到疲勞，或休息後仍無法恢復精神。肝易受風邪影響，可導致偏頭痛與頸部僵硬。肝藏魂，魂使人具備人生方向、目標與遠見。肝氣衰弱可表現為規劃能力不足。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 124; 2005 Edition, page 123-124; 1989 Edition, page 82"
