          "hant": "儲存與排泄膽汁",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Stomach is the origin of Body Fluids through its function of macerating food and liquids. In the context of fluids, the Stomach is the gate to the Kidneys and a deficiency of Body Fluids from the Stomach is the beginning of yin xu. If there are sufficient fluids in the Stomach then digestion, taste, and appetite will be normal. When Stomach fluids are low the patient will be thirsty, the tongue will be dry-cracked, and the digestion will be impaired. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 197; 2005 Edition, page 188; 1989 Edition, page 113",
      "exp_hant": "胃透過腐熟飲食水穀的功能，成為津液生成之源。就津液而言，胃為腎之關，胃津不足即為陰虛之始。若胃中津液充足，則消化、味覺與食慾皆正常。當胃津不足時，患者會感到口渴、舌乾裂，且消化功能受損。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 197; 2005 Edition, page 188; 1989 Edition, page 113"
    },
    {
      "number": 644,
      "question_en": "In TCM, Memory is associated with the",
      "question_hant": "在中醫理論中，記憶與下列何者相關？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Heart and Spleen",
          "hant": "心與脾",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "heart",
          "hant": "心",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Heart and Kidneys",
          "hant": "心與腎",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Heart, Spleen, and Kidneys",
          "hant": "心、脾與腎",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "When examining thinking, remembering, and memorization from a TCM perspective, there is a function overlap between the Yi (Spleen), Shen (Heart), and Zhi (Kidneys). Memory has two meanings. 1) memory is the capacity to memorize data when working or studying. 2) memory is the ability to remember past events. Both of these aspects of memory depend on the Heart-Mind and on the Spleen and Kidneys. With memory there is an overlap between the Yi of the Spleen, the Zhi of the Kidneys, and the Shen of the Heart. The Yi of the Spleen is responsible for memorizing data, studying, and concentration. The Heart and Kidneys are associated with the memory of past events (recent or long past). The Kidneys are associated with remembering recent events while the Heart is associated with remembering long-past events. A person can have an excellent memory (Yi) in their field of study but do poorly in remembering past events (Shen, and Zhi). There is a very close relationship between the Shen (Mind) of the Heart and the Yi (Intellect) of the Spleen and between the Yi and the Zhi (Will-Power) of the Kidneys. The Spiritual Axis writes that \"The Heart function of recollecting is called the Intellect\", \"The storing [data] of the Intellect is called Will-Power [Zhi]. Though Zhi is often translated as Will-Power, it also has the additional meanings of memory the Brain, as the Sea of Marrow, also controls memory, intelligence, and concentration. The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 246, 273; The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 150, 240",
      "exp_hant": "從中醫角度探討思考、回憶與記憶時，脾之意、心之神與腎之志三者的功能有所重疊。記憶有兩層含義：一是工作或學習時記憶資料的能力；二是回憶過往事件的能力。這兩方面皆有賴於心神，以及脾與腎。就記憶而言，脾之意、腎之志與心之神彼此重疊。脾之意負責記憶資料、學習與專注力。心與腎則與回憶過往事件（近事或遠事）有關，其中腎主近期記憶，心主久遠記憶。一個人可能在專業領域中記憶力（意）極佳，卻不擅長回憶往事（神與志）。心之神（心神）與脾之意（智力）之間，以及意與腎之志（意志力）之間，皆存在極為密切的關係。《靈樞》記載：「心之所憶謂之意」，「意之所存謂之志」。志雖常譯為 Will-Power（意志力），但亦兼有記憶之意。腦為髓海，亦主管記憶、智力與專注力。The Practice of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2008, page 246, 273; The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 150, 240"
    },
    {
      "number": 645,
      "question_en": "If the Hun (Ethereal Soul) comes and goes too much there can be",
