      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Kidneys are the mother of the Liver",
          "hant": "腎為肝之母",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Lungs are the mother of the Kidneys",
          "hant": "肺為腎之母",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Heart is the mother of Spleen",
          "hant": "心為脾之母",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Spleen is the mother of the Lungs",
          "hant": "脾為肺之母",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The Five Element (5E) theory is extremely useful clinically but it cannot be rigidly applied under all circumstances. One needs to pay attention to the actual zang fu (organs) functions and how these zang fu functions interact with each other. A common mistake is to try to superimpose all the 5E interactions on how the zang fu actually function. For example, in terms of 5E and zang fu function both these theories can show the same important interactions. For example, the interaction between Water generating Wood (5E) and the Kidney Yin nourishing Liver Yin (organ function) point to the same important relationship between the Kidneys (Water) and the Liver (Wood). The Spleen (Earth) nourishes the Lungs (Metal) by providing food-qi to the Lungs to generate the Gathering qi (zong qi). The Lungs (Metal) nourish the Kidneys as the Lung Qi descends and brings fluids to the Kidneys. However, in terms of zang fu functions, some 5E interactions have less clinical relevance such as Fire (Heart) generating Earth (Spleen). One can say that the Heart Qi moves the Blood and helps the transportation function of the Spleen but this interaction is not used in TCM clinical practice. As a matter of fact, it is more like the Spleen (Earth), which helps to produce the qi and Blood, that nourishes the Heart (Fire). This relationship between the Spleen (Earth) nourishing the Heart (Fire) is seen in the Cosmological sequence where Earth is at the center and supports all of the other elements. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 27, 28",
      "exp_hant": "五行理論在臨床上極為實用，但並不能在所有情況下生搬硬套。必須留意臟腑實際的功能，以及這些臟腑功能之間如何相互作用。一個常見的錯誤，是試圖將所有五行的相互關係，機械地套用於臟腑實際的運作方式上。舉例而言，五行與臟腑功能有時能呈現出相同的重要關係：水生木（五行）與腎陰滋養肝陰（臟腑功能）便指向腎（水）與肝（木）之間相同的重要關係。脾（土）透過為肺提供水穀之氣以生成宗氣，來滋養肺（金）。肺（金）則透過肺氣肅降、將津液輸佈於腎，來滋養腎。然而，就臟腑功能而言，某些五行關係的臨床意義較小，例如火（心）生土（脾）。雖然可以說心氣推動血液運行，有助於脾的運化功能，但此種相互作用在中醫臨床實務中並不常運用。事實上，情況更接近於脾（土）滋養心（火），因脾有助於生成氣血。脾（土）滋養心（火）的這種關係，可見於宇宙論序列中，土居中央並支撐其他所有元素。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 27, 28"
    },
