      "exp_en": "The Kidney primary meridian starts under the little toe, goes to KI-1 (yong quan) and emerges at KI-2 (ran gu), ascends the inner leg to meet with DU-1 (chang qiang). From DU-1 (chang qiang) one branch ascends the spine to connect with the Kidney and Bladder and emerges at KI-11 (heng gu). Another branch ascends from the Kidney organ and flows through the diaphragm to the Liver, Heart, and Lung, and proceeds upward to the throat to end at the root of the tongue. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 331",
