      "exp_en": "The ren mai regulates the Uterus and Blood. It also regulates the 7 year (women) and 8 year (men) developmental cycles. The 7 and 8 years should not be rigidly applied as there are natural variations. It is the chong mai (Penetrating Vessel) which has deep influence on the breast. It is the dai mai (Girdle Vessel) which regulates qi circulation in the legs. The ren mai can be selected to help the transitioning from one developmental cycle to another. The ren mai can be selected when there is a transitioning from childhood to puberty, to regulate the different phases of the menstrual cycle, to transition from infertility to fertility, transitioning from non-pregnant to pregnant, transitioning from pregnancy to childbirth, and transitioning from the reproductive phase to the menopausal phase. In each of these, the ren mai can be use to assist and smooth these transitions. The opening and coupled points are selected to activate the ren mai. Additional points are then added to treat the specifics. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 898; The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 453-455",
      "exp_hant": "任脈調節胞宮與血，亦主導女性七年、男性八年的發育週期。此七年、八年之數不應機械套用，因個體間存在自然差異。對乳房具有深刻影響的是衝脈；調節雙腿氣機運行的則是帶脈。任脈可用於協助各發育週期之間的轉換，例如：從兒童期轉入青春期、調節月經週期的不同階段、從不孕轉為受孕、從未懷孕轉為懷孕、從懷孕轉為分娩，以及從生育期轉入更年期等。在上述各種轉換中，任脈皆可用以協助並使轉換過程更為順暢。臨床上會選取開穴與配穴以啟動任脈，再依具體病情加取其他穴位。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 898; The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 453-455"
