      "exp_en": "The Triple Burner luo-connecting meridian separates from the Triple Burner primary meridian at TB-5 (wai guan), ascends the posterior part of the arm to the shoulder, and converges with the Pericardium primary meridian in the chest. Wai guan is translated as outer gate, in contrast to PC-6 (nei guan) inner gate. The Triple Burner meridian together with the Gall Bladder meridian is part of the shao yang division which is a hinge between tai yang (greater yang) and yang ming (bright yang). What this means is that the shao yang meridians can have an influence on both tai yang and bright yang. TB-5 (wai guan) can harmonize the yang, subdue Liver yang, and expel external and internal wind. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 388",
      "exp_hant": "三焦經絡脈由 TB-5（外關）別出於本經，沿手臂後側上行至肩部，並於胸部與心包經本經匯合。「外關」意為外側的關口，與 PC-6（內關，內側的關口）相對應。三焦經與膽經同屬少陽經，為太陽與陽明之間的樞紐，意即少陽經對太陽與陽明皆能發揮影響。TB-5（外關）可調和諸陽、平抑肝陽，並袪除內外風邪。A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 388"
