      "exp_en": "From the index finger the Large Intestine channel runs along the radial side of the forearm to LI-16 (ju gu) from which it goes to SI-12 (not SI-10), connecting to DU-14 and proceeding to ST-12. From ST-12 the channel ascends along the neck, curves around the upper lip (ST-4), crosses the philtrum at DU-26 (not DU-27), to terminate at the opposite side of the nose, LI-20, connecting with the Stomach channel. Another branch goes from ST-12 internally connecting to the Lung organ, descending to the Large Intestine organ, and ending at ST-37 (not all drawings show the ST-37 connection). The Lungs and Large Intestine organs are the only organs that the channel goes to. The channel also has meeting points with GB-5, GB-6, and GB-14 but most illustrations do not show this. Clinically, the Large Intestine points are selected to treat the lower teeth, lower gums, and lower jaw (the Stomach channel treats the upper gums, teeth, and jaw). As the channel crosses to the opposite side at DU-26 this means that to treat, for example, a gum/teeth/jaw problem on the left side, one would select Large Intestine points on the right arm. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion, 2010 Edition, page 96",
      "exp_hant": "大腸經自食指起，沿前臂橈側上行至 LI-16（巨骨），再行至 SI-12（秉風，而非 SI-10），聯繫 DU-14（大椎），並行至 ST-12（缺盆）。自 ST-12（缺盆）起，經脈沿頸部上行，環繞上唇（ST-4 地倉），於 DU-26（水溝，而非 DU-27）處交叉人中，終止於鼻部對側的 LI-20（迎香），與胃經相接。另有一支自 ST-12（缺盆）內行，聯繫肺臟，下行至大腸，並終止於 ST-37（上巨虛）（並非所有圖示皆呈現此與 ST-37 的聯繫）。肺與大腸為此經所聯繫的唯二臟腑。此經亦與 GB-5（頷厭）、GB-6（懸釐）及 GB-14（陽白）有交會點，但多數圖示並未呈現。臨床上，大腸經穴位常用於治療下齒、下齒齦及下頜的病症（胃經則主治上齒齦、上齒與上頜）。由於此經在 DU-26（水溝）處交叉至對側，因此，舉例而言，若欲治療左側的齒齦、牙齒或下頜問題，應選取右臂上的大腸經穴位。Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion, 2010 Edition, page 96"
