      "exp_en": "The Extraordinary Vessels have the function of absorbing excess qi from the main channels, thereby acting like a reservoir. The yin qiao mai and yang qiao mai are the first to do this. The yin qiao mai absorbs Excess qi from the abdomen while the yang qiao mai absorbs excess qi from the head. The yang qiao mai absorbs Excess yang from the head when there is Liver Yang Rising, Liver Fire, Liver Wind, or wind-stroke affecting the head. The yang qiao mai can also treat External Wind, especially with neck stiffness and severe headache. Further, the yang qiao mai drains excess yang in the Mind (insomnia, agitation, mania). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 926, 927",
      "exp_hant": "奇經八脈具有從十二正經吸收盛氣的功能，猶如水庫一般發揮調節作用。陰蹻脈與陽蹻脈是最先發揮此功能者。陰蹻脈自腹部吸收盛氣，陽蹻脈則自頭部吸收盛氣。當肝陽上亢、肝火、肝風或中風影響頭部時，陽蹻脈可吸收頭部的過盛陽氣。陽蹻脈亦可治療外風，尤其伴有頸項僵硬與劇烈頭痛者。此外，陽蹻脈亦能引導心神中過盛的陽氣外洩（失眠、煩躁、躁狂）。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 926, 927"
