      "exp_en": "The first and third internal branch of du mai go to the Kidneys. The primary external pathway and the third branch go to the brain. The second branch of du mai goes to the Heart. The first and second branch circle the genitals. The primary pathway of du mai begins at the lower abdomen (dan tian), descends and emerges at the perineum, ascends up the spine to DU-16 (where it enters the BRAIN), continues to ascend to DU-20, and then descends to DU-28. The first branch starts at the lower abdomen (dan tian) to the perineum, circles the GENITALS, goes to anus, ascends interior of the spinal column to enter the KIDNEYS. The second branch starts in the lower abdomen (dan tian), descends and circles the GENITALS, ascends to the navel, goes through the HEART, the throat, winds around the mouth, and ascends to the middle of the eyes. The third branch emerges at BL-1 to bilaterally follow the Bladder channel and converges to one point at DU-20 (to enter the BRAIN), descends as a single energetic line to DU-16 where there is another split into two energetic lines that pass through BL-12 and terminates in the KIDNEYS. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 529-530",
