      "exp_en": "One internal branch of the Stomach meridian goes from ST-12 descends through the diaphragm, links with REN-12 and REN-13, and then enters the Stomach and connects with the Spleen organ. An external branch goes from ST-12 goes four cun lateral to the midline as far as ST-18 and then goes two cun from the midline to ST-30. A third internal branch starts at the pyloric orifice of the Stomach (the opening between the stomach into the duodenum) descends within the abdomen and joins the external branch at ST-30. The fourth branch on the foot goes from ST-42 to SP-1 on the medial side of the big toe. Though the Stomach channel meets with SP-1, the point SP-1 is not categorized as a meeting point of the Stomach meridian. There are two branches which connect with ST-30 showing the importance of this point as a meeting point with the Penetrating Vessel (chong mai) and as a point of the Sea of Water and Grain. ST-30 regulates lower burner qi, regulates chong mai, and subdues running piglet qi. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 125-126",
      "exp_hant": "胃經的第一條內行支，自 ST-12（缺盆）貫穿橫膈，聯繫 REN-12（中脘）與 REN-13（上脘），進入胃並聯繫脾臟。外行支則自 ST-12（缺盆）沿正中線外開四寸下行至 ST-18（乳根），再改沿正中線外開二寸下行至 ST-30（氣衝）。第三條內行支起於胃之幽門（胃與十二指腸之間的開口），於腹內下行，並於 ST-30（氣衝）處與外行支會合。足部的第四條分支，則自 ST-42（衝陽）行至足大趾內側的 SP-1（隱白）。雖然胃經與 SP-1 相會，但 SP-1 並未被歸類為胃經的交會穴。有兩條分支皆聯繫於 ST-30（氣衝），顯示此穴作為衝脈交會穴、以及水穀之海之要穴的重要性。ST-30（氣衝）能調理下焦氣機、調節衝脈，並能平抑奔豚氣。A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 125-126"
    },
    {
      "number": 698,
      "question_en": "When it is said that the muscle meridians \"bind\" to certain body areas, it is somewhat generally equivalent to the Western concept of",
      "question_hant": "當提及經筋「結」於特定身體部位時，此概念大致相當於西方解剖學中的",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "fascia",
          "hant": "筋膜",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "muscle insertion",
          "hant": "肌肉止點",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "smooth muscles",
          "hant": "平滑肌",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "ligaments",
          "hant": "韌帶",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The word used in the Spiritual Axis is \"jie\". Deadman translates it as \"bind\" while Maciocia translates it as \"convergence\". The muscle meridians have areas of convergence where each one moves into smaller streams. These areas are very important in treatment as they are areas on the meridian which are more reactive. The idea of \"convergence\" is somewhat similar, but not always, to the Western idea of muscle insertion where each muscle originates from a bone that it is attached to and an insertion where the muscle attaches to a bone that the muscle moves. The areas of convergence in the texts are described according to related bones and not to Western names of bones. For example, the original and ancients texts describe the Small Intestine muscle meridian as converging or binding at the \"medial border of the elbow bone\" rather than the Western description of \"medial condyle of the humerus\". The meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 291",
      "exp_hant": "《靈樞》原文所用之字為「結」。Deadman 將其譯為「bind」（結聚），而 Maciocia 則譯為「convergence」（匯聚）。經筋皆有其匯聚部位，於此處各經筋分流為更細小的分支。這些部位在治療上極為重要，因其為經筋上反應較為敏感之處。「匯聚」的概念與西方解剖學中肌肉止點的概念有所相似（但並非完全相同），西方解剖學中，每條肌肉皆有其起點（附著於某骨）與止點（附著於受該肌肉牽動之骨）。古籍中所描述的匯聚部位，是依相關骨骼而定，而非依西方的骨骼命名方式。例如，古代原典將小腸經筋描述為結聚於「肘骨內側緣」，而非西方解剖學所稱的「肱骨內上髁」。The meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 291"
    },
