      "exp_en": "The du mai strengthens the Mind. The Mind (shen) is closely related to both the Heart and Brain. The Mind (shen) is housed in the Heart and nourished by Heart Blood. It is also housed in the Brain which is connected to du mai. The shen originates from the Prenatal Essence of the mother and father. The Spiritual Axis writes: \"When the two Essences of the mother and father unite, they form the Mind\". The Prenatal Essence is stored in the Kidneys which are the biological foundation of the Mind. Kidney Essence produces Marrow which fills the Brain. When the Brain is full of Marrow the thinking is clear. Many of the ancient TCM doctors, such as Li Shi Zhen, attributed mental functions to the Brain which they saw as the residence of the Original Mind (yuan shen). To treat the Mind in such conditions as depression, for example, it is important to treat both the Heart and Kidneys. This can be done through the du mai which has branches that connect and strengthen the Kidneys, Heart, and Brain. SI-3 and BL-62 activates the du mai connection between the Kidneys, Heart, and Brain. Adding moxa on DU-14 strengthens Kidney and Heart yang, will power and spirit. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 894",
      "exp_hant": "督脈能強化心神。心神與心臟、腦皆有密切關係。心神藏於心，由心血所滋養；同時心神亦藏於腦，而腦與督脈相聯繫。神源自父母之先天之精。《靈樞》記載：「兩精相搏謂之神」。先天之精藏於腎，為心神的生理根基。腎精化生髓，充盈於腦。腦髓充盈則思維清晰。許多古代醫家，如李時珍，皆將精神功能歸屬於腦，並視腦為元神所居之處。因此，欲治療如抑鬱等心神方面的病症，須同時調治心與腎。此可透過督脈達成，因督脈之分支能聯繫並強化腎、心與腦。SI-3（後谿）與 BL-62（申脈）能啟動督脈聯繫腎、心、腦的功能。於 DU-14（大椎）加灸，則能強化腎陽與心陽，並增強意志與精神。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 894"
    },
