      ],
      "exp_en": "The Luo-Connecting meridians are distributed superficially over the body. They are more superficial than the primary meridians and deeper than the cutaneous meridians. There are 16 luo-connecting meridians, one for each of the 12 primary meridians, one for du mai, one for ren mai, the great-luo meridian (SP-21), and the Stomach great luo which connects to the Lung and is felt as a throbbing below the breast. There are three luo meridians which have a very short pathway after separating from the luo-connecting point. These are the Lung luo (from LU-7 the luo only goes to the palm), the Bladder luo (from BL-58 the luo only goes to connect to the Kidney primary meridian), and the Gall Bladder luo (from GB-37 the luo connects with the Liver primary and then only goes to the top of foot). After connecting to the internally-externally paired primary meridian, the Luo-Connecting meridians usually continue to follow their own pathway. The luo-connecting meridians strengthen the bond between the internally-externally paired meridians. That is, they strengthen the yin and yang primary meridian relationship. A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 26",
      "exp_hant": "絡脈分布於體表較淺層，比十二正經淺，但比皮部深。共有十六條絡脈：十二正經各一條，督脈一條，任脈一條，脾之大絡（SP-21），以及連結於肺、在乳房下方可觸及搏動的胃之大絡。有三條絡脈在從絡穴分出後，循行路徑很短：肺絡（從LU-7分出後只到達手掌）、膀胱絡（從BL-58分出後只連接到腎的正經）、膽絡（從GB-37分出後與肝的正經相連，再到達足背）。絡脈在連接到表裡相合的正經之後，通常會繼續依循自己的路徑循行。絡脈能加強表裡相合經脈之間的聯繫，也就是強化陰陽正經之間的關係。A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 26"
