      ],
      "exp_en": "This is the most accurate answer. They can be affected by external pathogens but do not influence the functioning of internal organs. The muscle meridians do not have specific points like the primary meridians do. However, they can have \"ah shi\" points as a result of injury or trauma. The muscle meridians correspond to the striated skeletal muscles and not the smooth muscles that are found in the internal organs. The muscle meridians are more than actual muscles as they are involved in the circulation of qi and blood. The muscle or sinew meridians do not connect to the internal organs like the primary meridians and the luo-connecting meridians do. However, the muscle meridians can be influenced by internal organs via their association of the primary meridians to the muscle meridians. When the muscle meridians are invaded by pathogens there can be stiffness, pain, and aches but without the general symptoms that occur when the wei qi layer is invaded (aversion to cold, fever). Wind in the muscle meridians causes stiffness and wandering pain. Cold in the muscle meridians causes contraction and pain that improves with heat. Dampness in the muscle meridians manifests as swelling, numbness, and a feeling of heaviness. The primary and divergent meridians are coupled in yin-yang pairs whereas the muscle meridians are categorized into four groups of three muscle meridians: yin muscle meridians of the arm (LU, PC, HT), yang muscle meridians of the arm (TB, SI, LI), yin muscle meridians of the leg (SP, KI, LR), and yang muscle meridians of the leg (ST, GB, BL). A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 26; The meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 287-290",
      "exp_hant": "這是最正確的答案。經筋可受外邪影響，但不會影響臟腑功能。經筋不像正經那樣有特定的穴位，但可因外傷而出現「阿是穴」。經筋對應的是橫紋骨骼肌，而非分布於臟腑的平滑肌。經筋不僅止於實質的肌肉，也參與氣血的循行。經筋與絡脈不同，正經與絡脈能連結臟腑，經筋則不然；然而，經筋可透過正經與經筋之間的聯繫而受臟腑影響。當經筋被邪氣侵犯時，會出現僵硬、疼痛與痠痛，但不會出現衛氣層被侵犯時的全身性症狀（惡寒、發熱）。風邪侵犯經筋會導致僵硬與遊走性疼痛。寒邪侵犯經筋會導致拘攣，且疼痛遇熱可緩解。濕邪侵犯經筋則表現為腫脹、麻木與沉重感。正經與經別以陰陽表裡相配，而經筋則分為四組、每組三條經筋：手三陰經筋（肺、心包、心）、手三陽經筋（三焦、小腸、大腸）、足三陰經筋（脾、腎、肝）、足三陽經筋（胃、膽、膀胱）。A Manual of Acupuncture, Deadman, 2nd Edition, page 26; The meridians of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 287-290"
