        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "the sores have not ulcerated and the pulse is vacuous, weak, or thin",
          "hant": "瘡瘍尚未潰爛，脈象呈虛、弱或細",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The pulse has an important role in diagnosing skin sores. The commonly seen pulses in skin problems are the floating, deep, rapid, surging, thin, vacuous, and replete. It is important to determine if the pulse is forceful or forceless. If the sores have not ulcerated and the pulse is of the repletion/excess type then this indicates that the evil qi is effulgent and the righteous qi is also effulgent. If the sores have already ulcerated and the pulse is replete, surging, wiry, or rapid then this indicates that the evil qi is flourishing and that the qi is difficult to transform. If the sores have already ulcerated and the pulse is of the vacuous/empty type then this indicates that the evil qi has been eliminated but the righteous qi is debilitated. If the sores have not ulcerated and the pulse is vacuous, weak, or thin then this indicates that both the qi and blood are weak and debilitated, that the toxin is deep and flourishing. Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 376",
      "exp_hant": "脈象在瘡瘍的診斷上扮演重要角色。瘡瘍常見的脈象有浮、沉、數、洪、細、虛、實。判斷脈象是否有力極為重要。若瘡瘍尚未潰爛而脈象屬實證，表示邪氣熾盛，正氣亦旺盛。若瘡瘍已潰爛而脈象呈實、洪、弦或數，表示邪氣熾盛而氣難以轉化。若瘡瘍已潰爛而脈象屬虛證，表示邪氣已去而正氣衰弱。若瘡瘍尚未潰爛而脈象呈虛、弱或細，表示氣血兩虛衰弱，毒邪深伏而熾盛。Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 376"
