      "exp_en": "A soggy pulse (ru mai) is a combination of a thin pulse (xi mai), an empty pulse (xu mai), and a floating pulse (fu mai). It is a very soft pulse but less clear than a thin pulse and felt only at the superficial level. Slightly increasing the finger pressure makes the pulse disappear. A soggy pulse (ru mai) indicates Deficient Blood, Deficient Jing or Dampness. A moving pulse (dong mai) combines the short pulse, the tight pulse, the slippery pulse, and the rapid pulse. It is an incomplete pulse as it is only felt in one position like a bean and not having a head or tail. It indicates an extreme condition (fever, pain, fright, palpitations) and is rarely encountered in practice. A frail pulse (ruo mai) is soft, weak, a little thin, and felt at the deep level. It is like an inverted upside down empty pulse and indicates an extreme deficiency of Qi that fails to raise the pulse. The hurried pulse (cu mai) is rapid and irregularly skips beats. It can indicate Heat agitating the Blood. The Web That Has No Weaver, Kaptchuk, 2000, page 205",
      "exp_hant": "濡脈是細脈、虛脈與浮脈的綜合表現。它比細脈更為柔軟，但不如細脈清晰，且只能在淺層觸及。稍加指力按壓，脈象便隨之消失。濡脈主血虛、精虛或濕邪。動脈結合了短脈、緊脈、滑脈與數脈的特徵，是一種不完整的脈象，只能在單一部位觸及，如豆粒狀，無頭無尾。動脈主極端病證（發熱、疼痛、驚恐、心悸），臨床上較少見。弱脈柔軟、無力、略細，只能在深層觸及，如同倒置的虛脈，主氣虛極重、無力鼓動脈搏。促脈脈率快且不規則地歇止，可主熱擾血分。The Web That Has No Weaver, Kaptchuk, 2000, page 205"
    },
    {
      "number": 707,
      "question_en": "A 32 year-old man female complains of tiredness, weak muscles and poor appetite. You want to enquire about their energy level. Which \"yes\" answer from the patient helps confirm the diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位32歲的病患主訴疲倦、肌肉無力及食慾不振。您想詢問其精力狀況。病患的哪一個「是」的回答有助於確認診斷？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Is your energy level worse in the afternoon and improves with movement?",
