      "exp_en": "A red facial color tends to indicate blood heat which can result in early menstruation, copious menstruation, and flooding or spotting, but not scanty menstruation. Gynaecological disorders can be observed in the five facial colors. A dark-dusky face indicates Kidney vacuity debilitation and can be seen in infertility and vaginal discharges. If the facial color is green-blue or black and dark purple, this is generally due to Blood stasis which can cause painful menstruation. If the facial color is yellow and pale this is associated with Spleen vacuity with Dampness and Phlegm resulting in leucorrhea. If the facial color is dull-white and the body type is fat, then this can be associated with yang qi vacuity that can result in vaginal discharge, excess menstruation, and vacuity cold. A yellow and dusky facial color indicates body fluid depletion which can show as scanty menstruation and infertility. Lip color and tongue color can be associated with the same patterns as the facial colors just described. Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 354",
      "exp_hant": "面色紅多顯示血熱，可導致月經先期、月經量多，以及崩漏，但不會導致月經量少。婦科疾患可從五色觀察得知。面色黧黑晦暗顯示腎虛衰憊，可見於不孕與帶下。若面色青藍或黑而紫暗，通常因血瘀所致，可導致痛經。若面色黃而蒼白，則與脾虛兼濕痰有關，可導致帶下。若面色蒼白無華且體型肥胖，可能與陽氣虛有關，可導致帶下、月經過多及虛寒。若面色黃而晦暗顯示津液虧耗，可表現為月經量少及不孕。唇色與舌色也可能與上述面色相同的證型有關。Practical Diagnosis in Traditional Chinese Medicine, Deng, 1999, page 354"
