      "exp_en": "The pulsation of the apical pulse (left 5th intercostal space at the apex of the heart) should be compared to the radial pulse. Both should have the same strength or weakness. If the apical pulse is empty, weak or choppy then the radial pulse should also be weak. If there is a discrepancy between the two, this indicates poor prognosis or even heart disease. When just assessing for a healthy apical pulse, it should be distinctly felt, relatively slow, and not too hard. If the apical pulse is weak and feeble, this indicates a weak Zong Qi (Gathering Qi) and thus weak Lungs and/or Heart. If the apical pulse stops and starts, this can indicate shock or it can be a sign of alcoholism. The apical pulse can become very rapid when there is fright or extreme anger. Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 512",
      "exp_hant": "心尖搏動（左側第五肋間、心尖處）應與橈動脈脈象相互比較，兩者強弱應一致。若心尖搏動虛、弱或澀，橈動脈脈象也應同樣偏弱。若兩者出現落差，則顯示預後不良，甚至可能有心臟疾病。單就健康的心尖搏動而言，應能明顯觸及、速率相對較緩、且不過於堅硬。若心尖搏動微弱無力，顯示宗氣虛弱，因而肺與／或心亦虛弱。若心尖搏動時斷時續，可能顯示休克，也可能是酒精中毒的徵象。受驚或盛怒時，心尖搏動可變得非常快速。Diagnosis in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2004, page 512"
