        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "full pulse (shi mai)",
          "hant": "實脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Deep pulse (chen mai)",
          "hant": "沉脈",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "A big pulse (da mai) is categorized according to width. It has a broad diameter and can be distinctively felt. A big pulse (da mai) manifests when there is Excess Heat in the Stomach and/or Intestines. A full pulse (shi mai) is a pulse categorized according to strength. A full pulse (shi mai) is big, strong, and pounding hard against the finger tips on all the three depths. It is a Yang pulse and indicates Excess. A deep pulse (chen mai) becomes distinctly felt only at the deep or third level when heavy pressure is applied. It is not felt at the superficial or middle levels. A deep pulse (chen mai) indicates an internal disorder or an internal obstruction. The prison pulse (lao mai) is a form of a hidden pulse as it is deep, wiry, and often strong and long. The Web That Has No Weaver, Kaptchuk, 2000, page 198",
      "exp_hant": "大脈是依脈寬分類的脈象，脈幅寬大且能明顯觸及。大脈可顯示胃和／或腸有實熱。實脈是依脈力分類的脈象，實脈脈體大、有力，於浮、中、沉三部按之皆搏指有力，屬陽脈，主實證。沉脈需重按至深層（第三層）方能明顯觸及，浮取與中取皆不可得，主內臟疾病或內部阻滯。牢脈是伏脈的一種，脈沉、弦，且多兼強而長。The Web That Has No Weaver, Kaptchuk, 2000, page 198"
    },
    {
      "number": 722,
      "question_en": "A patient has poor appetite, abdominal distention which is worse after eating, lassitude, sallow complexion, no stamina, a bearing down sensation in the abdomen, and a prolapsed stomach. What pulse is expected?",
      "question_hant": "病患食慾不振、腹脹於進食後加重、倦怠、面色萎黃、體力不足、腹部有下墜感，且有胃下垂。預期會出現什麼脈象？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Weak pulse",
          "hant": "弱脈",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Floating-Empty pulse",
          "hant": "浮虛脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Slippery pulse",
          "hant": "滑脈",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Tight pulse",
          "hant": "緊脈",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Spleen Qi Sinking. Spleen Qi Sinking is a variation of Spleen Qi Deficiency in which the raising aspect of Spleen Qi is weak. The expected pulse in this pattern is a Weak pulse. The Weak pulse is a soft pulse that is not palpated at the superficial level but only at the deep level. It indicates Qi deficiency. When the Stomach is prolapsed the right middle position becomes Weak. A pale tongue is expected in this pattern. The pale tongue results from the weak Qi not raising the Blood to the tongue. A bearing down sensation and weak pulse are sufficient to make the diagnosis of Spleen Qi Sinking. The treatment principle is Tonify Spleen Qi and Raise Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 603; 2005 Edition, page 572; 1989 Edition, page 244",
      "exp_hant": "此診斷為脾氣下陷。脾氣下陷是脾氣虛的一種變證，其中脾氣的升提功能減弱。此證型預期脈象為弱脈。弱脈是一種軟脈，浮取無法觸及，只能於沉取觸及，主氣虛。當胃下垂時，右手中部脈位會呈現弱脈。此證型預期舌象為淡白舌，是因氣虛無力將血行至舌面所致。下墜感與弱脈，即足以診斷為脾氣下陷。治則為補脾氣、升提中氣。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 603; 2005 Edition, page 572; 1989 Edition, page 244"
    },
    {
      "number": 723,
      "question_en": "A 44 year-old patient complains of frequent and spontaneous sweating. She also reports palpitations, shortness of breath, feeling tired and feeling slight depressed. The pulse is empty. Which \"yes\" answer to the following questions helps to confirm the diagnosis?",
      "question_hant": "一位44歲病患主訴頻繁且自發性出汗，並主訴心悸、氣短、疲倦及輕微情緒低落。脈象為虛脈。以下哪一個問題得到「是」的回答，有助於確認診斷？",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Does the sweat have a yellow color?",
          "hant": "汗液是否呈黃色？",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Is the sweating only on the forehead?",
          "hant": "出汗是否僅限於額頭？",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Is the sweating oily like pearls?",
          "hant": "出汗是否如珠、油膩？",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Is the sweating only on the hands?",
          "hant": "出汗是否僅限於雙手？",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Asking about sweating is one of the 10 traditional diagnostic questions. The clinical picture can point to Deficient Heart Qi. With sweating you want to differentiate between Empty conditions (Deficient Yin or Yang) and Full conditions (Heat, Damp-Heat). You want to differentiate sweating occurring with different AREAS OF THE BODY: A Deficient Lung Qi pattern or a Deficient Heart Qi pattern can have sweating only on the hands. A Deficient Lung Qi pattern can have whole body sweating. Sweating only on the head can be part of a Stomach Heat or Damp-Heat pattern. A Yang Collapse pattern can have oily sweat, like pearls, only on the forehead. Sweating due to Yang Collapse indicates a severe disease and a danger of death. A Stomach and Spleen Deficiency pattern can have sweating only on the arms and legs. A Deficient yin pattern can have five-palm sweat (sweating on the palms, soles and chest). You want to differentiate sweating occurring at different TIME OF DAY: A Deficient Yang pattern can have daytime sweating. A Deficient Yin pattern can have sweating at night. Damp-Heat can also have night sweating. You want to differentiate sweating regarding QUALITY OF SWEAT: Oily sweat can be part of a severe Yang Deficiency pattern. Yellow sweat can be part of a Damp-Heat pattern. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 357, 491",
      "exp_hant": "詢問出汗情況是十項傳統問診之一。此臨床表現可能指向心氣虛。針對出汗，須區分虛證（陰虛或陽虛）與實證（熱證、濕熱）。您需要區分出汗發生的部位：肺氣虛證或心氣虛證可能僅雙手出汗。肺氣虛證可能全身出汗。僅頭部出汗可能是胃熱或濕熱證的一部分。陽脫證可能僅額頭出油汗如珠。陽脫所致的出汗顯示病情嚴重，有死亡之虞。脾胃虛弱證可能僅四肢出汗。陰虛證可能出現五心汗出（手心、腳心及胸部出汗）。您也需要區分出汗發生的時間：陽虛證可能白天出汗；陰虛證可能夜間出汗；濕熱證也可能有夜間出汗。您還需要區分汗液的性質：油汗可能是重度陽虛的一部分；黃汗可能是濕熱證的一部分。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 357, 491"
    },
    {
