      ],
      "exp_en": "Asking about pain is one of the diagnostic questions. Pain whether due to Empty Cold or Full Cold can cause pain which is cramping or spastic, worsens with cold weather/food/drinks and improves with heat. If the Cold pain had a slow onset then it is likely Empty Cold. If the Cold pain has a sudden onset then it is likely Full Cold. The most common location for pain due to Cold are the Uterus (Deficient Cold Uterus, Cold Invading the Uterus), joints (Cold Bi-Syndrome), epigastrium (Cold Invading the Stomach, Stomach Deficient Cold) and abdomen (Cold in Intestines, Empty Cold in abdomen). Pain that is dull and lingering, improves with pressure, worsens with bowel movement, better lying down, and has a slow and gradual onset and better with rest is due to Deficiency (Qi, Blood or Yin Deficiency). Pain that is burning, improves with cold, worsens with movement and improves with bowel movement is due to Full Heat (Hot Bi-Syndrome, Stomach Fire, Heat Obstructing Large Intestine). The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 343-344",
      "exp_hant": "詢問疼痛情況是診斷問診之一。無論是虛寒或實寒所致的疼痛，皆可能呈痙攣性或抽搐性，遇寒冷天氣／飲食／飲品加重，得熱則緩解。若寒性疼痛起病緩慢，多屬虛寒；若起病急驟，多屬實寒。寒邪所致疼痛最常見的部位為子宮（子宮虛寒、寒凝胞宮）、關節（寒痺）、胃脘（寒邪犯胃、胃虛寒）及腹部（腸中寒、腹中虛寒）。疼痛隱隱綿延、按之則舒、便後加重、臥則較舒、起病緩慢漸進且休息可緩解，屬虛證（氣虛、血虛或陰虛）。疼痛有灼熱感、得冷則減、活動則加重、便後可緩解，屬實熱證（熱痺、胃火、大腸熱結）。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 343-344"
    },
    {
      "number": 735,
      "question_en": "A 42 year-old patient has alternation of shivers and fever, a bitter taste, dry throat, blurred vision, hypochondrial fullness and distention, lack of desire to eat or drink, irritability, nausea, vomiting, unilateral thin-white coating on the tongue, and a wiry-thin pulse. Which stage is the patient manifesting?",
      "question_hant": "一位42歲病患寒熱往來、口苦、咽乾、視物模糊、脅肋脹滿、不欲飲食、煩躁、噁心、嘔吐、舌苔薄白偏於一側、脈弦細。病患目前處於哪個病程階段？",
