      "exp_en": "The list of Gall Bladder channel symptoms includes chest and hypochondrial pain, headache, deafness, swelling and pain of the supraclavicular fossa, axilla swelling, and numbness or pain along the channel. The Gall Bladder channel is selected to treat the head and hypochondrium. Because the Gall Bladder channel traverses the hypochondrium, it is always involved in pain and distention in that area. The main point for this is GB-34. The most frequent head disorder for the Gall Bladder channel is migraine headaches. The distal point for Gall Bladder channel migraine is GB-43, the local adjacent point is GB-20, and the local points can be GB-14, GB-4, GB-6, and GB-9. There is a branch of the Gall Bladder channel that descends to the chest from the supraclavicular fossa. This explains why GB-41 can treat breast disorders in women. A branch of the Gall Bladder channel enters the ear. Other channels that can treat acute ear disorders are the Triple Burner and Small Intestine channels. The channel can treat acute deafness and tinnitus. It is important to differentiate channel from organ symptoms which are often included in a channel symptom list. Organ symptoms in the Gall Bladder channel symptom list include bitter mouth taste, sighing, and malaria. The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 105; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804",
      "exp_hant": "膽經症狀清單包括胸脅疼痛、頭痛、耳聾、缺盆腫痛、腋下腫脹，以及沿經脈麻木或疼痛。選用膽經治療頭部與脅肋部位的疾患。因膽經行於脅肋部，凡此部位的疼痛與脹滿，均與膽經有關，主穴為GB-34。膽經治療頭部疾患中最常見的是偏頭痛。膽經偏頭痛的遠端取穴為GB-43，鄰近局部取穴為GB-20，局部取穴則可用GB-14、GB-4、GB-6及GB-9。膽經有一分支從缺盆下行至胸，這說明了GB-41為何能治療女性乳房疾患。膽經另有一分支入耳，三焦經與小腸經也能治療急性耳疾，膽經則能治療急性耳聾與耳鳴。需注意區分經脈症狀與臟腑症狀，因臟腑症狀常被列入經脈症狀清單中。膽經症狀清單中的臟腑症狀包括口苦、善太息及瘧疾。The Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 105; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804"
