      ],
      "exp_en": "The external Wind-Cold pathogen prevents the Lung Qi from descending (cough, stuffed/runny nose). Wind also blocks Lung Qi dispersion and causes sneezing. As the wei qi warms the skin-muscles, there is aversion to cold. The fever is a result of the struggle between the external Wind and the wei qi which is fighting the invasion. The fever is not necessarily an objective raised temperature but can just be the body feels hot on palpation (emission of heat). As this is a taiyang stage (Bladder-Small Intestine), the pathogen blocks taiyang and results in occipital headaches (could also be whole head). The pulse floats indicating the extra movement of wei qi to the surface to repel the external pathogen. The white tongue coating reflects the cold. The keynote symptoms of external Wind attack are aversion to cold and \"fever\". The treatment principle is Release the Exterior, Expel Cold, Descend and Diffuse Lung Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 579; 2005 Edition, page 550; 1989 Edition, page 235",
      "exp_hant": "外感風寒之邪妨礙肺氣下降（咳嗽、鼻塞流涕）。風邪亦阻遏肺氣的宣發，導致噴嚏。因衛氣溫煦肌表，故出現惡寒。發熱則是外風與奮起抵禦外邪的衛氣相爭所致。此處的發熱未必是可測得的體溫升高，也可能只是觸診時皮膚感覺發熱（熱的散發）。因這是太陽階段（膀胱、小腸），邪氣阻遏太陽經，導致後頭痛（也可能是整個頭部）。脈浮，顯示衛氣增強上行至體表以抵禦外邪。舌苔白，反映寒象。外感風邪的主要症狀是惡寒與「發熱」。治則為解表、祛寒、宣降肺氣。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 579; 2005 Edition, page 550; 1989 Edition, page 235"
