      "exp_en": "Another name for this pattern is Phlegm Obstructing Heart Orifices. This pattern is similar to the Phlegm-Fire Harassing the Heart pattern. The Phlegm Misting the Mind pattern is mostly seen in children (mental retardation or speech problems) or in adults (wind-stroke with Phlegm induced coma, paralysis, voice loss). In the Phlegm Misting the Mind pattern, the severe mental symptoms (uncontrolled laughter, hitting/scolding people, rash behavior, incoherent speech, depression, muttering) which occur in the Phlegm-Fire Harassing the Heart pattern are not there. The mental confusion, lethargy, stupor, rattling throat, and unconsciousness are all caused from Phlegm obstructing the Heart-Mind. As the tongue is the sprout of the Heart, the excess Phlegm prevents tongue movement (aphasia). Vomiting and rattling throat are caused by the Phlegm obstructing the chest. Sticky-greasy tongue and slippery pulse are a manifestation of the Phlegm. The treatment principle is to Open the Heart, Resolve Phlegm, and Open the Heart Orifices. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 505; 2005 Edition, page 477; 1989 Edition, page 211",
      "exp_hant": "此證型另稱為痰阻心竅。此證型與痰火擾心相似。痰迷心竅多見於兒童（智能障礙或言語障礙）或成人（中風後痰阻所致的昏迷、癱瘓、失音）。在痰迷心竅證型中，痰火擾心所見的嚴重精神症狀（狂笑無常、打人罵人、行為魯莽、言語不清、抑鬱、喃喃自語）並不存在。神志混亂、嗜睡、昏矇、喉中痰鳴及意識不清，皆由痰阻心神所致。因舌為心之苗，過盛的痰濁妨礙舌的運動，導致失語。嘔吐與喉中痰鳴由痰阻胸中所致。舌苔黏膩及脈滑為痰邪的表現。治則為開竅、化痰、開心竅。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 505; 2005 Edition, page 477; 1989 Edition, page 211"
    },
