      "exp_en": "This is the tai yang or Greater Yang stage. In the pattern of Invasion of Wind-Cold with Prevalence of Wind the emphasis is on Wind more than Cold. The ying qi is deficient compared to the wei qi. This is an external-deficient-cold pattern (8 Principles). When the wei qi resists the pathogenic factor there will be a fever. The fever does not necessarily mean an actual fever that can be measured but that the skin of the patient feels hot when palpated. The Chinese term for this is \"fa re\" or \"emission of heat\". In the Invasion of Wind-Cold with Prevalence of Wind pattern there is slight sweating because the weak ying-nutritive qi no longer holds the sweat in. An impaired Lung diffusing function to the nose can result in sneezing. When the pathogenic factor obstructs the wei qi in the space between the skin and muscles (exterior of the body), the warming function of the wei qi is impaired and causes aversion to cold. The patient still feels cold when covered up with blankets as the Cold is of the shi-excess type. When external Wind obstructs the tai yang channels (Bladder, Small Intestine) the muscles of the neck contract causing a stiff neck or occipital headache. The floating pulse results from the wei qi increasing on the surface of the body to resist the pathogenic factor. The treatment principle is to Release the Exterior, Expel Wind-Cold, Diffuse the Lung qi, Harmonize the ying and wei qi. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 753; 2005 Edition, page 711",
      "exp_hant": "這是太陽（太陽病）階段。在風寒外襲兼風邪偏盛的證型中，重點在於風邪甚於寒邪。營氣相對於衛氣較為不足，屬表、虛、寒證（八綱）。當衛氣抵禦邪氣時，會出現發熱。此處的發熱未必指可測得的實際體溫升高，而是觸診時病患皮膚感覺發熱，中文稱為「發熱」。在風寒外襲兼風邪偏盛的證型中，因虛弱的營氣無法收攝汗液，故有輕微出汗。肺的宣發功能受損，影響鼻竅，可導致打噴嚏。當邪氣阻遏衛氣於皮膚與肌肉之間（體表），衛氣的溫煦功能受損，導致惡寒。此時患者即使覆蓋被褥仍感覺寒冷，因此寒屬實證性質。當外風阻遏太陽經（膀胱、小腸）時，頸部肌肉拘急，導致頸項強直或後頭痛。脈浮是衛氣增強至體表以抵禦邪氣所致。舌苔白反映寒象。治則為解表、祛風寒、宣肺氣、調和營衛。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 753; 2005 Edition, page 711"
