      "exp_en": "The tai yin stage is the first of the yin stages (tai yin, shao yin, jue yin). The tai yin stage is mostly due to the pathogenic Cold attacking the Middle Burner. When a patient is constitutionally weak, when treatment is delayed, wrongly applied from the previous yang stages (tai yang, yang ming, shao yang) or it can be the result of a strong pathogenic factor going directly to tai yin. An example of the pathogen going directly to the tai yin stage is food poisoning. The tai yin stage corresponds to Spleen Yang Deficiency with Cold. The tai yin stage is an empty-internal-cold pattern (8 Principles). The Cold obstructs the Middle Burner causing abdominal fullness and vomiting. When the Spleen qi is deficient the transformation-transportation function is affected resulting in loose stools and poor appetite. This can also lead to poor nourishment of the limbs resulting in easily fatigued limbs. When the Spleen yang is deficient there is failure to warm the body (feeling cold) and leading to an accumulation of Body Fluids due to a failure to transform Body Fluids leading to an absence of thirst. The pulse is deep (internal disharmony), weak (deficient condition), and slow (cold). The treatment principle is to tonify Spleen yang and expel Cold. Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 761; 2005 Edition, page 717",
      "exp_hant": "太陰階段是三個陰經階段（太陰、少陰、厥陰）中的第一個。太陰階段多因寒邪侵犯中焦所致。當病患體質原本虛弱、治療延誤、前面陽經階段（太陽、陽明、少陽）誤治，或強盛的邪氣直接進入太陰階段時，皆可能發生此情形。邪氣直入太陰階段的例子如食物中毒。太陰階段對應脾陽虛兼寒。太陰階段屬裡、虛、寒證（八綱）。寒邪阻滯中焦，導致腹脹與嘔吐。當脾氣虛時，運化功能受影響，導致大便溏薄及食慾不振，亦可能因四肢失於滋養而容易疲乏。當脾陽虛時，溫煦身體的功能失調（畏寒），並因無法運化津液而導致津液積聚，因而不渴。脈沉（內在失調）、弱（虛證）、遲（寒證）。治則為溫補脾陽、祛寒。Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 761; 2005 Edition, page 717"
