      "exp_en": "This is an internal deficiency pattern. As the Heart governs the Blood, when the Blood is xu it will have an impact on the Heart and the Shen which resides in the Heart. When the Blood insufficiently nourishes the Heart, the Shen will lose its anchor in the Heart resulting in such symptoms as insomnia, anxiety, excess dreaming, poor memory, dull thinking, and startling easy. As the Blood is the mother of the qi, a deficiency of Heart Blood will impact the motive aspect of the Heart qi resulting in palpitations. There is a difference between palpitations caused by deficient Heart qi and deficient Heart Blood. With deficient qi the palpitations tend to occur during the day and with exertion. With deficient Blood the palpitations tend to occur in the evening, at rest, and with sense of anxiety or uneasiness in the chest. In this pattern there will be a dull-pale complexion as opposed to a bright-pale complexion found in deficient qi. When Blood fails to nourish the Brain the result will be dizziness. As the Heart opens into the tongue, an insufficient amount of Blood will reach it resulting in a pale tongue. The tongue can be dry as the Blood fails to moisten it. In this pattern one can expect a choppy or fine pulse. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 496; 2005 Edition, page 469; 1989 Edition, page 205",
      "exp_hant": "此為內在虛證。因心主血，當血虛時會影響心及居於心中的神。當血不足以滋養心時，神會失去在心中的依附，導致失眠、焦慮、多夢、記憶力差、思緒遲鈍及易受驚。因血為氣之母，心血虛會影響心氣的推動作用，導致心悸。心氣虛與心血虛所致的心悸有所不同：氣虛所致的心悸多發生於白天及勞動時；血虛所致的心悸則多發生於傍晚、休息時，並伴有胸中焦慮或不安感。此證型面色多為晦暗蒼白，而非氣虛所見的光亮蒼白。當血不能滋養腦部時，會導致頭暈。因心開竅於舌，血不足以濡養舌，導致舌淡。舌也可能因血不能滋潤而偏乾。此證型脈象可為澀或細。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 496; 2005 Edition, page 469; 1989 Edition, page 205"
    },
