      "exp_en": "This is the most complete and accurate answer. For there to be Kidneys and Heart Not Harmonized there would be symptoms pointing to the Heart such as palpitations, dream-disturbed sleep, or sexual dreams though there are symptoms that point to the Kidneys. This is a case involving both Kidney Yin and Kidney Yang Deficiency, a common occurrence in menopause. Kidney Yin deficiency manifested as hot flashes, constipation, night sweats, dry mouth and eyes, and weak left rear pulse position. Kidney Yang deficiency manifested as tiredness, frequent urination, back pain, cold feet, and weak rear right pulse position. The depression and lack of motivation is due to a lack of Will-Power (zhi) caused by weak Kidneys. This case also has Liver Yang Rising which is rooted in Kidney Yin Deficiency. The Liver Yang Rising manifested as headaches, irritability, tongue with red sides, and an overflowing left middle pulse position. Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1st Edition, page 754",
      "exp_hant": "此為最完整且準確之答案。若為心腎不交，應有指向心之症狀，如心悸、多夢或夢遺（夢交），然本病例僅見指向腎之症狀。此病例兼具腎陰虛與腎陽虛，此於更年期常見。腎陰虛表現為潮熱、便秘、盜汗、口乾眼乾及左尺脈弱；腎陽虛表現為疲倦、頻尿、腰痛、足冷及右尺脈弱。情緒憂鬱與缺乏動力乃因腎虛致「志」不足所致。此病例亦兼有肝陽上亢，其根源在於腎陰虛，表現為頭痛、急躁易怒、舌邊紅及左關脈洪。Obstetrics and Gynecology in Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 1st Edition, page 754"
