      "exp_en": "PATHOLOGY: When the qi of the Triple Burner muscle channel is disordered, there is a strain of the muscles along the pathway of the channel a curled tongue. PATHWAY: The Triple Burner muscle channel starts at the ulnar side of the ring finger to converge at the back of the wrist, travels along the posterior art of the arm and converges at the tip of the elbow from where it ascends to the lateral area of the upper arm and then to the shoulder and neck. It then goes to the angle of the mandible where it separates. One branch goes to the root of the tongue and the other main branch ascends in front of the ear to join the outer canthus an then ascends across the temple to converge at the corner of the forehead. The Triple Burner muscle channel connects with the muscle channel of the Small Intestine. Channels of Acupuncture, Maciocia, 2006, page 301, 317; Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 804; 2005 Edition, page 759",
