      "exp_en": "The diagnosis is Deficient Qi and Sinking Qi. The clinical picture points to a combination of Lung (SOB, weak voice) and Spleen (loose stools, poor appetite) Qi Deficiency with Sinking Qi (prolapse). The Sinking Qi can also manifest as a bearing down sensation and involve a prolapse (uterus, intestines, anus, vagina, stomach or bladder). Sinking Qi is not an independent pattern. Sinking Qi is always paired with Deficiency of Qi. In terms of treatment this means that it is important to not only raise the qi but also concurrently tonify the Qi. The patterns associated with Qi include Deficient Qi, Qi Stasis and Rebellious Qi. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 470",
      "exp_hant": "診斷為氣虛兼氣陷。此臨床表現顯示肺氣虛（氣短、聲音低弱）與脾氣虛（大便溏瀉、食慾不振）併見氣陷（下垂）。氣陷亦可表現為墜脹感，並可涉及各種下垂（子宮、腸、肛門、陰道、胃或膀胱）。氣陷並非獨立之證候，而必與氣虛並見。就治療而言，此意味著不僅須升提中氣，亦須同時補氣。與氣相關之證候包括氣虛、氣滯及氣逆。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 470"
