    {
      "number": 820,
      "question_en": "From a TCM point of view, a lack of animal food in the diet may induce",
      "question_hant": "從中醫觀點而言，飲食中缺乏動物性食物可能導致",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "en": "Qi Deficiency",
          "hant": "氣虛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "en": "Qi Stasis",
          "hant": "氣滯",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "en": "Excess Yin",
          "hant": "陰盛",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "en": "Blood deficiency",
          "hant": "血虛",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Meat is a strong Blood tonic. From the TCM view, food is more than seeing food in terms of nutrients (vitamin, minerals, protein). TCM views animal food as having a particular quality called \"qing\" or feeling. It is this qing that nourishes the Blood. A lack of animal food, especially in women, can produce a deficiency of Blood. Many vegetarians eat more salads and cheese. These are foods which are cold (salads) and can produce phlegm (cheese). However, a vegetarian diet with proper food combining to ensure protein requirements and a diet that includes a balance of hot and cold foods can be healthy. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 291",
      "exp_hant": "肉類為強力之補血食物。從中醫角度而言，食物之意義不僅在於營養素（維生素、礦物質、蛋白質）之攝取。中醫認為動物性食物具有一種特殊之性質，稱為「情」，正是此「情」滋養血分。缺乏動物性食物，尤其女性，可導致血虛。許多素食者攝取較多沙拉及乳酪，此類食物性偏寒涼（沙拉）或易生痰（乳酪）。然而，若素食飲食搭配得宜，以確保蛋白質攝取充足，並注意寒熱食物之均衡，仍可維持健康。The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 291"
    },
