      "exp_en": "Chang San Feng is also known as the Father of the \"Grand Supreme Fist\" or Tai Chi Chuan. Chang discovered that most Wu Kuen (martial forms) were too hard, too vigorous and relied too heavily upon the physical strength. As a result he developed a softer style of martial art. The Wade-Giles romantization is T'ai Chi Ch'uan. In the pinyin system it is Tai Ji. tcmtests.com, January 2020",
