          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "exp_en": "Bitter foods are also valerian, echinacea, and pau d'arco. Bitter foods are yin and cooling in nature. They contract the qi and move the qi down. The bitter tastes acts as sedation in an excess patient (loud voice, red face, robust body, thick tongue coating, excess pulse, etc). The bitter flavor clears heat, clears mucoid deposits (cholesterol) and can lower blood pressure. The bitter taste also lowers fever and drains dampness. The bitter taste helps with infections, inflammations, and conditions which has an excess of dampness. Patients who are slow, overweight, and lethargic can benefit from the bitter flavor. Patients who are deficient, weak, cold, thin, and dry should limit the bitter flavor in their diet. Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 314",
      "exp_hant": "苦味食物尚包括纈草、紫錐花及紫葳（風鈴木）。苦味食物性屬陰而偏涼，能收斂氣機並使氣下行。對於實證患者（聲音洪亮、面赤、體格壯實、舌苔厚膩、脈實等），苦味具有鎮靜之效。苦味能清熱、清除黏濁沉積物（膽固醇），並可降血壓。苦味亦能退熱、利濕。苦味有助於改善感染、發炎及濕邪偏盛之病症。反應遲鈍、體重過重及倦怠乏力之患者可受益於苦味食物；虛弱、畏寒、體形瘦弱及乾燥體質之患者則應限制苦味食物之攝取。Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 314"
