      "exp_en": "The pungent taste Scatters. The sweet taste Tonifies. The bitter taste Clears Heat. The salty taste Flows Downward. The sour taste Generates fluids. The action of the sweet taste is to tonify while the sour taste generates fluids. The sweet taste tonifies, balances, and moderates. It is used to tonify deficiency and stop pain. The sour taste generates fluids and yin. It is used to astringe, to control sweating and diarrhea. The bitter taste clears heat, sedates, and hardens. It is used to clear damp-heat and descend rebellious qi. The salty taste flows downward and softens hardness. It is used to treat constipation and swelling. The pungent taste scatters. It is used to expel pathogenic factors the \"taste\" of a food refers to the innate quality of the food and not its actual flavor. However, most times the flavor and the innate quality are identical such as when lemon is classified as sour. The Foundations of Chinese Medicine, Maciocia, 2015, page 40",
