      "exp_en": "As a general rule bitter foods reduce excess heat and dampness. The bitter taste is yin and cooling. It reduces the excess type of patient (loud voice, red face, robust body, thick tongue coating, excess pulse, etc). The bitter taste clears heat, dries body fluids, and drains dampness. Certain bitter foods (rhubarb) induce bowel movements as the bitter taste increases contractions of intestinal muscles. The bitter taste is associated with the Fire element (Heart) and clears Heart Heat, cleans the arteries (cholesterol), and can lower blood pressure (celery). The bitter taste also moves Liver stagnation and cools Liver Heat arising from overeating rich foods. Bitter foods drain dampness (candida, mucus, skin eruptions, tumors, obesity, edema). The bitter flavor clears Lung Phlegm/Heat. Patients who are slow, overweight, and lethargic can benefit from the bitter flavor. Weak, deficient, cold, thin, nervous, and dry patients should reduce the bitter flavor. Examples of bitter food are artichoke (cool-bitter-sweet, cools liver heat), spinach (cool, bitter-sweet, cools liver and blood), dandelion (bitter-cold, cools liver heat), celery (bitter-cool, cools stomach heat, loosens stuck qi), burdock (cool-pungent-bitter, clears heat, expels wind), chamomile (neutral-bitter-sweet, harmonizes digestion), valerian (cool-bitter-sweet, tonifies heart qi, relaxes), and eggplant (cool, bitter-sweet, cools heat, cools blood). Patients who are deficient, weak, cold, thin, and dry should limit the bitter flavor in their diet. Other foods that help to reduce excess are raw foods. Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 238-250; Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 90, 313,314,",
      "exp_hant": "一般而言，苦味食物能減輕實熱與濕邪。苦味性屬陰而偏涼，可減損實證患者之邪氣（聲音洪亮、面赤、體格壯實、舌苔厚膩、脈實等）。苦味能清熱、燥濕、利濕。某些苦味食物（大黃）可促進排便，因苦味能增強腸道肌肉收縮。苦味與五行中之火（心）相應，能清心熱、清潔血脈（膽固醇），並可降血壓（芹菜）。苦味亦能疏解肝鬱，並清瀉因過食肥甘厚味所生之肝熱。苦味食物能利濕（念珠菌感染、黏液、皮膚疹、腫瘤、肥胖、水腫）。苦味能清肺之痰熱。反應遲鈍、體重過重及倦怠乏力之患者可受益於苦味食物；虛弱、畏寒、體形瘦弱、神經緊張及乾燥體質之患者則應減少苦味食物之攝取。苦味食物之例包括朝鮮薊（涼、苦甘，清肝熱）、菠菜（涼、苦甘，清肝血之熱）、蒲公英（苦寒，清肝熱）、芹菜（苦涼，清胃熱，疏理鬱滯之氣）、牛蒡（涼、辛苦，清熱袪風）、洋甘菊（平、苦甘，調和消化）、纈草（涼、苦甘，補心氣、鎮靜安神）及茄子（涼、苦甘，清熱涼血）。虛弱、畏寒、體形瘦弱及乾燥體質之患者應限制飲食中苦味之攝取。其他有助於減輕實證之食物尚有生食。Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 238-250; Healing with Whole Foods, Paul Pitchford, 3rd Edition page 90, 313,314,"
