      "exp_en": "Through the ke cycle (Metal controls Wood) an excess of the pungent flavor can injure the Liver and Gall Bladder resulting in irritability, insomnia, hyperactivity. As such it should be restricted in this condition. The pungent flavor disperses the shen (Mind) creating restlessness. Through the sheng cycle (Metal is mother of Water), an excess of the pungent flavor can exaggerate sexual desires and compulsions. An excess of the pungent flavor can also affect the skin (Metal) with dryness, itching. The pungent flavor moves qi, loosens stagnation, opens the pores, and produces sweating. The pungent flavor helps the Lungs to disperse external pathogenic and acute wind-cold. Moderate pungent flavor can loosen emotional stagnation manifesting as a tight chest and shallow breathing. Because the pungent flavor moves upward it can help alleviate sadness, grief, and melancholy. Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 26",
      "exp_hant": "依相剋（相克）之理（金克木），過食辛味可損傷肝膽，導致急躁易怒、失眠、亢奮，故此類情況應限制辛味攝取。辛味能發散心神（神），使人躁動不安。依相生（相生）之理（金為水之母），過食辛味可能加劇性慾與衝動。過食辛味亦可能影響皮膚（金），出現乾燥、搔癢。辛味能行氣、疏散鬱結、開腠理、發汗。辛味能助肺袪散外邪及急性風寒。適量之辛味可疏解情志鬱結所致之胸悶及呼吸淺短。因辛味主升散，故有助於緩解悲傷、哀痛及憂鬱。Chinese Nutrition Therapy, Kastner, 2004, page 26"
