      "exp_en": "Statins are drugs that lower cholesterol. They are classified as HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors. Examples are atorvastatin (Lipitor), simvastatin (Zocor), and lovastatin (Mevacor). Grapefruit juice (32 oz. or more per day) can inhibit the enzyme (CYP3A4) in the small intestine which metabolizes the drug resulting in increased blood levels of the drug. This increased level increases the risk of statin-related side effects such as myalgia or myopathy. The amount of the CYP3A4 enzyme in the intestine varies from patient to patient. Therefore, grapefruit juice can affect patients differently even when the same drug is taken. The statin drugs that have this interaction are rosuvastatin (Crestor), pravastatin (Pravachol), and fluvastatin (Lescol). However, not all statin drugs have this interaction. The statins rosuvastatin (Crestor), pravastatin (Pravachol), and fluvastatin (Lescol) can be alternatives for patients drinking large amounts of grapefruit juice. There are other drug classes that interact with grapefruit juice (calcium channel blockers, some psychiatric drugs,some antihistamines, some impotence drugs, some immunosuppressant drugs, some antiarrhythmic drugs, etc). www.uspharmacist.com",
      "exp_hant": "史他汀類藥物（Statins）為降膽固醇藥物，屬於HMG-CoA還原酶抑制劑，例如atorvastatin（立普妥）、simvastatin（素果）及lovastatin（美乏脂）。葡萄柚汁（每日32盎司或以上）可抑制小腸中代謝此類藥物之酵素（CYP3A4），導致藥物血中濃度升高，進而增加與他汀類藥物相關之副作用風險，如肌肉痛或肌病變。小腸中CYP3A4酵素之含量因人而異，因此即使服用相同藥物，葡萄柚汁對不同患者之影響亦有差異。具此交互作用之他汀類藥物包括rosuvastatin（冠脂妥）、pravastatin（普凡）及fluvastatin（來適可）。然而並非所有他汀類藥物皆有此交互作用。對於大量飲用葡萄柚汁之患者，rosuvastatin（冠脂妥）、pravastatin（普凡）及fluvastatin（來適可）可作為替代選擇。尚有其他藥物類別亦會與葡萄柚汁產生交互作用（鈣離子通道阻斷劑、部分精神科藥物、部分抗組織胺藥物、部分治療陽痿之藥物、部分免疫抑制劑、部分抗心律不整藥物等）。www.uspharmacist.com"
